pan>Pairing its future fair coin with its flip gives a contribution of half this mass.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Synchronous noisy voter dynamics on connected locally finite simple graphs with a neighbor at every vertex, fair independent opinions, noise 0 &lt; ε &lt; 1 and positive lag.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="benjamini-helman-tov-zhukovskii-2023-noisy-voter-repetition-variance"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The repetition-count variance of the noisy voter model</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>I. Benjamini, H. Helman Tov and M. Zhukovskii, <em>Global information from local observations of the noisy voter model on a graph</em>, Annals of Probability 51(5), 1963–1992 (2023), Section 2.2, asks:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>May Var(ζ₁ + … + ζ_t) be sublinear? We do not have an answer. However, we prove that it is either linear in t or O(ln t).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The quotation is from arXiv:2207.01224v2, p. 6. The answer is no. For a connected locally finite simple graph with a neighbour at every vertex, noise $0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1$, observation vertex $u$ of degree $D$ and lag $d\ge1$, put $\zeta_i=\mathbf{1}{X_i(u)=X_{i+d}(u)}$ and $W_t=\sum_{i=1}^{t}\zeta_i$. The formal settlement is <code>D5.S3.StatisticalMechanics.NoisyVoter.RepetitionVarianceLinear.result : claim</code>. Preregistration: <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/16646">#16646</a>. The <a href="../Library/StatisticalMechanics/benjaminihelmantovzhukovskii2023noisyvoter.md">Library note</a> supplies the publication locator and quotations.</p>
