<p>These sentences occur in <code>main.tex</code>, lines 289 and 290, respectively, in the downloaded v1 source (709 lines; MD5 <code>b2275e7db7e3a63cc4c871c172f7943a</code>). The source specifies $\chi=|\Psi\rangle\langle\Psi|$ with $|\Psi\rangle=\tfrac12\sum_{i=0}^3|ii\ldots i\rangle$ on $N$ four-dimensional process factors (lines 286–289), and evaluates $F(\chi,\chi_{\mathrm{MA}})=4^{-N}$ (lines 292–296). Its MATEN definition is at lines 226–232. See also <a href="../Library/QuantumContext/sudmarshallwangrieffelwudarski2022dual.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/20689">#20689</a> fixes the settlement as a universal fidelity lower bound and attainment by cyclic wire permutations. The source's particular GHZ witness and its trace-preservation assertion require the qualification in Triage.</p>
<p>Write $a\in{0,1,2,3}^N$ for a Pauli string and $P_a=\bigotimes_k\sigma_{a_k}$, with $\sigma_0=I$, $\sigma_1=X$, $\sigma_2=Y$ and $\sigma_3=Z$, without Hilbert–Schmidt normalization. The formal definitions are:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>IsProcessCPTP</code> means $\chi\succeq0$ and $\sum_{a,b}\chi_{ab}P_bP_a=I$. This is the process representation of $\mathcal E_\chi(\rho)=\sum_{a,b}\chi_{ab}P_a\rho P_b$, matching the source's CP and TP conditions at lines 93–100.</li>
<li><code>marginal</code> is the single-site partial trace: $(\chi_k)<em>{ij}=\sum</em>{y:y_k=i}\chi_{y,y[k\leftarrow j]}$. <code>productMap</code> forms $\chi_{\mathrm{MA}}=\bigotimes_k\chi_k$, entrywise $(\chi_{\mathrm{MA}})<em>{ab}=\prod_k(\chi_k)</em>{a_kb_k}$.</li>
<li>The fidelity used is squared Uhlmann fidelity, $F(\rho,\sigma)=(\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{tr}\sqrt{\sqrt\rho,\sigma\sqrt\rho})^2$, exactly <code>sqFidelity</code>. This convention agrees with the source's projector calculation and distinguishes squared fidelity from root fidelity.</li>
<li>Put $U_N=(\mathtt{qubitPermutation}(\mathtt{finRotate},N))^{\mathsf T}$. Here the untransposed permutation matrix has entries $1$ when $y=x\circ\mathtt{finRotate},N$ and $0$ otherwise. <code>shiftCoeff</code> is $\psi_N(a)=2^{-N}\operatorname{tr}(P_aU_N)$, and <code>rankOneDensity</code> gives $\chi_N=\psi_N\psi_N^\dagger$, with entries $\psi_N(a)\overline{\psi_N(b)}$.</li>
</ul>
