<p>The settled question is the second sentence. In the module, a hyperdisk is a set of unit vectors in <code>EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin n)</code> represented by an orthonormal family <code>φ</code>, positive real coefficient moduli <code>r</code>, equality of the span of <code>φ</code> with the span of the set, and equality with the full unit-vector level set having those coefficient moduli. A regular subset <code>c</code> of <code>s</code> satisfies <code>IsHyperdisk s</code> and <code>(Submodule.span ℂ c : Set _) ∩ s = c</code>. The claim asks, for every natural <code>n</code> and every such <code>c</code> and <code>s</code>, for a natural <code>k</code> and a map <code>h : Fin k → Set (EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin n))</code> such that every <code>h i</code> is a hyperdisk contained in <code>c</code> and <code>c = ⋃ i, h i</code>.</p>
