ent can four qubits share? four qubits cannot be maximally entangled across every two-versus-two split. what is the largest possible average? higuchi and sudbery asked this extremal question in 2000. it concerns the limits of distributing entanglement across a four-qubit pure state. we prove the exact maximum average two-qubit marginal entropy, 1 + ½ log₂ 3 bits, and show that the higuchi–sudbery state attains it. an entropy majorant reduces the optimization to a coupled polynomial inequality. an exact sum-of-squares identity proves the bound for all normalized four-qubit pure states. the result concerns the average entropy of the three complementary two-qubit cuts of a pure four-qubit state. qubit-cuts source-bound-editorial ac15e5da03e5d89391294d71d6fd44606a24073a6fa94327fb8ce4d3b97fd20c 四个量子比特，究竟能共享多少纠缠？ 四个量子比特无法在每一种二对二划分下都达到最大纠缠。那么，平均值的极限在哪里？ higuchi 与 sudbery 在 2000 年提出这个极值问题，研究四量子比特纯态中纠缠分配的极限。 我们证明了两比特约化态平均熵的精确最大值：1 + ½ log₂ 3 比特，并证明 higuchi–sudbery 态达到这一极限。 用熵的上界函数把优化问题化为耦合的多项式不等式，再用精确的平方和恒等式完成证明，覆盖所有归一化四量子比特纯态。 结论针对四量子比特纯态的三个互补二对二划分，以及对应两比特约化态的平均熵。 qubit-cuts "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Quantum information</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Sharp bound proved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>Source</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2000</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>How much entanglement can four qubits share?</strong><span class="result-excerpt">We prove the exact maximum average two-qubit marginal entropy, 1 + ½ log₂ 3 bits, and show that the Higuchi–Sudbery state attains it.</span><span class="result-formal-title">Higuchi Sudbery Entropy Maximum</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Four qubits cannot be maximally entangled across every two-versus-two split. What is the largest possible average?</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>Higuchi and Sudbery asked this extremal question in 2000. It concerns the limits of distributing entanglement across a four-qubit pure state.</p><p><span>The idea</span>An entropy majorant reduces the optimization to a coupled polynomial inequality. An exact sum-of-squares identity proves the bound for all normalized four-qubit pure states.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>We prove the exact maximum average two-qubit marginal entropy, 1 + ½ log₂ 3 bits, and show that the Higuchi–Sudbery state attains it.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>The result concerns the average entropy of the three complementary two-qubit cuts of a pure four-qubit state.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="higuchi-sudbery-2000-four-qubit-average-entropy-maximum"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>higuchi sudbery 2000 four qubit average entropy maximum</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>For every normalized pure state $\psi\in(\mathbb C^2)^{\otimes4}$, the average two-qubit marginal von Neumann entropy in bits satisfies</p>
<p>$$\frac{S(\rho_{AB})+S(\rho_{AC})+S(\rho_{AD})}{3}\le 1+\frac12\log_2 3.$$</p>
<p>Equality is attained at the explicit Higuchi–Sudbery state</p>
<p>$$|M_4\rangle=\frac1{\sqrt6}\bigl[|0011\rangle+|1100\rangle+\omega(|1010\rangle+|0101\rangle)+\omega^2(|1001\rangle+|0110\rangle)\bigr],\qquad\omega=e^{2\pi i/3}.$$</p>
<p>Higuchi–Sudbery, Section 3: “Given that a four-qubit state cannot have maximal entropy of entanglement for every two-qubit subset, we now ask what is the greatest possible average for such entropies, i.e. we seek to maximise”. Their average over the six pairs equals the displayed average over the three complementary cuts.</p>
