<p>The <a href="../Library/QuantumBounds/kuaserafinigenoni2025daemonic.md">Library note</a> gives the source locators and Eq. (66). Write $r=2\chi/\kappa$, $\nu=2n_{\rm th}+1$ and $c=\sqrt{1-r^2}$, with $\kappa&gt;0$, $0\le\chi&lt;\kappa/2$ and $n_{\rm th}\ge0$. For every finite physical general-dyne measurement covariance $M$ and physical stationary conditional covariance $S$, the result proves</p>
<p>$$\sqrt{\det S}\ge v_* = \frac{(\nu-1)c+\sqrt{(\nu-1)^2c^2+4\nu}}{2}.$$</p>
<p>The pure aligned covariance</p>
<p>$$M_*=\operatorname{diag}\left(\frac{1-r}{1+r},\frac{1+r}{1-r}\right)$$</p>
<p>has a physical stationary solution attaining this value. No uniqueness of the minimizing measurement is asserted by the public theorem.</p>
