urations on a periodic chain.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="mukherjee-banerjee-sengupta-sen-2021-bubble-eigenstate-degeneracy"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>A closed formula for the bubble-eigenstate configuration count</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>B. Mukherjee, D. Banerjee, K. Sengupta and A. Sen, <em>Minimal model for Hilbert space fragmentation with local constraints</em> (Phys. Rev. B 104, 155117, 2021; arXiv:2106.14897v3), section “Construction of bubble eigenstates”, TeX <code>fragmentation_prb_v2.tex</code>, lines 729–731, immediately following Table I:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>While we have not been able to find a closed form expression for the degeneracy of the different bubble eigenstates for an arbitrary $L$, we can still place a lower bound on the degeneracy of such states when $L \gg 1$.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The counting prescription is explicit in the same source, lines 670–674:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The number of bubble eigenstates at an integer energy $E=n_1-n_2$ can be calculated for a given system size from the number of configurations that satisfy the hard core constraint of at least two consecutive $\downarrow$ spins separating any of the $n_1$ $X$ and $n_2$ $Y$ units on the periodic one-dimensional lattice.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Here $X$ and $Y$ are three-site units with energies $+1$ and $-1$, respectively (the source's construction, lines 634–647). Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/26367">#26367</a> fixes the combinatorial reading: sites are $\mathrm{Fin},L$, a centre set $B$ is admissible when every ordered pair of distinct centres has clockwise separation at least five, and a subset $x\subseteq B$ specifies the $X$ labels, with the other centres labelled $Y$. Its energy is $2|x|-|B|$. Translations are counted separately, and the empty placement contributes one configuration at energy zero. Let $D_B(L,E)$ denote this count, defined by <code>bubbleCount</code>.</p>
<p>For $1\le n\le\lfloor L/5\rfloor$, write</p>
<p>$$C(L,n)=\left(L\binom{L-4n-1}{n-1}\right)\mathbin{\mathrm{div}}n,$$</p>
<p>where $\mathrm{div}$ is natural-number division, and put</p>
<p>$$A(n,E)=\begin{cases}\displaystyle\binom{n}{(n+E)/2},&amp;n+E\text{ is even and }|E|\le n,\0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}$$</p>
<p>The module proves <code>claim</code>: for every natural $L\ge5$ and every integer $E$,</p>
<p>$$D_B(L,E)=[E=0]+\sum_{n=1}^{\lfloor L/5\rfloor}C(L,n)A(n,E).$$</p>
<p>Here $[E=0]$ is one when $E=0$ and zero otherwise; the equality is evaluated in the integers by casting the natural count and placement coefficients. The guarded index $(n+E)/2$ is a nonnegative integer. This settles the stated closed-form gap for labelled configurations; identifying these configurations with eigenstates of $H_3$ uses the source's construction and is not part of the Lean theorem.</p>
