sequences and primes that are inert in quadratic fields</em>, arXiv:2610.00765v1,
Section 7, question 2, asks:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For the recursions of this paper the exponent m=2 is forced. Is there a natural family of rational recursions for which c a_n+b_n is always a cube, other than those conjugate to z -&gt; z^3?</p>
