<p>The reduced-fraction convention is inherited from Problem 1.1: a_n,b_n are
coprime positive integers, starts are positive integers, c is positive rational,
and indices are n&gt;=2. “Natural” is undefined. The explicit minimal reading here
is a uniform autonomous rational family over Q of fixed degree, parameterized
by a nonnegative integer, with one formula and a single c independent of the
parameter, initial value and index. An unstated stricter author intent is not
resolved by this reading.</p>
<p>For every t in N, including zero, put</p>
<p>$$F_t(x)=\frac{x+t}{(x+t+1)^3-(x+t)},\qquad x_n=F_t^{\circ n}(x_0).$$</p>
<p>The proved endpoint is: for every positive rational x_0, the intrinsic reduced
numerator a_n and denominator b_n are positive and coprime for every n&gt;=0;
