act-history"><span>First preprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2026</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Unique integral circulant energy maximum at order $p^2q^3$</strong><span class="result-excerpt">For distinct odd primes p and q, one divisor set uniquely maximises integral circulant energy at order p squared q cubed, including q = 3.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Roldán, Graph Energy Maximisation for Integral Circulant Graphs of Order n = p^2q^3, arXiv:2604.09491v1, Section 1, Conjecture 1.3 (Universality):</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>A uniform proof for all distinct odd primes closes this exceptional family and Conjecture 1.3 as stated.</p><p><span>The idea</span>Fourier diagonalization gives eigenvalues as Ramanujan sums.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>For distinct odd primes p and q, one divisor set uniquely maximises integral circulant energy at order p squared q cubed, including q = 3.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="roldan-2026-integral-circulant-energy-p2q3"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Unique integral circulant energy maximum at order $p^2q^3$</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>D. G. Roldán, <em>Graph Energy Maximisation for Integral Circulant Graphs of Order n = p^2q^3</em>, arXiv:2604.09491v1, Section 1, Conjecture 1.3 (Universality):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For every pair of distinct odd primes (p, q), the set D* = {1, p^2, pq, q^2, p^2q^2, pq^3} is the unique maximiser of E(p^2q^3, D) over all nonempty D ⊆ div(p^2q^3) ∖ {p^2q^3}.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The graph has vertices $\mathbb Z_n$ and adjacency condition $\gcd(a-b,n)\in D$. Its energy is the sum of the absolute values of its adjacency eigenvalues, with multiplicity. Source quotations and locators are in <a href="../Library/GraphInvariants/roldan2026integralcirculant.md">the literature note</a>. Preregistration: <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/19144">#19144</a>.</p>
