ényi Bounds on Information
Combining”, ISIT 2020, arXiv:2004.14408v1, §IV-D, Conjecture IV.18, Eq. (88):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>There exists a value $1 &lt; \hat\alpha &lt; 1.3863$, such that
$h_\alpha(h_\alpha^{-1}(x) \ast h_\alpha^{-1}(y))$ is convex for
$0 &lt; \alpha &lt; \hat\alpha$ and concave for $\alpha \ge 2$.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The formal claim supplies the witness $\hat\alpha=5/4$ and quantifies over
every fixed $y\in[0,\log2]$, with convexity or concavity in $x$ on the whole
closed entropy interval. Put</p>
<p>$$
h_\alpha(p)=
\begin{cases}
-p\log p-(1-p)\log(1-p),&amp;\alpha=1,\
\log(p^\alpha+(1-p)^\alpha)/(1-\alpha),&amp;\alpha\ne1,
\end{cases}
\qquad p\star q=p+q-2pq.
$$</p>
<p>The inverse branch has probability domain $[0,1/2]$. Logarithms are natural,
all orders are real, and the Shannon value is Mathlib's <code>Real.binEntropy</code>.</p>
