 class="eyebrow">Integer sequences (OEIS)</p><h3>Mathar&#x27;s D-finite recurrence for OEIS A308815</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>OEIS A308815, FORMULA section, states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjecture: D-finite with recurrence: n*(2*n+1)*a(n) -32*(9*n-4)*(n-1)*a(n-1) +1024*(3*n^2-23*n+29)*a(n-2) +65536*(n-2)*(2*n-5)*a(n-3)=0. - <em>R. J. Mathar</em>, Jan 27 2020</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Its PARI definition is:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a(n) = 16^n*sum(i=0, n, (-2)^i*binomial(n, i)*C(2*n-i));</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Here $C_k$ is the ordinary Catalan number. Put</p>
<p>$$a_n=16^n\sum_{i=0}^n(-2)^i\binom ni C_{2n-i}.$$</p>
<p>For every natural $n\ge3$, the conjecture asserts</p>
<p>$$n(2n+1)a_n-32(9n-4)(n-1)a_{n-1}
+1024(3n^2-23n+29)a_{n-2}+65536(n-2)(2n-5)a_{n-3}=0.$$</p>
<p>The external tier-1 claim is preregistered in
https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/15713.
The signed PARI formula is the sequence convention; the NAME line's
unsigned $2^i$ conflicts with the displayed data.</p>
