 <em>On the Steiner k-diameter and Steiner
(k, k′)-radius of trees</em>, arXiv:2511.22492v1, p. 14, Conjecture 5.1, states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Let n, k, k′ be integers with n ≥ k ≥ 3 and k &gt; k′ ≥ 1 and let T be a tree with order n. Then Sd_k(T) ≤ k/(k − k′) Sr_{k,k′}(T) − k′(k′ − 1)/(k − k′).</p>
