<blockquote>
<p>Number of n X 2 0..1 arrays avoiding the patterns 0 1 0 or 1 0 1 in any row, column, diagonal or antidiagonal.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Its first FORMULA states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Empirical: a(n) = 2*a(n-1) + 2*a(n-2) - a(n-3). G.f.: -4*x*(-1-2*x+x^2) / ( (1+x)*(x^2-3*x+1) ).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Its OFFSET is <code>1,1</code>. The source has no DOI or arXiv identifier. The source
note is <code>Library/Automata/hardin2012a206981.md</code>; preregistration is
<a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/24139">#24139</a>.</p>
<p>For the actual source-array count $a(n)$, the proved assertion is</p>
<p>$$
\forall n\ge4,\quad a(n)=2a(n-1)+2a(n-2)-a(n-3),
$$</p>
<p>and, with $G(X)=\sum_{n\ge1}a(n)X^n$ as an integer formal power series,</p>
<p>$$
G(X)(1-2X-2X^2+X^3)=4X+8X^2-4X^3.
$$</p>
<p>The denominator equals $(1+X)(X^2-3X+1)$ and has constant coefficient
one. Thus clearing the denominator preserves the source's rational
formal-series assertion. It imposes no analytic convergence assumption.</p>
