ximal elements minus the number of minimal elements is 0-mesic under rowmotion on interval-closed sets. l… result max-minus-min homomesy for rectangle interval-closed rowmotion question resolved discrete structures max-minus-min homomesy for rectangle interval-closed rowmotion elder, lafrenière, mcnicholas, striker and welch, toggling, rowmotion, and homomesy on interval-closed sets, arxiv:2307.08520v2, conjecture 4.9, states that for every product of two finite chains the number of maximal elements minus the number of minimal elements is 0-mesic under rowmotion on interval-closed sets. the result gives the exact all-rectangle resolution requested by the original conjecture. the max-minus-min statistic is zero-sum on every literal interval-closed rectangle rowmotion orbit. these facts yield an integer coboundary for maxminusmin. the follow-up paper&#x27;s separate signed-cardinality result, its explicit orbit descriptions for [2] × [n], and any broader poset or higher-product statement are outside this result. released-dossier ea77b76afccafead2a639b02be0ff9cb5f06aa06aa6e2af96049c8b02f0f9c8e "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Discrete structures</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Question resolved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>First preprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2023</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Max-minus-min homomesy for rectangle interval-closed rowmotion</strong><span class="result-excerpt">The max-minus-min statistic is zero-sum on every literal interval-closed rectangle rowmotion orbit.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Elder, Lafrenière, McNicholas, Striker and Welch, Toggling, rowmotion, and homomesy on interval-closed sets, arXiv:2307.08520v2, Conjecture 4.9, states that for every product of two finite chains the number of maximal elements minus the number of minimal elements is 0-mesic under rowmotion on interval-closed sets.</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The result gives the exact all-rectangle resolution requested by the original conjecture.</p><p><span>The idea</span>These facts yield an integer coboundary for maxMinusMin.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>The max-minus-min statistic is zero-sum on every literal interval-closed rectangle rowmotion orbit.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>The follow-up paper&#x27;s separate signed-cardinality result, its explicit orbit descriptions for [2] × [n], and any broader poset or higher-product statement are outside this result.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="rectangle-rowmotion-max-minus-min-homomesy"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Max-minus-min homomesy for rectangle interval-closed rowmotion</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Elder, Lafrenière, McNicholas, Striker and Welch, <em>Toggling, rowmotion, and
