</blockquote>
<p>These quotations are from the downloaded v3 source, md5 <code>18bc93c300903edbf34bf142ad00519d</code>; the source's definition of a simple eigenvalue as one of algebraic multiplicity one is at lines 123–125. See also <a href="../Library/QuantumContext/vomende2024diagonalizable.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/21152">#21152</a> fixes the positive-Gibbs-vector reading: for every $n\in\mathbb N$ and every $d:\mathrm{Fin},n\to\mathbb R$ with $d_i&gt;0$ for all $i$, there exists a real $n\times n$ matrix $P$ with nonnegative entries, every column summing to one, $Pd=d$, and no repeated roots in its complex characteristic polynomial. This existence statement is proved. Normalization of $d$ is not required; $n=0$ is included. The source's density consequence is separate from the formal claim.</p>
