<p>The resolved statement is the literal ordinary formal-power-series identity for every integer <code>n &gt;= 3</code>. For each <code>n</code>, the graph has distinct labelled vertices <code>alpha</code>, <code>beta</code>, <code>a_0,...,a_(n-1)</code>, and <code>b_0,...,b_(n-1)</code>, the alternating rim cycle, alpha adjacent to every <code>a_i</code>, beta adjacent to every <code>b_i</code>, and no other edges. The coefficient counts actual subsets <code>S</code> whose closed neighbourhood is the full graph, every proper subset of <code>S</code> fails to dominate, and the induced graph on <code>S</code> is connected. Minimality ranges over all proper subsets independently of their connectivity; no quotient by rotations, reflections, or other automorphisms is taken. Coefficients below order three are zero.</p>
