disjunction. The log-convex clause reads:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If $f_k^2\le f_{k-1}f_{k+1}$ for all $k\in\mathbb N$, the sequence is called log-convex (this inequality implies that a nontrivial sequence is strictly positive).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Here $\mathbb N={1,2,\ldots}$. The literal inequalities permit the
exception supported on ${0}$; no extra strict-positivity assumption is
imposed. For $\mu,\alpha,\beta\ge0$, set</p>
<p>$$
\delta_m=\sum_{k=0}^{m}h_kh_{m-k}
\left[a_k(\mu+\alpha)a_{m-k}(\mu+\beta)
-a_k(\mu)a_{m-k}(\mu+\alpha+\beta)\right].
$$</p>
<p>The assertion is $\delta_m\ge0$ for log-concave $h$ and $\delta_m\le0$
