<p>Here $(a)_k$ is the rising factorial. Definition 1.1, page 2:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Let ${f_k}<em>{k=0}^{\infty}$ be a non-negative nontrivial real sequence. We call ${f_k}</em>{k=0}^{\infty}$ log-concave (or Pólya frequency two – $PF_2$, or doubly positive) if $f_k^2\ge f_{k-1}f_{k+1}$ for each $k\in\mathbb N$, and ${f_k}<em>{k=0}^{\infty}$ is supported on an interval of integers (i.e., $f_N=0$ implies either $f</em>{N+i}=0$ for all $i\in\mathbb N_0$ or $f_{N-i}=0$ for $i=0,\ldots,N$).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The Lean predicate retains nonnegativity, nontriviality, adjacent inequalities
