p><span>Our contribution</span>The generalized doubly nonnegative cone inclusion for orthant and Lorentz products.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="nishijima-nakata-2024-gdnn-inclusion"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Generalized doubly nonnegative cone inclusion</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>The cited article, arXiv:2204.12119v4, Section 5.1, Conjecture 5.1, asks for
the inclusion of the NN-type generalized doubly nonnegative cone in the
BD-type cone for products of a nonnegative orthant and second-order cones.
The statement reads verbatim: “If K is a direct product of a nonnegative
orthant and second-order cones, DNN^NN(K) ⊆ DNN^BD(K) holds.” The article
notes that the case of a single second-order cone follows from its
Proposition 4.12 and that the general inclusion relationship is unknown.</p>
<h3>Formal reading</h3>
<p>Let $p,r\ge0$ and $k_j\ge1$ for $1\le j\le r$, and put</p>
<p>$$K=\mathbb R_+^p\times\prod_{j=1}^r
{(t,z)\in\mathbb R\times\mathbb R^{k_j}:|z|_2\le t}.$$</p>
<p>Let $q$ square each orthant coordinate and send each Lorentz block $(t,z)$
to $(t^2+|z|<em>2^2,2tz)$. Write $\Sigma</em>{n,4}$ for the convex hull of
squares of homogeneous quadratic polynomials. With the standard coordinate
pairing and $n=p+\sum_j(k_j+1)$, define</p>
<p>$$\mathcal K_{\mathrm{NN},0}(K)
={A\in\mathbb S^n:q(x)^\mathsf{T}Aq(x)\in\Sigma_{n,4}}.$$</p>
<p>Every $X\in\mathbb S^n$ satisfying
$\operatorname{tr}(XA)\ge0$ for every $A\in\mathcal K_{\mathrm{NN},0}(K)$
is positive semidefinite and satisfies $Xs\in K$ for every extreme ray
generator $s$ of $K^*$. Thus $\mathrm{DNN}^{\mathrm{NN}}(K)\subseteq
\mathrm{DNN}^{\mathrm{BD}}(K)$.</p>
