<p>Line 424 specifies the asymptotic family: the exceptional clockwise rate is $ak$, the other rates are $k$, and $a=A/N$ as $N\to\infty$. Appendix line 792 states that the extremal-topology assertion was numerically conjectured. Thus the analytic endpoint on the proposed topology is source input; its universal validity for arbitrary positive rate vectors needs proof.</p>
<p><strong>Source sign discrepancy.</strong> The detailed display at line 432 and Figure 6 concern $\mathcal S-\mathcal K$, but the summary at line 133 prints $\mathcal K-\mathcal S\in[-0.15,0.465]$. The two signs conflict. This problem follows the detailed display and Figure 6; it does not identify the reversed-sign summary with that claim.</p>
<p>The exact reading is preregistered in <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/25765">#25765</a> and its <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/25765#issuecomment-6585311119">unchanged endpoint comment</a>. For every natural $N\ge2$ and every $k:\mathrm{Fin},N\to\mathbb R$ with $k_i&gt;0$ for all $i$, put</p>
<p>$$
