$$</p>
<p>The proved claim is the conjunction of $\mathcal S(k)-\mathcal K(k)\le B$ for every such $N,k$ and $\operatorname{IsLUB}(V,B)$. Both ratios use the same vector, repeated rates retain their multiplicities, the coordinates are arbitrary positive reals, and $N$ is unbounded. The claim includes $N=2$ and assumes no extremal topology. Sharpness concerns this full actual-value set, not a finite prefix or a relaxation to independently chosen moments.</p>
<p>The source's $\mathcal S$ and $\mathcal K$ are third-to-first and fourth-to-second <strong>scaled current-cumulant ratios</strong> (<code>main.tex</code> lines 53–54), not standardized central moments. The inverse-rate formulas follow by substitution in the source's winding-number and waiting-time cumulant expressions (Appendix lines 772–775 and 787–790). Their original Lean definitions are <code>UnicyclicSkewnessMinimum.skewness</code> and <code>UnicyclicKurtosisLowerBound.kurtosis</code>. See <a href="../Library/StatisticalMechanics/ptaszynski2022skewness.md">the source note</a>.</p>
