<p>Let p(x) be an even polynomial over GF(2). Then p(x) is self-conjugate if and only if p(x)=x^{2^{k_1}}+x^{2^{k_2}}+...+x^{2^{k_m}}, where m is odd if x^0 is a term and m is even otherwise.</p>
