<blockquote>
<p>For fixed k ≥ 3 and n &lt; 0, the upper bound is ζ_{n,k} ≤ ⌊|n|/k⌋.
The bound is attained whenever r_{n,k} = 1 (equivalently n = −sk,
where s ≥ 1), i.e. it is a tight bound.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The recurrence (1.2)–(1.3) and initial values are</p>
<p>$$
\mathcal F_{n,k}(x)=\sum_{j=1}^{k}x^{k-j}\mathcal F_{n-j,k}(x),\qquad
\mathcal F_{1,k}=1,\qquad
\mathcal F_{n,k}=0\quad (-(k-2)\le n\le0).
$$</p>
<p>The source statistic is the maximum of $|x|^k$ over nonzero complex roots;
it is zero when there are none, including vanishing polynomials. The Lean
encoding uses <code>a k m</code> for $\mathcal F_{1-m,k}$, <code>F k n := a k (1-n).toNat</code>,
and the real supremum of the nonzero-root amplitude image. Its empty and
unbounded totalizations give zero. The guards in <code>claim</code> are $k\ge3$ and
