<blockquote>
<p>The cut-off values α_n converge to 1/√5 from above.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The source defines the Katz matrix by $K_{P_n}(\alpha)=(I-\alpha A_n)^{-1}-I$ and the cut-off values as roots of
$p_{n,1}(\alpha)=\min_i K_{i,i+1}-\max_i K_{i,i+2}$, with each extremum restricted to existing vertex pairs.
Theorem 19 locates a root between $1/\sqrt5$ and $1/2$ for every $n\ge6$.
The preregistration is <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/20122">#20122</a>.</p>
