$a(n)=\binom{2n+1}{n}/(2n+1)\cdot\binom{3n-1}{n}$ for $n\geq0$ and states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjectures: given A033042 is the sums of distinct powers of 5, then
(1) a(5*A033042(n)) == 4 (mod 5) for n &gt; 0,
(2) a(5*A033042(n) + 1) == 2 (mod 5) for n &gt; 0,
(3) a(n) == 0 (mod 5) for n &gt; 0 except when n or n-1 equals 5*A033042(k) for some k &gt;= 0.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The problem is preregistered in <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/18656">#18656</a>.
The three settlements are Proved. For every positive sum $m$ of distinct powers of five,
$a(5m)\equiv4\pmod5$ and $a(5m+1)\equiv2\pmod5$. For every positive $n$ outside
$n=5m$ or $n-1=5m$ with $m$ a sum of distinct powers of five (including zero), $a(n)\equiv0\pmod5$.
The companion statements are preregistered in <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/18657">#18657</a>
and <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/18658">#18658</a>.</p>
