ass="result-statement prose"><p>F. La Piana, <em>Graph Quantum Magic Squares and Free Spectrahedra</em>, arXiv:2512.08797v3, Question 1.3 asks:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Given a graph Γ, does the matrix convex hull of its quantum permutation matrices P^(Γ) generate all graph quantum magic squares? That is, mconv(P^(Γ)) = M^(Γ)?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Section 4.1 names $C_5$ and the Petersen graph among the candidates for strict containment. The settlement is <strong>Proved</strong> for $C_5$, under the complete conventions preregistered in <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/19303">#19303</a>:</p>
<p>$\operatorname{mconv}(\mathcal P^{(C_5)})_s\subseteq\mathcal M^{(C_5)}_s$ at every internal size, and some $X\in\mathcal M^{(C_5)}_2$ lies outside that hull.</p>
<h3>Statement echo</h3>
<p>| Source clause | Lean counterpart | Scope |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Definition 2.1: positive semidefinite blocks and identity row/column sums | <code>IsQMS</code> | All external and internal natural-number sizes; complex matrices |
| Definition 3.1: adjacency-block commutation | <code>IsGraphQMS</code> | Every pair of vertices, both adjacency-filtered sums |
| Definition 3.2: graph magic squares | <code>M</code> | Set of blocks satisfying <code>IsGraphQMS</code> |
