| Definition 2.3: normalized finite blockwise compressions | <code>IsMatrixConvex</code> | All finite families, varying input sizes and all output sizes |
| Smallest containing matrix convex family | <code>mconv</code> | Intersection of every containing matrix convex family |
| Section 4.1, named candidate $C_5$ | <code>claim</code>, <code>result</code> | All-level containment and existential separation |</p>
<p>The source uses positive sizes and a Hermitian ambient family. The preregistered encoding uses arbitrary complex block families and includes level zero; <code>IsQMS</code> itself enforces Hermitian blocks through positivity. The size-zero matrices are unique. <code>Fin</code> indices, the matrix identity <code>1</code>, and <code>SimpleGraph.cycleGraph 5</code> implement the source's indices, identity and graph. The strictness statement is existential in the internal size, with a size-two witness; it does not assert strictness at every size.</p>
