arXiv:2507.11596v4, p. 19, Section 6, Conjecture 6.4, states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For k ≥ 2 and n = −sk, where s ∈ [2, k + 1] (the pattern fails for s ≥ k + 2),
𝓕_{−sk,k}(x) = −x(x^k + 1)^{s−2}(x^k + s). (6.4)
Hence 𝓕_{−sk,k}(x) has roots x^k = −s.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The recurrence (1.2)–(1.3) is</p>
<p>$$
\mathcal F_{n,k}(x)=\sum_{j=1}^k x^{k-j}\mathcal F_{n-j,k}(x),\qquad
\mathcal F_{1,k}=1,\qquad \mathcal F_{n,k}=0\quad (-(k-2)\le n\le0).
$$</p>
<p>The frozen definitions <code>a</code> and <code>F</code> in
<code>D5/S3/Zeros/NegativeIndexTribonacciAttainmentRefutation.lean</code> encode
$a_k(m)=\mathcal F_{1-m,k}$ and <code>F k n = a k (1-n).toNat</code>.
The claim is an identity in $\mathbb Z[X]$ with natural $k,s$,
$k\ge2$ and $2\le s\le k+1$; the index is the integer $-sk$.</p>
