<p>The quoted TeX label denotes Eq. (1): for $n\ge1$, the real phases of a $2^{2n}\times2^{2n}$ diagonal unitary satisfy $\theta_{j,j'}=\theta_{2^n-1-j,,2^n-1-j'}$ for every $0\le j,j'&lt;2^n$ (<code>main_arXiv2.tex</code>, lines 207–227). Equivalently, writing $m=2n$ and $x\in{0,1}^m$, $\theta(\bar x)=\theta(x)$, where $\bar x$ complements every bit. The source specifies ancilla-free ${\mathrm{CNOT},R_z}$ circuits at lines 194 and 1225 and realization up to a global phase at lines 429–445.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/24527">#24527</a> fixes the reading: for every $n\ge1$ there is such a phase function $\theta$ for which every finite circuit realizing $\operatorname{diag}(e^{\mathrm i\theta(x)})$ up to a global phase has at least $2^{2n-1}+2n-2$ CNOT gates. This lower-bound statement is proved. The source's matching upper bound from Algorithm 1 is separate from <code>claim</code>.</p>
