<blockquote>
<p>The maximum number of scattered palindromic subwords in a word of length $n$ is $3(2^{\lceil n/2\rceil-1})-2$ if $n$ is odd, $2^{n/2+1}-2$ if $n$ is even, and this bound is achieved only when $q=\lceil n/2\rceil$ if $n$ is odd, $\frac n2$ and $\frac n2+1$ if $n$ is even.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>$SP(w)$ counts distinct nonempty palindromic scattered subwords, rather than their embeddings. A scattered subword is a subsequence; $q$ counts the distinct letters in $w$. Write $M(n)$ for the displayed maximum.</p>
