<ul>
<li><strong>The map entropy.</strong> S_map(Φ) is the von Neumann entropy of the normalized Choi state. By Proposition 1, S_map(Φ) = S(Φ̃(I/N)) and S_map(Φ̃) = S(Φ(I/N)).</li>
<li><strong>The conjecture.</strong> Conjecture 1 (page 5): &quot;For qutrit channels with qutrit environment the lower boundary of the allowed set A_3 is given by the parametric curve p(a) = (−a log a − (1 − a) log(1 − a), log 3/3 − (a + 1/3) log(a + 1/3) − (a − 1/3) log(a − 1/3)) (20) with a ∈ (0, 1/3), together with reflection through line S = S̃&quot;.</li>
</ul>
<p>The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/QuantumChannels/czartowski2019tradeoff.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/17038">#17038</a> fixes the reading:</p>
<ul>
<li>The last term of Eq. (20) is read as −(1/3 − a) log(1/3 − a): the printed term is not real for a &lt; 1/3, and the source's attaining channels give the corrected one.</li>
<li>Put h(a) = H(1 − a, a) and g(a) = H(1/3 + a, 1/3, 1/3 − a). The lower boundary means two things for a ∈ [0, 1/3]:
<ul>
<li>for every isometry V : ℂ³ → ℂ³ ⊗ ℂ³, S_map(Φ) ≤ h(a) implies S_map(Φ̃) ≥ g(a), and the same with Φ and Φ̃ exchanged;</li>
<li>the curve and its reflection are attained.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>The conjecture is proved in this reading.</p>
