h the operators rho1, ..., rhon are given by the closed formula conjectured by m.   released-dossier 2fd30758cb0644c68edb91b75351ffe78219d549d411ee3fa1800d8d1180a333 "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Geometry &amp; algebra</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Question resolved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>First preprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2015</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>The closed form of the higher-antibracket coefficients</strong><span class="result-excerpt">For every n &gt;= 2, the coefficients c1^n, ..., cn^n that express the higher Koszul bracket Phi^(n+1) through the operators rho1, ..., rhon are given by the closed formula conjectured by M.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Ricciardi, Universal Lie Formulas for Higher Antibrackets, SIGMA 12 (2016), 053, arXiv:1509.09032v3, Conjecture 2.4:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>Higher Koszul brackets (higher antibrackets) measure the failure of an operator to be a derivation and govern the BV formalism.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>For every n &gt;= 2, the coefficients c1^n, ..., cn^n that express the higher Koszul bracket Phi^(n+1) through the operators rho1, ..., rhon are given by the closed formula conjectured by M.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="manetti-ricciardi-2015-higher-antibracket-coefficients"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The closed form of the higher-antibracket coefficients</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>M. Manetti and G. Ricciardi, <em>Universal Lie Formulas for