ccessive applications.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="yang-chen-li-fei-wang-2018-coherence-breaking-amendment"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Every incoherent channel with coherence-breaking index at least two is amended by one unitary</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>L.-M. Yang, B. Chen, T. Li, S.-M. Fei and Z.-X. Wang, <em>Amending Coherence-Breaking Channels via Unitary Operations</em> (Int. J. Theor. Phys. 57, 3776 (2018); arXiv:1810.09642), study incoherent channels.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Definitions.</strong> An incoherent channel is coherence-breaking if it maps every state to an incoherent state. The coherence-breaking index n(Φ) is the least k with Φ^k coherence-breaking.</li>
<li><strong>Results.</strong> For qubit channels with n(Φ) = 1 and 2 they find unitaries Λα that make Λα ◦ Φ and Φ ◦ Λα ◦ Φ not coherence-breaking.</li>
<li><strong>The conjecture.</strong> Section 5 states: &quot;for a d-dimensional quantum channel Φ with n(Φ) ≥ 2, one may conjecture that the channel Φ can also be amended by Φ ◦ Λα ◦ Φ ◦ · · · ◦ Φ ◦ Λα ◦ Φ [n Φ] with proper unitary operations Λα.&quot;</li>
<li><strong>The later preprint.</strong> MiS Preprint 7/2019 asserts the qudit statement in its conclusions without a proof.</li>
</ul>
<p>The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/QuantumChannels/yang2018coherencebreaking.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/18385">#18385</a> fixes the reading: for every incoherent trace-preserving Kraus channel with n(Φ) = n ≥ 2, some unitary U makes Φ ◦ (Λ_U ◦ Φ)^{n−1} not coherence-breaking, with the same U in every slot. The conjecture is proved.</p>
