Transactions on Information Theory 63(2), 1299–1310, Section V, Theorem 3,
Equation (8), ask:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It seems quite likely that in Eq. (8) the first inequality should be strict and the second one should be an equality. However, this is still an unsettled issue.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The equality in the second inequality is
$D(\Phi,\operatorname{Conv}(U_d))=D(\Phi,\Lambda_d)$ for every Schur channel
$\Phi$, where $\Lambda_d=S_d\cap\operatorname{Conv}(U_d)$.
The distance is the unhalved diamond distance. The
<a href="../Library/QuantumChannels/yuduanxu2017unitarydistance.md">literature note</a>
contains the definitions and source quotations. Preregistration
<a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/16745">#16745</a>
specifies the full quantified statement.</p>
