<summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="camilo-landi-eliens-2019-bosonic-gaussian-renyi-strong-subadditivity"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Strong subadditivity of bosonic Gaussian Rényi entropy for $0&lt;\alpha\le2$, $\alpha\ne1$</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>G. Camilo, G. T. Landi and S. Eliëns, <em>On the Strong Subadditivity of the Rényi entropies for bosonic and fermionic Gaussian states</em>, arXiv:1810.07070v2 (Phys. Rev. B 99, 045155, 2019), Section IV.A, <code>RenyiGaussian_v2.tex</code>, line 463:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It provides clear evidence that SSA is violated for all $\alpha&gt;2$, while no violation is found for $0\le\alpha\le2$. We conjecture that this result holds true in general.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Section V, line 532, requests:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>An obvious continuation of this work is to prove the conjectured domains of validity of the SSA for the R'enyi-$\alpha$ entropies.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>For $n$ modes, put $\Omega=\bigoplus_{j=1}^n\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;1\-1&amp;0\end{pmatrix}$. The covariance formulation takes a real symmetric $2n\times2n$ matrix $V$ with $V+i\Omega\succeq0$. For a mode set $X$, retain both quadratures to obtain $V_X$ and $\Omega_X$. The module defines</p>
<p>$$s_\alpha(\nu)=\frac{\log\left[((\nu+1)/2)^\alpha-((\nu-1)/2)^\alpha\right]}{\alpha-1},\qquad
S_\alpha(V_X)=\frac12\sum_{\lambda\in\operatorname{spec}(V_X^{1/2}(i\Omega_X)V_X^{1/2})}s_\alpha(|\lambda|),$$</p>
<p>with eigenvalues counted with multiplicity. This is the covariance entropy formula of Eq. <code>renyi_bosonic_1</code> (TeX lines 216–220), using both signs of the symplectic spectrum. The empty sum is zero.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/26322">#26322</a> fixes the statement: for every $n$, every such physical $V$, every pairwise disjoint mode sets $A,B,C$, and every $0&lt;\alpha\le2$ with $\alpha\ne1$,</p>
<p>$$S_\alpha(V_{A\cup B})+S_\alpha(V_{B\cup C})\ge S_\alpha(V_{A\cup B\cup C})+S_\alpha(V_B).$$</p>
