><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Jain: multiplicity two for absolute-cosine Hadamard powers</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Tanvi Jain, <em>Hadamard powers of some positive matrices</em>, Linear Algebra
and its Applications 528 (2017), 147–158, states in the final
unnumbered paragraph of section 3, after the proof of Theorem 3.3:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We conjecture that the multiplicity of every nonzero eigenvalue of |C|∘r∘ (except the top eigenvalue) equals two.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>For every natural m at least one, put n=2m+1 and
C_ab=cos((a-b)pi/n), with a,b from zero through n-1. The conjecture
concerns the matrix A(r) whose entries are |C_ab|^r for every real
r at least zero. Every nonzero characteristic-polynomial root other
than the top Fourier value must have algebraic multiplicity exactly
two. The formal definition <code>Defs.claim</code> retains all these quantifiers
and both exceptions.</p>
<p>The sentence is attributed to the publisher's indexed full text. The
journal PDF was inaccessible, so its page number is unverified.
The first version of arXiv:1803.06803 omits this sentence; the journal
article is the source of the conjecture.</p>
