ographic position recurrence after removing the leading bit. define w by heinz&#x27;s even and odd recurrence and rev by stephan&#x27;s even and odd recurrence, both through nat.binaryrec.  released-dossier fb2adb218e397d1e3b62a71d0c66b97d93b5b04d53d5ca43a5216dc574d62c7d "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Number theory</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Recurrence proved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>Posed in</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2017</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Yanev&#x27;s position identity for binary reversal</strong><span class="result-excerpt">Binary reversal is determined by the lexicographic position recurrence after removing the leading bit.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>0,1,1,3,1,5,3,7,1,9,5,13,3,11,7,15,1,17,9,25,5,21,13,29,3,19,11,27,7,</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The conjecture connects two independent views of a binary word: reversal of its digits and its lexicographic rank when the least significant digit is read first.</p><p><span>The idea</span>Define w by Heinz&#x27;s even and odd recurrence and rev by Stephan&#x27;s even and odd recurrence, both through Nat.binaryRec.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Binary reversal is determined by the lexicographic position recurrence after removing the leading bit.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="oeis-a030101-yanev-binary-reversal-position-identity"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Integer sequences (OEIS)</p><h3>Yanev&#x27;s position identity for binary reversal</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>OEIS A030101, OFFSET (<code>%O</code>, verbatim):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>0,4</p>
</blockquote>
<p>OEIS A030101, initial sequence line (<code>%S</code>, verbatim):</p>
<blockquote>
