j + V{piV/2 - j}, and V{-k} = Vk turns that into Vn + V{n + piV/2} = 0 for all n, which refers to no entry point.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Vertical slices admit criteria in terms of two consecutive traces, integer companion powers under a unit discriminant, and half the companion period when four is nonzero.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="fiebig-mbirika-spilker-vertical-slice"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">arXiv</p><h3>Necessary and sufficient conditions for the vertical slice result</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Write <code>V_n = V_n(p, q)</code> for the companion Lucas sequence and <code>pi_V(m)</code> for its least period
