estion</span>Morelli, Enhanced Schmidt number criteria based on correlation trace norms, arXiv:2402.09972v2, Phys.</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>For r = 1, (52) is the separability bound, and for larger r it detects states of Schmidt number greater than r with n &lt; d² outcomes per side.</p><p><span>The idea</span>1. Pure states as a Gram product. For a unit vector ψ with coefficient matrix Ψ = U D Vᴴ (singular value decomposition, D = diag(λ)), put S = D^{1/2}.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Equiangular measurements obey the Schmidt-number correlation trace-norm bound of Tavakoli and Morelli&#x27;s Conjecture 2.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="tavakoli-morelli-2024-conjecture-2-incomplete-eam-schmidt-bound"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Conjecture 2 of Tavakoli–Morelli: the Schmidt-number bound for equiangular measurements</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>A. Tavakoli and S. Morelli, <em>Enhanced Schmidt number criteria based on correlation trace norms</em>, arXiv:2402.09972v2, Phys. Rev. A 110, 062417 (2024), bound the trace norm of the table of joint outcome probabilities of local measurements for states of Schmidt number at most r.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Equiangular measurement (EAM).</strong> n &gt; d unit vectors ψ_a in C^d with Σ_a |ψ_a⟩⟨ψ_a| = (n/d)𝟙 (Eq. (49)) and |⟨ψ_a|ψ_a′⟩|² = (n − d)/(d(n − 1)) for a ≠ a′ (Eq. (50)); its effects are E_a = (d/n)|ψ_a⟩⟨ψ_a|.</li>
<li><strong>The table.</strong> For Alice's EAM {E^A_a} and Bob's {E^B_b}, (P_n)_ab = tr[ρ (E^A_a ⊗ E^B_b)].</li>
<li><strong>Conjecture 2</strong> (§V A, p. 7): &quot;For any state of Schmidt number r it holds that ‖P_n‖_tr ≤ [d(d − 1) + r(n − d)]/[n(n − 1)]. (52)&quot; The introduction leaves deciding the conjectures as an open problem.</li>
</ul>
<p>The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/QuantumBounds/tavakolimorelli2024schmidttracenorm.md">the literature note</a>. Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/17745">#17745</a> fixes the reading:</p>
<ul>
<li>for all d ≥ 1, 1 ≤ r ≤ d, n &gt; d, any two n-element EAMs on C^d chosen independently, and every state of Schmidt number at most r, the bound (52) holds;</li>
<li>a state of Schmidt number at most r is a finite convex combination of pure states whose coefficient matrices have rank at most r.</li>
</ul>
<p>This conjecture is proved.</p>
