<p>The section assumes a finite nonempty subtraction set of positive integers with gcd one. A player selects uniformly among legal subtractions, and loses when none is available. Writing $A_n={s\in S:0&lt;s\le n}$, the next player's winning probability is $a_n=0$ if $A_n$ is empty and otherwise $a_n=1-|A_n|^{-1}\sum_{s\in A_n}a_{n-s}$.</p>
