em>,
arXiv:2411.08139v2, §5.2:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We believe that (23, 13) is not in SPP_{R+}(7).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>For a domain X, the spectrum is</p>
<p>$$
\operatorname{SPP}_X(n)
= {(|A+A|,|AA|): A\subseteq X,\ |A|=n}.
$$</p>
<p>Here R+ denotes the strictly positive reals, and A+A and AA denote the
pointwise sumset and product set. The exact assertion is that every finite
set A of positive reals with seven elements satisfies</p>
<p>$$
\neg\bigl(|A+A|=23\ \land\ |AA|=13\bigr).
$$</p>
<p>The Lean <code>claim</code> retains these quantifiers and hypotheses. Its theorem
<code>result : claim</code> follows from the stronger statement</p>
<p>$$
