ng that a non-trivial lower bound of min{S(ρ¹A), S(ρ²A)} might hold for qubits, fails in general for qudits … Rigorous proofs of these observations for qubits … are still lacking&quot; (§3.3).</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The SVD entropy measures entanglement of a transition between two states.</p><p><span>The idea</span>5. Entropy. The entropy of a 2 × 2 density matrix is an increasing function of its determinant p(1 − p), so S(Q) ≥ min{S(ρψ), S(ρφ)}.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>For two unit two-qubit states with nonzero reduced transition, SVD entanglement entropy is at least the smaller input entanglement entropy.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="parzygnat-takayanagi-taki-wei-2023-two-qubit-svd-entropy-lower-bound"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>For two qubits the SVD entanglement entropy is at least the smaller of the two entanglement entropies</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>A. J. Parzygnat, T. Takayanagi, Y. Taki and Z. Wei, <em>SVD entanglement entropy</em>, JHEP 12 (2023) 123, arXiv:2307.06531v2, define an entropy for a pair of pure states.</p>
