r contribution</span>On the interval from zero to two thirds, the noisy qutrit Werner-Holevo channel is a GKSL exponential exactly at zero noise.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="roofeh-karimipour-2024-werner-holevo-lindblad-embedding"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The noisy qutrit Werner–Holevo channel is a GKSL exponential only at zero noise on $[0,2/3]$</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Shayan Roofeh and Vahid Karimipour, <em>The noisy Werner-Holevo channel and its properties</em>, Phys. Rev. A 109, 052620 (2024), arXiv:2310.15353v7, subsection “Spectral properties of the channel,” ask:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The question remains whether, within the range of $0\leq x\leq \frac{2}{3}$, the channel can be described as the exponential of Lindbladian dynamics. We will explore this question in our future work.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is verbatim from <code>ModifiedLSChannel-12.tex</code>, line 249, in the downloaded v7 source, md5 <code>bcff52a86196a2e1a0054a34c48a8117</code>. The channel formula is at line 153; its spectral multipliers and determinant are at lines 237–247. The <a href="../Library/QuantumContext/roofehkarimipour2024wernerholevo.md">literature note</a> records these locators.</p>
<p>The module defines, for every real $x$, the complex-linear map on $M_3(\mathbb C)$</p>
<p>$\Lambda_x(X)=(1-x)X-\frac{x}{2}X^{\mathsf T}+\frac{x}{2}\operatorname{tr}(X)I_3.$</p>
<p>This is <code>wernerHolevo</code>; the source uses the same formula with $0\le x\le1$. <code>IsGKSLGenerator G</code> means that there exist $m\in\mathbb N$, a Hermitian $H\in M_3(\mathbb C)$ and matrices $V_k\in M_3(\mathbb C)$ indexed by $k\in\mathrm{Fin},m$ such that, for every $X\in M_3(\mathbb C)$,</p>
<p>$G(X)=-i(HX-XH)+\sum_k\left(V_kXV_k^\dagger-\frac12(V_k^\dagger V_kX+XV_k^\dagger V_k)\right).$</p>
<p>The empty jump family is allowed. <code>generatorExp G</code> is the ordinary exponential of the $9\times9$ complex matrix of $G$ in the matrix-unit basis, transported back to a linear map. Equality is equality on the entire complex matrix space.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/21274">#21274</a> fixes the statement: for every $x\in[0,2/3]$, there exists such a $G$ with $\operatorname{generatorExp}(G)=\Lambda_x$ if and only if $x=0$. This statement is proved.</p>
