<p>The source's introduction, equation (1), defines ordinary complex Toeplitz matrices by equality of adjacent southeast diagonal entries. Section 4 explicitly writes the left-multiplier constructions <code>M = P T_1 T_2</code> and <code>M = P_0 rref(M)</code>. The ambient matrices are complex and square, including singular matrices. The version was submitted 2025-06-19; the inspected arXiv history lists v1 only and no journal reference. The <a href="../Library/Eigenstructure/garciamarco2025toeplitzfactors.md">literature note</a> gives the original definitions and neighboring questions.</p>
<p>The target F is the complete first assertion:</p>
<p>$$
