<blockquote>
<p>In fact, for rank-one G, Romeo and Tilli [23, Theorem 1.2] proved (1.1) with c1=1 and the unitary restriction (2.3) with c2=1. They explicitly left the corresponding nonsingular version of Problem 3 unresolved; see [23, Remark 3.1].</p>
