<p>For every natural $n$, every complex $n\times n$ matrix $G$ with
$\operatorname{rank}(G)\le1$, and every unitarily invariant norm $N$, the
precise conclusion is</p>
<p>$$
\inf_{W\in\mathrm{GL}<em>n(\mathbb C)}
N(W\circ G)N(W^{-1}\circ G^{\mathsf T})
=\min</em>{P\text{ permutation}}N(P\circ G)^2.
$$</p>
<p>A permutation minimizing $N(P\circ G)$ attains the infimum. The transpose
of $G$ is plain transpose. The zero matrix, zero weights, and $n=0$ are
