{M(a+\delta;c;x)M(b;c;x)}.$$</p>
<p>Theorem 4 assumes $\delta&gt;0$ throughout. Its inequality (10), for
$b&gt;a&gt;0$ and $c,x&gt;0$, is</p>
<p>$$\frac{\Gamma(a+\delta)\Gamma(b)}
{\Gamma(b+\delta)\Gamma(a)}&lt;R(x)&lt;1.$$</p>
<p>Its inequality (11), for $a&lt;b&lt;c-\delta$ and $c&gt;0&gt;x$, is</p>
<p>$$\frac{\Gamma(c-a-\delta)\Gamma(c-b)}
