the required determinant comparison between powers one half and one for every internal weight, refuting Conjecture 5.7.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="gan-kim-2024-wasserstein-weak-log-majorization"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Gan–Kim: weak log-majorization monotonicity of Wasserstein power means</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Luyining Gan and Sejong Kim, <em>Weak log-majorization between the geometric and Wasserstein means</em>, arXiv:2301.07934v4, §5, Conjecture 5.7. See <a href="../Library/Eigenstructure/gankim2024wasserstein.md">gankim2024wasserstein</a>.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjecture 5.7. Let A, B ∈ Pm and t ∈ (0, 1). Then (A^p ⋄t B^p)^{1/p} ց≺w log exp((1 − t) log A + t log B) as p ց 0.</p>
