</blockquote>
<p>Here $A#B=A^{1/2}(A^{-1/2}BA^{-1/2})^{1/2}A^{1/2}$ and $\mathbb P_m$ is the cone of complex Hermitian positive definite matrices. Weak log-majorization compares every initial product of decreasingly sorted eigenvalues, including the product of all $m$ eigenvalues.</p>
<p>For $F_t(p)=(A^p\diamond_tB^p)^{1/p}$, the decreasing arrow is the conjunction of the comparisons $F_t(p)\prec_{w\log}F_t(q)$ for all real $0&lt;p&lt;q$ and the right-hand limit $F_t(p)\to\exp((1-t)\log A+t\log B)$ as $p\downarrow0$. The formal statement includes both assertions, every finite dimension, all complex positive definite inputs and every real $0&lt;t&lt;1$.</p>
