source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Minimum Seidel energy of chain graphs</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Santanu Mandal, Ranjit Mehatari and Kinkar Chandra Das, <em>On the spectrum and energy of Seidel matrix for chain graphs</em>, arXiv:2205.00310v1, Conjecture 4.14:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Let $G$ be a chain graph of order $n$ with the binary string $b=0^{s_1}1^{t_1}0^{s_2}\ldots0^{s_k}1^{t_k}$ such that $\sum_i(s_i+t_i)=n$, $s_i\ge1$ and $t_i\ge1$. Then $SE(G)\ge SE(H)$, where $H\in\Gamma_{n,k}$. Moreover, the equality holds if and only if $G\in\Gamma_{n,k}$.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Here $\Gamma_{n,k}$ has binary word $0^{s_1}(10)^{k-1}1^{t_k}$ with positive endpoints, each at most $n-2k+1$, and $s_1+t_k=n-2k+2$. Seidel matrices are $J-I-2A$ and energy sums the absolute eigenvalues with multiplicity. The theorem quantifies over every comparator $H$.</p>
