<p>The source's two-term moving average is $Y_n=X_{n-1}+X_n$, with records counted from the first complete sum $Y_2$. The formal <code>recordProb</code> event is the strict comparison $Y_n&gt;\max(Y_2,\ldots,Y_{n-1})$ in the preregistered zero-based coordinates. The theorem <code>movingAverage_record_bound</code> proves the bound for every atomless probability measure on $\mathbb R$ and every $n\ge3$; <code>result</code> specializes it to the density-form <code>claim</code>. Its <code>Continuous f</code> hypothesis is the density restriction fixed by preregistration <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/15864">#15864</a>; discontinuous densities in the paper are covered by the public atomless theorem.</p>
