ontribution</span>Escobar, Garcia and Minenkova (arXiv:2507.18767, Section 4) conjecture that a 7 x 7 Jacobi matrix with symmetric spectrum realizing perfect state transfer does not have early state exclusion if and only if its positive eigenvalues are integer multiples of the smallest positive eigenvalue, and they prove two one-parameter families of spectra.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="escobar-garcia-2025-seven-site-early-state-exclusion"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Early state exclusion in seven-site chains with symmetric spectrum</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>M. G. Escobar, V. Garcia and A. Minenkova, <em>Early State Exclusion in 7-Qubit
