<blockquote>
<p>We consider a special case where $J$ has symmetric spectrum in section 3, meaning that for ${\lambda_k}<em>{k = 0}^N$, $\lambda_j = -\lambda</em>{N - j}$ for all $1 \leq j \leq N - 1$.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Let $J$ be a Jacobi matrix realizing PST at earliest time $T &gt; 0$. If there exists some $\tau \in (0, T)$ such that $\langle e^{-iJ\tau}\e_0, \e_0 \rangle = 0$, then we say that $J$ exhibits \textbf{early state exclusion} (ESE) at time $\tau$.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>and conjectures:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Let $J$ be a $7 \times 7$ Jacobi matrix with symmetric spectrum realizing PST. Then $J$ does not have ESE if and only if its positive eigenvalues are integer multiples of the smallest positive eigenvalue.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Issue #14487 fixes the reading. &quot;Symmetric spectrum&quot; is read as closure of the
