source's condition; the eigenvalues are Mathlib's
<code>(pathHamiltonian_isHermitian r q).eigenvalues</code>, and the spectrum is symmetric
when the negative of every eigenvalue is an eigenvalue; <code>T</code> is an earliest time
when <code>0 &lt; T</code>, there is transfer at <code>T</code> and at no time in <code>(0, T)</code>; early state
exclusion is a <code>τ ∈ (0, T)</code> with <code>hamiltonianPropagator J τ 0 0 = 0</code>; the
divisibility condition asks for a positive eigenvalue that is the least
positive one and of which every positive eigenvalue is an integer multiple.
The statement is universally quantified over <code>r</code>, <code>q</code> and <code>T</code>.</p>
