er ZMod 3 that preserve Q, with invertible β at every g ≠ 1: every vector over ZMod 3 lifts, and the determinant of β reduces to a unit.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>When 3 divides N, no copy of the symmetric group S3 inside the anyon permutation symmetries of the ZN x ZN SymTFT has all of its non-identity elements beta-invertible, as conjectured by D.-C.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="lu-sun-zhang-2024-beta-invertible-s3-obstruction"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>No β-invertible S₃ symmetry in the ℤ_N × ℤ_N SymTFT when 3 ∣ N</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>D.-C. Lu, Z. Sun and Z. Zhang (arXiv:2406.12151, JHEP 11 (2025) 081) study
G-ality defects of 2d QFTs through the SymTFT of the finite Abelian symmetry
<code>A</code>. The anyons of the SymTFT are the pairs <code>(a, â) ∈ A ⊕ Â</code>, and an anyon
permutation symmetry is a block matrix <code>U = (α β; γ δ)</code> with <code>β : Â → A</code> that
preserves the self-statistics and the braiding; <code>U</code> is β-invertible when <code>β</code>
is invertible. A G-ality extension needs a subgroup isomorphic to <code>G</code> whose
