<p>A position is a finite multiset of positive natural numbers. A move chooses
one occurrence of a heap h and a positive integer d ≤ h, requires d to divide
every other heap, and replaces h by h − d, omitting a zero remainder. The
removal need not divide h. The Grundy value is the mex of follower values.</p>
