<p>Item 1 of Theorem 1.1, at lines 502–516, states that, assuming $n_\varsigma&lt;\bar{\mathfrak p}(q)$, the unit $P_\varsigma$ and the projected boundary generators
$U_i^{\mathrm{JW}}=P_\varsigma U_{s_1+\cdots+s_i}^{\mathrm{TL}}P_\varsigma$, $1\le i&lt;d$, form a minimal generating set. The conjecture replaces the total-size hypothesis by the individual-box hypothesis.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/25910">#25910</a> fixes the generation assertion <code>claim</code>: for every nonzero complex $q$, every list $\varsigma$ of positive sizes individually below $\bar{\mathfrak p}(q)$, and every $T\in\mathrm{TL}<em>{n</em>\varsigma}(-q-q^{-1})$, the sandwich $P_\varsigma TP_\varsigma$ belongs to the ambient unital complex subalgebra generated by $P_\varsigma$ and the $U_i^{\mathrm{JW}}$. This assertion is refuted, which suffices to refute the conjecture independently of minimality. The definitions and source locator are in <a href="../Library/StatisticalMechanics/florespeltola2018generators.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
