<p>For every finite-dimensional tripartite density operator $\rho_{ABC}$, let
$\rho_{AB}=\operatorname{Tr}<em>C\rho</em>{ABC}$,
$\rho_{BC}=\operatorname{Tr}<em>A\rho</em>{ABC}$ and
$\rho_B=\operatorname{Tr}<em>{AC}\rho</em>{ABC}$. The proposed assertion is</p>
<p>$$
Q(\rho_{ABC})+Q(\rho_B)
\le Q(\rho_{AB})+Q(\rho_{BC}).
$$</p>
<p>The formal statement quantifies over arbitrary finite coordinate
types and the repository's <code>DensityState</code>; changing the parentheses of a
product coordinate type only relabels matrix entries. The original assertion
does not impose commutation, full rank, separability or purity.</p>
