<blockquote>
<p>Let G be an infinite torsion group. Describe the product intersection sets H_Q(G). Must there exist X in H_N^*(G) with X != {1} and X != N?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This dossier anchors exactly the final existence question. The preceding classification
request is outside its selected unit. The source uses N = {1,2,3,...}, ordered h-fold
products with repetitions, and H_N^*(G) for the spectra of asymptotically strictly decreasing
sequences of subsets of the same group G. Empty common intersections are allowed.</p>
