<blockquote>
<p>Definition 3.1. We say that a mapping F : F_{2^n} → F_{2^n} breaks a flat A of F_{2^n} if F(A) is not a flat of F_{2^n}. If F breaks all k-dimensional flats, F is said to be k-breaking.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjecture 3.1. Any APN function F over F_{2^n} is k-breaking for ⌊n/2⌋ + 1 ≤ k ≤ n − 1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A k-flat is a coset a+V of a k-dimensional binary subspace. APN means
that F(x+a)+F(x)=b has at most two solutions for every nonzero a and every b.
The Lean <code>claim : Prop</code> quantifies over all finite fields K of characteristic
two and cardinality 2^n, every such APN function, every permitted k,
every offset and every submodule of binary dimension k. Its conclusion
excludes an image equal to a coset of a subspace of any dimension.
Characteristic two provides the canonical <code>ZMod 2</code>-algebra and module.
A decidable equality instance enables finite fiber counting and places
