<blockquote>
<p>We conjecture that Proposition 10 can be extended to all unitaries with added white noise. We leave this as an open problem.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Proposition 10 assumes $|B'|=|B|=2$. The statement here retains that hypothesis and takes $A'=A=\mathbb C^d$, for every positive natural $d$. For every unitary $U$ on $\mathbb C^d\otimes\mathbb C^2$ and every $p\in[0,1]$, put $N_p(Z)=p\operatorname{tr}(Z)I/(2d)+(1-p)UZU^\dagger$. Then</p>
<p>$$
S_\infty[A\mid B]<em>{N_p}=S</em>\infty(R_AA\mid R_BB)_{\Phi^{N_p}}-\log_2 d.
$$</p>
