<blockquote>
<p>More dramatically, do there exist strongly polynomial families $G_q$, $H_n$ such that the depth function of $\hom(G_q,H_n)$ is constant while the degree function is a polynomial of positive degree?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The binding assertion in <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/21296">#21296</a> reads depth as maximal uniform integer constant depth. Definition 1.2 is downward closed in depth and does not select a pointwise greatest function. The assertion requires one integer $d\geq-1$ for which the coefficient condition holds at every nonnegative parameter, and excludes every larger integer constant. Pointwise greatest depth and maximality on every tail are separate assertions.</p>
<h3>Statement echo</h3>
<p>All Lean names below belong to <code>D5.S3.Combinatorics.ExtremalDensity.BogartJimenezSalazarConstantDepthHom</code> unless an owner is stated.</p>
