| Positive degree and constant depth | <code>claim</code> | Positive natural degree of $g$, a finite integer depth at least $-1$, and failure of every larger uniform integer depth. |</p>
<p>The finiteness encoding by <code>Fin</code> is a labelling choice; no injectivity, connectivity or positive-parameter assumption is added. Rational polynomial coefficients suffice for polynomial integer-count functions. The eventual-nonnegative and guarded coefficient bodies are inlined literally, without duplicate aliases; <code>Polynomial.reverse</code> is used inside the private proof through <code>reverse_coeff</code>.</p>
