an> <span class="result-impact-year">2025</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>GNP arXiv v4 Question 8.20: Dicke extension cones</strong><span class="result-excerpt">Star and complete graph Bose symmetric fully PPT extensions of unnormalized Dicke diagonal operators.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Gulati, Nechita and Park, Positive maps and extendibility hierarchies from copositive matrices, arXiv:2509.15201v4, Question 8.20, asks:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>It equates the full star and complete-graph existence predicates, retaining the same matrix witness in each implication.</p><p><span>The idea</span>The two-particle antisymmetric projector annihilates every Dicke vector.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Star and complete graph Bose symmetric fully PPT extensions of unnormalized Dicke diagonal operators.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="gnp-2025-v4-question-8-20-dicke-extensions"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>GNP arXiv v4 Question 8.20: Dicke extension cones</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Gulati, Nechita and Park, <em>Positive maps and extendibility hierarchies from
copositive matrices</em>, <a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.15201v4#S8.Thmtheorem20">arXiv:2509.15201v4, Question 8.20</a>, asks:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For mixtures of Dicke states, are the following two sets equivalent?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>$$
\mathsf{PPTBExt}<em>{n}^{(\mathcal K_r)}
=\mathsf{PPTBExt}</em>{n}^{(r-1)},\qquad r\ge2.
$$</p>
<p>The target is exactly this versioned question. For every integer $n\ge1$,
$r\ge2$ and every real upper-triangular family $Y_{ij}\ge0$, put</p>
<p>$$
D_{ii}=e_i\otimes e_i,\qquad
D_{ij}=\frac{e_i\otimes e_j+e_j\otimes e_i}{\sqrt2}\quad(i&lt;j),\qquad
\rho=\sum_{1\le i\le j\le n}Y_{ij}|D_{ij}\rangle\langle D_{ij}|.
$$</p>
<p>The star predicate is existence of $E\succeq0$ on $(\mathbb C^n)^{\otimes r}$
with $(I\otimes\Pi_{r-1})E(I\otimes\Pi_{r-1})=E$, every root-leaf marginal
$\rho$, and $E^{T_S}\succeq0$ for every nonempty proper register subset $S$.
The complete-graph predicate is existence of $F\succeq0$ on the same tensor
power with $\Pi_rF\Pi_r=F$, every two-register marginal $\rho$, and
$F^{T_S}\succeq0$ for every such $S$. Here $\Pi_k$ is the orthogonal projector
onto $\operatorname{Sym}^k(\mathbb C^n)$, marginals are genuine unnormalized
partial traces, and transposes use the standard tensor basis. The assertion is
equivalence of these predicates for every $n,r,Y$, including all-zero weights,
without trace normalization or invertibility.</p>
<p>The <a href="../Library/Quantum/gnp2025dickeextensions.md">Library note</a> holds the source
identity and bounded source checks. The original
<a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/26251#issuecomment-6617097653">preregistration</a>
fixes this event before execution; its tier is the first-tier short complete-proof
unit.</p>
