dual count satisfies Gupta&#x27;s total degree bound.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="gupta-2026-miura-residual-degree-conjecture-83"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Gupta&#x27;s uniform residual degree bound</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Chakshu Gupta, <em>One construction for the Miura-ori flip-graph degree sequence</em>, arXiv:2607.05567v3, Conjecture 8.3 (Degree bound), states: “For d ≥ 5 and every split (a,b) with a+b=d and a≤b, the remainder R_(a,b) has total degree at most d−3.” Lemma 8.2 identifies one bivariate polynomial on all m,n≥2d−1. Section 7, Lemma 7.3 identifies the remainder with the configurations whose minima do not all lie on one common boundary side. The source's splits have positive a and b.</p>
