<p>The statement here has $n\geq1$. Each occurrence of a part $a$ independently contributes either $(2a)$ or $(a,a)$; coincident cycle types retain multiplicity. The set $R_3(2n)$ consists of decreasing triples of even natural numbers with sum $2n$, including zero padding. Section 6 asks for the extension from single part sizes to all partitions. The journal version is Electronic Journal of Combinatorics 33(1) (2026), P1.57, DOI 10.37236/14401. Preregistration: <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/17766">#17766</a>.</p>
