theses of this lemma.  released-dossier 094fb6396de5443b721916fb2c061d65383572ed98bf21aad434677c43912e3d "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Quantum information</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Question resolved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>First preprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2025</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Integral adjacency support gives transfer through uniform clone matchings</strong><span class="result-excerpt">Integral adjacency support gives perfect state transfer at pi/2 after adding the same perfect matching in every clone set.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Kirkland, Laplacian quantum walks on blow-up graphs (2025), arXiv:2504.11585v1, DOI 10.1016/j.laa.2025.10.001, ask in Section 11, Future work (main.tex, line 814):</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>Integral adjacency support is required only at the vertex whose clones are to transfer; the graph need not have integral spectrum at every vertex.</p><p><span>The idea</span>Involutivity and the absence of fixed points are not hypotheses of this lemma.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Integral adjacency support gives perfect state transfer at pi/2 after adding the same perfect matching in every clone set.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="monterde-pal-kirkland-2025-blowup-matching-adjacency-transfer"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Integral adjacency support gives transfer through uniform clone matchings</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>H. Monterde, H. Pal and S. Kirkland, <em>Laplacian quantum walks on blow-up graphs</em> (2025), arXiv:2504.11585v1, DOI 10.1016/j.laa.2025.10.001, ask in Section 11, Future work (<code>main.tex</code>, line 814):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Lastly, we ask: does Theorem \ref{pt1} hold for the adjacency case? That is, if $n\equiv 0$ (mod 4), will the addition of an appropriate matching in $\up{n}G$ induce adjacency LPST?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Their Laplacian Theorem <code>pt1</code>, Section 10, Edge perturbation (<code>main.tex</code>, lines 666–668), states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Let $n\equiv 0$ (mod 4) and $v$ be a vertex in $G$ with $\sigma_v(G)\subset\Zl.$ Then the addition of a matching in $T_v$ results in LPST in $\up{n}G$ at $\frac{\pi}{2}$ between the end vertices of every edge inserted.  Moreover, the resulting graph is periodic at all vertices in $T_v$ that are not incident to the newly added edges with period $\frac{\pi}{2}.$</p>
</blockquote>
<p>These quotations retain the source macros: <code>\up{n}G</code> denotes the $n$-fold blow-up and <code>\Zl</code> denotes the integers. In the source, $\sigma_v(G)$ is Laplacian eigenvalue support. The quotations were checked against the downloaded v1 TeX member <code>main.tex</code>, md5 <code>b21c68f0d57c75bbf8eb7530da0c4d04</code>; the definitions are discussed in <a href="../Library/Eigenstructure/monterdepalkirkland2025blowup.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/22707">#22707</a> fixes the reading settled here. Let $G$ be a finite simple graph with adjacency matrix $A_G$, let $v$ have integral <strong>adjacency</strong> eigenvalue support, and let $4\mid n$. Choose a fixed-point-free involution $\rho$ of the $n$ clone indices and insert its perfect matching in <strong>every</strong> clone set. With vertices indexed by $(v,j)$, the resulting matrix is
$H=A_G\otimes J_n+I_m\otimes P_\rho$.
For every clone index $j$, the settlement proves adjacency perfect state transfer at $\pi/2$ between $(v,j)$ and $(v,\rho j)$. This answers the appropriate-matching reading; it does not assert the literal variant with a matching inserted only in $T_v$.</p>
