<p>For positive real x,y put a=(x+y)/2 and d=(x-y)/2. In equations (2)–(4),</p>
<p>$$
G_* = \frac{\Gamma(1+x)\Gamma(1+y)}{\Gamma(1+a)^2},\qquad
H(s,b)=\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}\frac1{(j+b)^s},
$$
$$
S_m=\sum_{k=1}^{m-1}\frac{d^{2k}H(2k,1+a)}{k},\qquad
R_m=\log G_*-S_m.
$$</p>
<p>The expansion order m tends to infinity through integers, with m &gt;= 2
in the source. Its n is already summed out. Every positive real pair,
including x=y and positive integer Gamma arguments, is in scope.</p>
