<p>A. Ayyer and V. Strehl, <em>The spectrum of an asymmetric annihilation process</em>,
arXiv:1008.2134v1, FPSAC 2010, DMTCS Proc. AN, 461–472,
DOI 10.46298/dmtcs.2884, Conjecture 1, p. 466:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The matrix M_L is maximally degenerate in the sense that it has exactly 2L
eigenvectors.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The model has $L$ Boolean sites, bulk transitions $10\to01$ and $11\to00$
at rate $1$, a symmetric left-site flip at rate $\alpha$, and right-site
removal at rate $\beta$. This is the papers' specialization $\lambda=1$.
The matrix entry $M_L(t,s)$ is the rate from $s$ to $t$ off the diagonal;
each diagonal entry is the negative sum of the other entries in its column.</p>
