<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/20152">#20152</a> fixes the restricted reading: for every $N,m\in\mathbb N$, every finite family of traceless complex $N\times N$ jumps $L_k$ and nonnegative real rates $\gamma_k$, put $\mathcal L=\sum_{k\in\mathrm{Fin},m}\gamma_k\mathcal D_{L_k}$, where $\mathcal D_L(\rho)=L\rho L^\dagger-\tfrac12(L^\dagger L\rho+\rho L^\dagger L)$. Define $\nu$ as the supremum of $|\langle\psi|\mathcal L(|\psi\rangle\langle\psi|)|\psi\rangle|$ over $\sum_i|\psi_i|^2=1$. If $\nu&gt;0$, every nonzero eigenmatrix $X$ with $\mathcal L(X)=\lambda X$ would satisfy $|1+\lambda/\nu|\le1$. This is <code>claim</code>; <code>result</code> refutes it.</p>
