$\prod_{i&lt;j}|a_i-a_j|$ on $K^n$, and defines
$F_a(z)=\prod_i(z-a_i)$.</p>
<p>The Lean <code>claim</code> says that for every compact connected $K$, every
$n\geq1$, every Fekete tuple $a$ in $K$, and every $p\in P_n(K)$,
$m(\Lambda_{F_a})\leq m(\Lambda_p)$. Thus <code>result : ¬ claim</code> refutes
exact area minimization in the stated connected-set setting.</p>
