 one-site basis in section 2.1, printed p. 3:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We denote basis vectors in ℂ² by
<code>|↑⟩ = (1, 0)ᵀ, |↓⟩ = (0, 1)ᵀ</code>.</p>
<p>The basis in End(ℂ²) is provided by the Pauli matrices
<code>σ⁺ = [[0, 1], [0, 0]], σ⁻ = [[0, 0], [1, 0]], σᶻ = [[1, 0], [0, −1]]</code>.</p>
<p>We will also use projectors onto the spin-up and spin-down states:
<code>n↑ = ½(1 + σᶻ), n↓ = ½(1 − σᶻ)</code>.</p>
