and the projector <code>Π_{j,j+1}</code> onto the spin-0 state, which is essentially the
antisymmetrizer,
<code>Π_{j,j+1} = ½(1 − P_{j,j+1})</code>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It then prints the Hamiltonian density and periodic Hamiltonian:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><code>F_{j,j+1,j+2} = n↑_j Π_{j+1,j+2} + Π_{j,j+1} n↓_{j+2}</code>. (2.2)</p>
<p>The periodic boundary conditions mean that the Hamiltonian is the cyclic sum,
<code>H = Σ_{j=1}^{N} F_{j,j+1,j+2}</code>. (2.3)</p>
<p>where identification of sites by modulus N is assumed.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Across printed pp. 3-4 the source gives the ordered product and its action:</p>
<blockquote>
