n><span class="result-impact-tag">Question resolved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>Source</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2011</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Merca&#x27;s lifted residue sum at prime order</strong><span class="result-excerpt">Merca&#x27;s lifted residue sum over an even multiplicative-order cycle for a prime modulus.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Merca defines the remainder operation on printed page 2:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>Conjecture 2 asks for an exact identity over the full multiplicative-order cycle.</p><p><span>The idea</span>The half-order power satisfies a^s = -1 in ZMod m: its square is one, while minimality of the order rules out a^s = 1.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Merca&#x27;s lifted residue sum over an even multiplicative-order cycle for a prime modulus.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="merca-2011-lifted-residue-sum-prime-order"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Merca&#x27;s lifted residue sum at prime order</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Merca defines the remainder operation on printed page 2:</p>
