<p>The multiplicative-order convention appears on printed page 17:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For every positive integer m and every integer a relatively prime to m, we denote by ord_m(a) the multiplicative order of a modulo m, i.e., the smallest positive integer n such that a^n ≡ 1 (mod m), namely ord_m(a) = min {n ∈ N∗ | a^n ≡ 1 (mod m)}</p>
