limit divisible</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Mikhail Shkolnikov, <em>Algebraic Limits of Sandpiles</em>, arXiv:2506.09912v3, Section 3, states that the image of the direct limit of rectangular sandpile groups may be a rational subtorus or a divisible group. The settled question is the divisibility alternative: for every positive rectangle, every circle-valued sandpile function on it, and every positive integer $k$, a later rectangular stage contains a sandpile function whose $k$-fold sum equals the signed reflected image of the original function.</p>
