<p>For $n\in\mathbb N$, set
$a(n)=\sum_{k\geq0} 3^k \binom{k^2}{n}/(4)^{k+1}$.
The settlement is <strong>Proved</strong>: for every $n\geq1$ there is $q\in\mathbb Z$ with $a(n)=21q$.
The preregistration is <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/21834">#21834</a>.</p>
