rrelations in bipartite quantum systems, arXiv:1607.06585v1, abstract:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The source proposes CM as an algebraic measure of correlations.</p><p><span>The idea</span>Write x for the Bloch vector of A, T for the correlation matrix, and Q = T − x yᵀ for the connected correlation matrix.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>For every two-qubit density matrix, one-sided trace-norm geometric discord is at most maximal mutual correlation.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="jakobczyk-2016-trace-norm-discord-mutual-correlation-bound"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">arXiv</p><h3>Maximal mutual correlation dominates the trace-norm geometric discord of two qubits</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>L. Jakóbczyk, <em>Maximal mutual correlation: an algebraic measure of correlations in bipartite quantum systems</em>, arXiv:1607.06585v1, abstract:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In the  states containing some quantum correlations, maximal mutual correlation is always greater or equal to geometric measure of quantum discord. This relation is proved to be valid in the class of Bell - diagonal states and it is conjectured that  is also true for general two - qubit states.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The quantities are defined as follows:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Trace-norm geometric discord:</strong> D₁(ρ) = min over projective measurements 𝒫 on A of ‖ρ − 𝒫(ρ)‖₁, where 𝒫(ρ) = Σ_k (P_k ⊗ I) ρ (P_k ⊗ I).</li>
<li><strong>Maximal mutual correlation:</strong> C_M(ρ) is the supremum of |ω(ab) − ω(a)ω(b)| over local a, b of operator norm 1.</li>
</ul>
<p>The definitions are quoted in <a href="../Library/QuantumContext/jakobczyk2016maximalmutual.md">the literature note</a>; C_M is the quantity of the companion settlement <code>D5/S3/Quantum/Information/GeometricDiscordMutualCorrelationBound</code>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/19706">#19706</a> fixes the reading: for every two-qubit density matrix ρ, D₁(ρ) ≤ C_M(ρ). This is proved.</p>
