<p>$\displaystyle \forall\phi\ne\theta\in X:\quad \left|\sum_{j=1}^d e^{i(\phi_j-\theta_j)}\right|^2\in{0,d}.$</p>
<p>Use the source's representatives with first coordinate zero. For a finite uniformly weighted set, the second-design condition in <code>main.tex</code> lines 198–206 is</p>
<p>$\displaystyle \sum_{\phi\in X}e^{i(\phi_{a_1}+\phi_{a_2}-\phi_{b_1}-\phi_{b_2})}=\begin{cases}|X|&amp;\text{if }{!{a_1,a_2}!}={!{b_1,b_2}!},\0&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}$</p>
<p>for every four coordinate indices. This is the normalized moment equation multiplied by $|X|$.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/26419">#26419</a> fixes the reading <code>claim</code>: for every positive natural number $d$ and finite $X\subset T^d$ with zero first coordinates, cardinality $d^2$, the second-design condition, the overlap condition, and $0\in X$, there exists an additive subgroup of $T^d$ whose carrier is exactly $X$. The added identity hypothesis weakens the source's universal assertion. Even this weaker assertion is refuted.</p>
