<blockquote>
<p>Under hypotheses of Theorem 2 the function µ → g(µ, x) is log-concave on (0, ∞) for each fixed x ≥ 0. Moreover, the function x → g(µ + α, x)g(µ + β, x) − g(µ, x)g(µ + α + β, x) has positive power series coefficients for µ ≥ −1 and µ + α ≥ 0, µ + β ≥ 0, where α, β &gt; 0.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Theorem 2's sequence hypotheses are nontriviality, nonnegativity,
log-concavity $g_{n-1}g_{n+1}\le g_n^2$ for $n\ge1$, and no internal
zeros. Equation (20) is</p>
<p>$$g(\mu,x)=\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}\frac{g_n x^n}{\Gamma(n+\mu)},$$</p>
<p>where reciprocal Gamma is zero at its poles. Only the “Moreover” clause
is refuted; the first assertion is not addressed.</p>
