<p>The relevant branch of Theorem 3, page 5, states verbatim (line breaks joined):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Theorem 3. If p ≤ q and conditions (13) are satisfied, then ∆f (α, β; x) ≥ 0 for x ≥ 0, µ, β ≥ 0 and α ∈ N, where ∆f (α, β; x) is defined in (9) with f from (10). Moreover, if α ≤ β + 1, then δm ≥ 0 for all m ∈ N0.</p>
