<p>For positive parameter vectors with $p\le q$, equations (9) and (10) are</p>
<p>$$
c(t)=\frac{\prod_i\Gamma(a_i+t)}{\prod_j\Gamma(b_j+t)},\qquad
f(\mu;x)=\sum_{n=0}^\infty c(\mu+n)\frac{x^n}{n!},
$$</p>
<p>$$
\Delta_f(\alpha,\beta;x)=f(\mu+\alpha;x)f(\mu+\beta;x)
-f(\mu;x)f(\mu+\alpha+\beta;x).
$$</p>
<p>Condition (13) is</p>
<p>$$
\frac{e_{q-j}(\mathbf b)}{e_{p-j}(\mathbf a)}
\le\frac{e_{q-j-1}(\mathbf b)}{e_{p-j-1}(\mathbf a)}\quad(0\le j&lt;p).
$$</p>
<p>This dossier concerns $\Delta_f\ge0$ for all $x\ge0$, $\mu\ge1$ and
