<blockquote>
<p>For the energy game, the Shapley value is in the core.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The source defines the energy of a finite simple undirected graph as the
sum of absolute adjacency eigenvalues, with multiplicity. Its game has
$w_G(S)=\mathcal E(G[S])$. For each vertex $i$ its allocation is</p>
<p>$$
\phi_i(w_G)=\sum_{S\subseteq V\setminus{i}}
\frac{|S|!(|V|-|S|-1)!}{|V|!}
\bigl(w_G(S\cup{i})-w_G(S)\bigr).
$$</p>
<p>The core consists of all $x$ satisfying
$\sum_{i\in S}x_i\ge w_G(S)$ for every coalition $S$ and
$\sum_{i\in V}x_i=w_G(V)$. The conjecture quantifies over every finite
simple graph, without connectedness, degree or bipartiteness assumptions.
<a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/21951">Preregistration #21951</a>
binds this universal proposition and its expected refutation.
The <a href="../Library/GraphInvariants/arizmendi2020energygame.md">Library note</a>
records the versioned source and the literal defining formulas.</p>
