<div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>What relation must equiangular parameters satisfy when the Gerzon bound is attained?</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The known identity omitted two characteristic classes of dimensions. The result includes them and allows isotropic vectors.</p><p><span>The idea</span>Trace identities and fourth moments establish the same parameter relation in both scalar-frame branches.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>At Gerzon equality, the parameters satisfy a² = (d + 2)b in every dimension at least two over fields of characteristic different from two.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>The theorem gives a necessary identity at equality; it does not construct extremal configurations in every dimension.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="greaves-iverson-jasper-mixon-2021-gerzon-equality-identity"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Gerzon equality fixes the equiangular parameters in every dimension at least two</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>G. R. W. Greaves, J. W. Iverson, J. Jasper and D. G. Mixon, <em>Frames over finite fields: Equiangular lines in orthogonal geometry</em>, arXiv:2012.13642v2, Example 5.8, page 21, asks:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The authors do not know how to construct an ETF with any of the parameters given in Table 4. In particular, every instance of Gerzon equality that we currently know satisfies the identity a² = (d + 2)b, but this equation does not occur anywhere in Table 4 (where b = 1). Proposition 2.10 implies that a² = (d + 2)b whenever Gerzon’s bound is saturated, d ≢ₚ 0, and d ≢ₚ 1. The authors do not know if these conditions can be removed.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The answer is affirmative for every $d\ge2$. Preregistration: <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/16342">#16342</a>. The <a href="../Library/QuadraticForms/greavesiversonjaspermixon2021orthogonalframes.md">Library note</a> records Definition 2.8, Propositions 2.9–2.10 and the source locator.</p>
