4). a self-orthogonal binary stabilizer space containing parity on at most fourteen modes has a logical operator of weight below four whenever twice its dimension is less than the number of modes. the proof uses induction. their optimality remains open here, as do extensions that remove the parity convention; no classification or uniqueness of sixteen-mode codes is established. released-dossier c0826b533371b8027e156c2dea4184797218db17423533f8f63408282a704db1 "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Quantum information</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Question resolved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>First preprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2017</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>No parity Majorana code on at most fourteen modes has distance four and a logical qubit</strong><span class="result-excerpt">A self-orthogonal binary stabilizer space containing parity on at most fourteen modes has a logical operator of weight below four whenever twice its dimension is less than the number of modes.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Hastings, Small Majorana Fermion Codes, Quantum Inf.</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The source&#x27;s distance-four codes target correction of errors on a single Majorana mode (c.tex, lines 121–124).</p><p><span>The idea</span>The proof uses induction.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>A self-orthogonal binary stabilizer space containing parity on at most fourteen modes has a logical operator of weight below four whenever twice its dimension is less than the number of modes.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>Their optimality remains open here, as do extensions that remove the parity convention; no classification or uniqueness of sixteen-mode codes is established.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="hastings-2017-small-majorana-fourteen-mode-distance-four"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>No parity Majorana code on at most fourteen modes has distance four and a logical qubit</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>M. B. Hastings, <em>Small Majorana Fermion Codes</em>, Quantum Inf. Comput. 17(13–14), 1191–1205 (2017), arXiv:1703.00612v1, Section II.B, PDF p. 5 (<code>c.tex</code>, line 272):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For $N_{\rm maj}=14$, we performed a numerical search (described in the next section) for a code with $N_{\rm stab}=6$ and did not succeed. Hence, we believe that no such code exists, i.e., we believe that $N_{\rm maj}=16$ is the minimum number of modes to have $d=4,K&gt;0$.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The paper uses $N_{\rm maj}$ for the number of Majorana modes, $N_{\rm stab}$ for the number of independent stabilizers, and $K=N_{\rm maj}/2-N_{\rm stab}$ for the number of logical qubits. Its stabilizer bit strings form a self-orthogonal binary subspace $C$, meaning $x\cdot y=0$ for every $x,y\in C$, including $x=y$ (<code>c.tex</code>, lines 85–105). Logical operators correspond to $C^\perp\setminus C$, and distance is their minimum Hamming weight (lines 108–113). The paper requires the all-ones fermion-parity vector $\mathbf1$ to belong to $C$ (lines 115–118). These definitions and the quotation are also recorded in <a href="../Library/Hamming/hastings2017smallmajorana.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/23984">#23984</a> fixes the statement: for every natural number $n\le14$ and every binary linear subspace $C\le\mathbb F_2^n$, if $C$ is self-orthogonal, $\mathbf1\in C$, and $2\dim C&lt;n$, then</p>
<p>$\exists v\in C^\perp\setminus C,\quad \operatorname{wt}(v)&lt;4.$</p>
<p>This is <code>claim</code>, and <code>result : claim</code> proves it. The conclusion supplies a logical operator directly; it does not define distance through an infimum. The sixteen-mode existence statement is outside <code>claim</code>.</p>
