<p>a(n) = sigma_n(n): sum of n-th powers of divisors of n.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Velin Yanev's FORMULA conjecture (<code>%F</code>, verbatim):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjecture: sigma_m(n) = sigma(n^m * rad(n)^(m-1))/sigma(rad(n)^(m-1)) for n &gt; 0 and m &gt; 0, where sigma = A000203 and rad = A007947. - <em>Velin Yanev</em>, Aug 24 2017</p>
</blockquote>
<p>AUTHOR (<code>%A</code>, verbatim):</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>Olivier Gérard</em></p>
</blockquote>
<p>The exact formal statement, with all variables natural, is
<code>forall n m, 0 &lt; n -&gt; 0 &lt; m -&gt; sigma m n * sigma 1 (primeRadical n ^ (m - 1)) = sigma 1 (n ^ m * primeRadical n ^ (m - 1))</code>, where
<code>D5/S1/Deficit/AlmostAdditivity.primeRadical n = ∏ p ∈ n.primeFactors, p</code>
is the frozen natural radical (A007947).
Both sides are positive under these hypotheses. The denominator is also
positive, so this multiplied-out form is equivalent to the quoted identity,
including its exact natural-number quotient. Subtraction in <code>m - 1</code> is
