Integer sequences (OEIS)</p><h3>Browne&#x27;s Chebyshev numerator and floor product</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Anthony Browne's final FORMULA in OEIS A164660, revision 19, reads:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a(n+1) = Product_{k=1..n} ( 1-2*(floor(k^n/n)-floor((k^n -1)/n)) ) = (-1)^(A003557(n)) for n&gt;0 (conjecture). - <em>Anthony Browne</em>, May 29 2016</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The sequence, introduced by Wolfdieter Lang, defines:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a(n) = numerator(Sum_{m=1..n+1} IT(n,m)), n&gt;=0, with IT(n,m):= A164658(n,m)/A164659(n,m) (coefficient triangle from the indefinite integral Integral_{x} T(n,x), n&gt;=0, in lowest terms).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Let $T_m$ be the first-kind Chebyshev polynomial over $\mathbb Q$ and put
$S_m=\sum_{j=1}^{m+1}[X^{j-1}]T_m/j$ and $a(m)=\operatorname{num}(S_m)$,
where the numerator is reduced and signed with positive denominator.
Let $R(n)=\operatorname{rad}(n)$, including $R(1)=1$.
For every positive natural $n$, the theorem proves</p>
<p>$$
a(n+1)=\prod_{k=1}^{n}\left(1-2\left(\left\lfloor\frac{k^n}{n}\right\rfloor-\left\lfloor\frac{k^n-1}{n}\right\rfloor\right)\right)=(-1)^{n/R(n)}.
$$</p>
<p>The division and subtraction inside each floor are rational; $n/R(n)$ is natural integer division.</p>
