<p>The source defines $T_{jk}=\operatorname{Tr}[\rho_{AB}\sigma_j\otimes\sigma_k]$ for $j,k=1,2,3$ in Sec. II, Eq. (2) (<code>finalversion.tex</code>, lines 129–133). Thus each term in Eq. (36) is the sum of the nine squared real entries of a two-qubit correlation matrix.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/26136">#26136</a> fixes the reading. In the module, a vector $\psi:(\mathrm{Fin},4\to\mathrm{Fin},2)\to\mathbb C$ has its sixteen computational-basis amplitudes indexed by four bits. The qubits are ordered $A,B,C,D$. The indices $X=0,1,2$ denote targets $B,C,D$, and $i,j=0,1,2$ denote Pauli directions $x,y,z$. Let $P_{Xij}$ be <code>wordOp (twoBodyWord X i j)</code>: Pauli $i$ on $A$, Pauli $j$ on target $X$, and identities elsewhere. The definition <code>rankOneDensity</code> is the outer product $\psi\psi^{\dagger}$, and <code>correlation</code> is</p>
<p>$$c_{Xij}(\psi)=\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{Tr}[\psi\psi^{\dagger}P_{Xij}].$$</p>
<p>The proposition <code>claim</code> states, exactly,</p>
<p>$$\forall\psi,\quad \sum_q\overline{\psi(q)}\psi(q)=1\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
\sum_{X=0}^{2}\sum_{i=0}^{2}\sum_{j=0}^{2}c_{Xij}(\psi)^2\leq3.$$</p>
<p>The module proves <code>result : claim</code>. The correspondence with reduced-state correlation matrices is explained below.</p>
