<p>The first terms (<code>%S</code>, verbatim excerpt) are
<code>0,3,4,4,6,7,8,5,5,9,12,8,14,...</code>.</p>
<p>For every natural n, define
<code>F(n) = Sum (p + factorization(n)(p))</code> over <code>p</code> in <code>primeFactors(n)</code>. The
literal proved statement is
<code>forall m : Nat, 4 &lt; m -&gt; exists t : Nat, F^[t](m) = 5</code>. Thus &quot;reaches 5&quot;
means that some finite iterate equals 5. The values follow the cycle
<code>5 -&gt; 6 -&gt; 7 -&gt; 8 -&gt; 5</code>; four is a fixed point, so <code>m &gt; 4</code> is sharp; and
