E (<code>%N</code>, verbatim):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Let cn(n,k) denote the number of times 11..1 (k 1's) appears in the binary representation of n; a(n) = n - cn(n,1) + cn(n,2) - cn(n,3) + cn(n,4) - ... .</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The settled FORMULA (<code>%F</code>, verbatim):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjecture: a(n) = n - A329320(n) for n &gt;= 0 (noticed by Sequence Machine). - <em>Mikhail Kurkov</em>, Oct 13 2021</p>
</blockquote>
<p>AUTHOR (<code>%A</code>, verbatim):</p>
<blockquote>
<p><em>N. J. A. Sloane</em>, Apr 07 2014</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Occurrences overlap. In the binary word <code>111</code>, the counts for block lengths
1, 2, and 3 are 3, 2, and 1; hence <code>a(7)=7-3+2-1=5</code>, as required by the
data. Numbering bits from the least significant end preserves counts of
the palindromic block of ones. The index range has length <code>n.size</code>, the
binary length, with the empty range at zero.</p>
<p>For every natural <code>n</code>, define <code>cn(n,k)</code> to count starts <code>i&lt;n.size</code> with
<code>n.testBit(i+j)=true</code> for every <code>j&lt;k</code>. Define <code>b(n)</code> to count starts
<code>i&lt;n.size</code> for which <code>v_2(n div 2^i+1)</code> is odd, where <code>div</code> is natural
floor division. For positive <code>n</code> this is the A329320 NAME sum under the
supplied characterization <code>1-A035263(m)=[v_2(m) odd]</code> for positive <code>m</code>.
All valuation arguments are positive. At <code>n=0</code> both ranges are empty,
so the identity reads <code>0=0</code>.</p>
<p>The exact Lean statement, with integer subtraction and integer summands, is:</p>
<pre><code class="language-lean">theorem result (n : ℕ) :
    (n : ℤ) - ∑ k ∈ Finset.Icc 1 n.size, (-1 : ℤ) ^ (k + 1) * (cn n k : ℤ) =
      (n : ℤ) - (b n : ℤ)
</code></pre>
<p>Only Kurkov's quoted <code>%F</code> line is settled. The interpretation of A329320
uses the cited valuation characterization; the morphism-to-valuation
identity for A035263 is not independently formalized here.</p>
