z–Viruel Question 31</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Kaygorodov, Martín González and Viruel, <em>Evolution algebras: a survey of results and a list of open problems</em>, arXiv:2610.22248v1, section 2.2.5, page 24, ask: “Let G be a linear algebraic group over 𝕜. Is there a finite-dimensional evolution 𝕜-algebra A with Aut(A) ≅ G(𝕜) as abstract groups? with Aut(A) ≅ G as algebraic groups? with 𝐀𝐮𝐭(A) ≅ G as group schemes?”</p>
