ext question</span>The other half, a general method to compute post-processed improvements for arbitrary channels, remains open in this settlement.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="masini-theurer-plenio-2021-postprocessed-improvement-unfaithfulness"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Biased post-processed interferometric improvements are not faithful</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>M. Masini, T. Theurer and M. B. Plenio, <em>Coherence of operations and interferometry</em>, Phys. Rev. A 103, 042426 (2021), arXiv:2102.04863v2, Section IV (Conclusions), <code>PaperMasiniTheurerPlenio.tex</code>, line 300:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Whilst we provided a method to compute the pre-processed improvements and showed that they are not faithful for $\lambda\ne\mu$, it is an open question whether there exist analogous results for the post-processed cases.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The source defines faithfulness in Section II A, line 153:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>$M(\Theta)=0$ exactly if $\Theta$ is a free channel.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Here $\mu=1-\lambda$, $\Delta$ removes off-diagonal entries in the chosen incoherent basis, and the free channels for coherence creation are the maximally incoherent operations, characterized by $\Psi\Delta=\Delta\Psi\Delta$ (Section II A, lines 132–134). The phase channel is conjugation by $U=\operatorname{diag}(e^{i\phi_k})$ (Section II B, lines 171–175). The post-processed improvement is defined in Section III B, Eq. (14), line 273:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>$N_{\lambda,\vec{\phi}}(\Theta):=\max_{\Psi\in\mathcal{MIO}}\left|\left|\left(\lambda-\mu \Lambda_{\vec{\phi}}\right) \Psi \Theta\Delta\right|\right|_1-|\lambda-\mu |$.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The source calls the operation norm the induced trace norm (Section III A, line 202). The formal reading uses $|\Phi|<em>{1\to1}=\sup</em>{|A|_1\le1}|\Phi(A)|_1$ over all complex matrices, with no positivity or Hermiticity restriction on $A$.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/22607">#22607</a> fixes the faithfulness half of the question: for every $\lambda\in[0,1]$ with $\lambda\ne\tfrac12$, every natural $M\ge1$, and every $\vec\phi\in\mathbb R^M$, there exists a qubit-to-qubit channel $\Theta$ that is not maximally incoherent and has $N_{\lambda,\vec\phi}(\Theta)=0$, optimizing over all MIO channels from the qubit to dimension $M$. This is proved.</p>
<p>The definitions and source locators are collected in <a href="../Library/Divergence/masinitheurerplenio2021interferometry.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
