<p>Issue #19173 fixes the formal statement. For a received binary word, the posterior on uniformly transmitted inputs is proportional to the number of increasing index sets realizing the received word as a subsequence. Entropy is Shannon entropy in bits. The claim gives the two alternating families and their complements, the exact deletion and large insertion maxima, and the finite insertion cases of received lengths two, three and four.</p>
<h3>Statement echo</h3>
