<p>The free O(2) measure is the product of the rotation-invariant probability
measures on S¹. Its angle coordinates use normalized Haar measure on
Real.Angle, with spin θ = (cos θ, sin θ). The basic observables are all pair
inner products σᵢ·σⱼ, i &lt; j. The parity map assigns one bit to each endpoint
of each pair; the source's evenness means ρ(u) = 0.</p>
<p>For every p ≥ 1, the proposed assertion requires, for every m ≥ 0, every
