Discrete Applied Mathematics 322 (2022), 391–403,
DOI 10.1016/j.dam.2022.08.027:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Let X to be a non-empty set of even numbers, each of which is at least 4. Let Y to be a non-empty set of odd numbers, each of which is at least 5. Let x = 2c and y be the smallest elements of X and Y, respectively.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>Family A: C = {1, 3} ∪ X, or C = {1, 3} ∪ X ∪ Y.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>The nim-sequence for all games of cut in this family are all precisely (0, 1)^c (+2).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is Conjecture 1. Preregistration:
<a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/19674">#19674</a>.
The settling theorem is
<code>D5.S0.Certificates.Games.EllisThanatipanondaCutFamilyA.result</code>.</p>
