<p>The settled classical statement uses a finite type $x$ and arbitrary maps $a,b,c:x\times x\to x\times x$. The circuit applies $a$ to the first two wires, $b$ to the first output of $a$ and the third wire, and $c$ to the second output of $a$ and the second output of $b$. If its six-column graph is an index-one orthogonal array of strength $3$, the question is whether each four-column gate graph is an index-one orthogonal array of strength $2$.</p>
