arent on ℓ² to a parent of the 2 × 2 compressions.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>For every natural n at least one, some n+1 binary measurements on the full one-mode Fock space remain incompatible under pure loss of transmissivity 1/n.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="mehboudi-rezaeinia-rahimi-keshari-2025-loss-incompatibility"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>n + 1 displaced on-off measurements stay incompatible under pure loss of transmissivity 1/n</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>M. Mehboudi, F. Rezaeinia and S. Rahimi-Keshari, <em>Measurement incompatibility under loss</em>, arXiv:2411.05920v3 (Phys. Rev. Lett. 135, 100202 (2025)), model pure loss by a beam splitter of transmissivity τ with vacuum in its second input, E_τ(ρ) = tr₂(U_BS(ρ ⊗ |0⟩⟨0|)U_BS†), and define the dual by tr(M E_τ(ρ)) = tr(ρ E*_τ(M)). Result 2 shows that for τ ≤ 1/n the images under E*_τ of any n measurements are jointly measurable. Result 3 asserts that some n + 1 measurements stay incompatible at τ = 1/n: &quot;We prove this result numerically for 2 ≤ n ≤ 13, and conjuncture it to hold for arbitrary n.&quot; The measurements are the displaced on-off detections of Eq. (4), M^k_1 = |μ_k⟩⟨μ_k| and M^k_2 = I − M^k_1, with coherent states of equal modulus separated by the phase 2π/(n + 1). The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/QuantumBounds/mehboudi2025lossincompatibility.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/15985">#15985</a> fixes the reading. For every n ≥ 1 there are n + 1 binary POVMs on the single-mode Fock space ℓ²(ℕ) whose images under E*_{1/n} have no parent POVM. A parent ranges over all 2^{n+1} outcome strings and has exactly the given effects as marginals.</p>
<p>The Lean statement takes E*_τ in the source's own form: N is the image of M when tr(M E_τ(|ψ⟩⟨ψ|)) = ⟨ψ, N ψ⟩ for every ψ. Here E_τ(|ψ⟩⟨ψ|) = tr₂(U_BS(|ψ⟩⟨ψ| ⊗ |0⟩⟨0|)U_BS†) is built from the frozen beam splitter and partial trace, and the trace is the Fock-basis sum. Pure states determine an operator, so this relation determines E*_τ(M). The statement asserts both that such images exist and that no family of them has a parent.</p>
