<p>Write $F(a,b;c;r)={}_2F_1(a,b;c;r)$. Inequality (1.6) is</p>
<p>$$\frac{\partial}{\partial b}
\left[\frac{F(a+1,b+1;a+b+1;r)}{F(a,b;a+b;r)}\right]&lt;0,$$</p>
<p>and inequality (1.7) is</p>
<p>$$\frac{F(a+1,2-a;2;r)}{F(a,1-a;1;r)}</p>
<blockquote>
<p>\frac{F(a+1,5/2-a;5/2;r)}{F(a,3/2-a;3/2;r)}.$$</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The first classification is read pointwise in the positive parameters:
for each $a,b&gt;0$, the derivative is negative at every $r\in(0,1)$
if and only if $b\le\sqrt{a(a+1)}$.
The second classification assumes $0&lt;a&lt;1$.
This corrects Baricz's 2007 Conjecture A, which the same paper refutes
as an unrestricted statement.</p>
