<p>Write $[k]=(q^k-q^{-k})/(q-q^{-1})$, ${k}=q^k+q^{-k}$ and
$\alpha_z=z+z^{-1}$. Proposition C.1 defines $X^{(p)}_m$ by (C.3)–(C.4):</p>
<p>$$
X^{(p)}<em>p=1,\qquad
X^{(p)}</em>{p+1}=\alpha_x+\frac{\alpha_y\alpha_w}{{p+1}},
$$</p>
<p>$$
X^{(p)}_{k+1}=\left(\alpha_x+
\frac{{p}\alpha_y\alpha_w}{{k}{k+1}}\right)X^{(p)}<em>k+
\frac{({p}^2-{k}^2)(\alpha_y^2-{k}^2)(\alpha_w^2-{k}^2)}
{(q-q^{-1})^2[2k-1][2k+1]{k}^2}X^{(p)}</em>{k-1}.
$$</p>
<p>Conjecture C.1 states: “For p ⩾ 1, the function X^{(p)}_m(ω, x, y)
specialised to y = εq^m evaluates to” (C.5):</p>
<p>$$
X^{(p)}<em>m(w,x,\varepsilon q^m)=(wx)^{p-m}
\prod</em>{r=-(m-p-1)/2}^{(m-p-1)/2}
(xq^{2r}+\varepsilon w)(\varepsilon q^{2r}+xw).
$$</p>
<p>Proposition C.2 defines $\sigma^{(0)}_{0,m}$ by (C.24)–(C.25):</p>
<p>$$
\sigma_0=1,\qquad \sigma_1=\alpha_x+
\frac{\alpha_y\alpha_w}{{1}},
$$</p>
<p>$$
\sigma_{k+1}=\left(\alpha_x+
\frac{2\alpha_y\alpha_w}{{k}{k+1}}\right)\sigma_k-
\frac{[k]^2(\alpha_y^2-{k}^2)(\alpha_w^2-{k}^2)}
{[2k+1][2k-1]{k}^2}\sigma_{k-1}.
$$</p>
<p>Conjecture C.2 states: “The intermediate seed states σ^{(0)}_{0,m}(w, x, y)
specialised to y = εq^m evaluate to” (C.26), the same product with $p=0$.</p>
