<p>Both expressions use the same vector; repeated rates retain their multiplicity. The domain includes arbitrary positive real coordinates, $N=2$, and unbounded finite $N$. A bound only on an exceptional-rate family, a fixed dimension, or a conjectured topology would not establish this conjunction. Neither strict finite inequality nor finite-$N$ optimizer classification is asserted.</p>
