<p>“Works” is the source's wording. The source defines its measure in Eq. <code>eq:Hada_measure</code>, <code>main.tex</code> lines 780–783. For a real sign matrix, write $G=CC^{\mathsf T}$ and $\mathfrak h(C)=\operatorname{Tr}(G^2)=\sum_{i,j}G_{ij}^2$; conjugate transpose and transpose coincide here. The source and its table are described in <a href="../Library/Eigenstructure/singhnechita2022evolution.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/22426">#22426</a> fixes the reading encoded by <code>claim</code>: for every odd natural $d$, there exists an integer $d\times d$ matrix $C$ with every entry equal to $1$ or $-1$, such that $\mathfrak h(C)=v_d$ and every integer sign matrix $B$ of that order satisfies $v_d\leq\mathfrak h(B)$. Here $v_d=d^3+d(d-1)$ is evaluated in the natural numbers, including subtraction, and then embedded in the integers. Thus attainment and the lower bound are both explicit; no infimum convention is used. The conjecture is refuted, using order nine.</p>
