<p>Here $\mathrm{Sym}<em>0(\mathbb R^n)$ consists of real symmetric matrices with zero diagonal (line 240). The effective coupling is $M=A\oslash J$, with $M</em>{ij}=A_{ij}/J_{ij}$ when $i\ne j$ and $J_{ij}\ne0$, and zero otherwise; the physical interpretation assumes $\operatorname{nz}(A)\subseteq\operatorname{nz}(J)$ (lines 250–263). The source's LP minimizes $T=\sum_m\lambda_m$ over $\lambda_m\ge0$ with</p>
<p>$M_{ij}=\sum_{m\in{-1,+1}^n,\ m_n=+1}\lambda_m m_i m_j\quad(i&lt;j)$.</p>
