<p>For every finite number t of parts with t at least two, and every positive integer part-size function n on Fin t, let N be the sum of the sizes, s the number of parts of size at least two and h the number of singleton parts. Vertices are pairs consisting of a part and a vertex in that part. The real squared-distance matrix delta has diagonal zero, same-part off-diagonal four and between-part one. Assume delta is singular and the sum of all its cofactors is nonzero. The latter is the sum of all adjugate entries, not a principal cofactor.</p>
<p>The functions phi, psi and theta, their single and double omissions, and all three entry cases of sourceL are exactly the author-defined omitted-list functions and equation (3.6). Empty products are one and empty sums zero. No expanded hatted-Psi display is substituted for the omitted-list definition.</p>
<p>The matrix sourceL is Hermitian. Its entire positive real characteristic-root multiset equals N-t copies of 1/4 together with h-1 copies of one, with algebraic multiplicity and no other positive roots. Its positive, zero and negative indices are N-s-1, one and s, respectively. These are a conjunction on the same actual matrix and domain. All finite part counts, repeated sizes and zero multiplicities are included; no additional matrix identity, genericity, classification or spectral-transfer premise is assumed.</p>
