article class="news-result" id="saied-marshall-anand-rieffel-2025-heralding-rate-monotonicity"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The ideal heralding rate of Fourier photon distillation decreases strictly to 1/4 from n = 5</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>J. Saied, J. Marshall, N. Anand and E. G. Rieffel, <em>General protocols for the efficient distillation of indistinguishable photons</em>, Phys. Rev. Applied 23, 034079 (2025), arXiv:2404.14217v4, distill indistinguishable photons with n-photon protocols built from an n × n unitary whose first row is constant (for example the discrete Fourier transform).</p>
