<p>G.f. A(x) such that the sum of the first n coefficients in A(x/n)^n equals 4^(n-1) for n &gt;= 1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Its FORMULA gives:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>(1) 4^(n-1) = Sum_{k=0..n-1} [x^k] A(x/n)^n for n &gt;= 1.
(2) (4*n)^(n-1) = [x^(n-1)] A(x)^n / (1 - n*x) for n &gt;= 1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The conjecture is:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjecture: for n &gt; 3, a(n) is odd iff n is of the form 2^k-1 or 2^k+1 (k &gt; 1).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The series is $A(X)=\sum_{n\geq0}a(n)X^n\in\mathbb Z[[X]]$, with
$a(0)=1$. Rational rescaling means coefficientwise mapping to
$\mathbb Q[[X]]$ followed by $X\mapsto X/m$. Powers are ordinary formal
products. There is no analytic convergence assumption.</p>
