<p>The paper defines <code>D_{q,k}(n)</code> as the number of distinct exact <code>k</code>-decks of
length-<code>n</code> words over a <code>q</code>-letter alphabet and defines
<code>E_q(k) = sum_{j=1}^k j L_q(j) - 1</code>, where <code>L_q(j)</code> is the number of actual
length-<code>j</code> Lyndon words over that alphabet. Preregistration issue #9512 records
this complete target, not one of the cases already proved in the source.</p>
<p>The formal target quantifies over an arbitrary finite linearly ordered type
<code>A</code>, assumes exactly <code>2 &lt;= Fintype.card A</code>, takes every natural <code>k</code> with
<code>1 &lt;= k</code>, and proves <code>Real.IsTheta</code> at <code>Filter.atTop</code> for the real-valued
cardinality of <code>exactKDeckImage A k n</code>. Its exponent is
<code>weightedLyndonExponent A k - 1</code>, with
<code>weightedLyndonExponent A k = sum_{i=0}^k i * actualLyndonCount A i</code> and
<code>actualLyndonCount A i</code> the cardinality of the subtype of actual Lyndon words
of length <code>i</code>. The zero term vanishes, so this is the source exponent. There is
no free proxy parameter and no extra hypothesis on <code>n</code> or on <code>k</code>.</p>
