<blockquote>
<p>Remark. The coprimality hypothesis is not merely a technicality in the present argument: it is what permits the product labeling to be viewed as a cyclic labeling. Proposition 3.7 does not prove closure under arbitrary weak products. Consequently, unrestricted closure of the equality class under the weak product has not been established. Whether such closure holds is a natural open question.</p>
