<p>The assertion is that any two finite simple graphs with positive size satisfying $\operatorname{FR}_{\min}(G)=E(G)/\sqrt{2s(G)}$ have a weak product satisfying the same equality. Definition 3.1 gives adjacency precisely when both coordinate pairs are adjacent. The Fourier transform has coefficient $1/N$, the numerator of $\operatorname{FR}$ is entrywise $\ell^1$, and the denominator is Frobenius; $E$ is the sum of the absolute adjacency eigenvalues.</p>
