<li><strong>The assertion.</strong> &quot;Under periodic boundary conditions, the conjecture is fully satisfied with no exceptions at all system sizes and across all three phases: topological, trivial, and crossing&quot; (§VI, p. 9), for half-filled ground states of the periodic Hamiltonian of Eq. (15) at w = 1.</li>
</ul>
<p>The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/QuantumBounds/khareletal2026pseudoentropy.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/17503">#17503</a> fixes the reading:</p>
<ul>
<li>The Fock space of the 2N modes (1,A), (1,B), …, (N,A), (N,B) carries the Jordan–Wigner annihilation operators in this order.</li>
<li>A half-filled ground state is a nonzero N-particle vector of minimal energy in the N-particle sector.</li>
<li>A is the first L unit cells, 1 ≤ L &lt; N, and Tr_B is the partial trace over the remaining modes.</li>
<li>The entropy of a matrix is −Σ λ log λ over its eigenvalues with multiplicity.</li>
<li>The assertion: for all such N, L, all v₁, v₂ in the same phase, and all such ground states, ∆S ≤ 0.</li>
</ul>
<p>The assertion is refuted in this reading.</p>
