<blockquote>
<p>Let Γ = G(ℤ_n, C) be an oriented circulant graph with n ≡ 2 (mod 4). If
zero transfer occurs between vertex v and 0, then v must be odd.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Issue #10142 fixes the readings: vertices are <code>ZMod n</code>; <code>U(t)</code> is the matrix
