<blockquote>
<p>Is f(n) = O(n)? Is f(n) = ⌈(n + 1)/2⌉ for every n?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Section 1 specifies:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a k-colouring of 2^[n] is a map χ : 2^[n] → [k], and a family ℱ ⊆ 2^[n] is monochromatic if χ is constant on ℱ. … it is a sublattice if it is closed under both union and intersection. … f(n) = min_χ max{|ℒ| : ℒ ⊆ 2^[n] is a monochromatic sublattice}, where the minimum is over all 2-colourings.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Sublattices here are nonempty. The Lean definition uses finite families of
subsets of <code>Fin n</code>, constant Bool colour, and closure under both union and
intersection. The extremal function is literally a minimum over all colourings
