sult-summary"><strong>Absolute Hermite coefficient modes: the complete A381524 difference assertion</strong><span class="result-excerpt">The smallest exponent of a largest absolute physicists Hermite coefficient changes by one or minus one.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Smallest exponent of x of maximal coefficient (ignoring signs) in Hermite polynomial of order n.</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>This is a Tier 1 explicit recent OEIS conjecture under the repository&#x27;s source classification, not an arXiv assertion or a difficulty measurement.</p><p><span>The idea</span>The proof uses the original physicistsHermite, signedCoeff and HermiteSignedMode.polynomialcoeff, whose original statement and proof are preserved with only the consumed extraction made public.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>The smallest exponent of a largest absolute physicists Hermite coefficient changes by one or minus one.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="oeis-a381524-hermite-absolute-differences"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Integer sequences (OEIS)</p><h3>Absolute Hermite coefficient modes: the complete A381524 difference assertion</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>OEIS A381524, revision 18, by Mike Sheppard (2025), defines:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Smallest exponent of x of maximal coefficient (ignoring signs) in Hermite polynomial of order n.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Its independently printed Comments assertion is:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjecture: Differences are either +1 or -1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The offset is zero. Let $H_n$ be the physicists Hermite polynomial represented
by the original <code>HermiteSignedMode.physicistsHermite</code>, and let $b(n)$ be the
least $j\in{0,\ldots,n}$ maximizing $|[x^j]H_n|$. The complete event is</p>
<p>$$
\begin{aligned}
\forall n\in\mathbb N,\quad &amp;b(n)\le n,\
&amp;\forall k\le n,\quad |[x^k]H_n|\le |[x^{b(n)}]H_n|,\
&amp;\forall k\le n,\quad |[x^k]H_n|=|[x^{b(n)}]H_n|\ \Longrightarrow\ b(n)\le k,\
&amp;b(n+1)-b(n)\in{1,-1}\quad\text{in }\mathbb Z.
\end{aligned}
$$</p>
<p>Both selector values are cast to integers before subtraction. Every natural
