lternating signed square matrices zumbrägel, generalising latin square orthogonality and frobenius-könig with alternating sign matrices, arxiv:2606.25884v1, section 8, printed p. 27: the total sum must be the same whether all entries are counted by rows or columns. signed row and column margins admit an alternating signed square matrix exactly when their total sums agree. let p,q count positive and negative row margins and p′,q′ the corresponding column margins.  released-dossier b7fb263563ea49b1e4d2346746c0d6e56bdb98678a724a004b583eaf84e84e26 "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Discrete structures</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Question resolved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>First preprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2026</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Equal totals characterize margins of alternating signed square matrices</strong><span class="result-excerpt">Signed row and column margins admit an alternating signed square matrix exactly when their total sums agree.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Zumbrägel, Generalising Latin square orthogonality and Frobenius-König with alternating sign matrices, arXiv:2606.25884v1, Section 8, printed p. 27:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The total sum must be the same whether all entries are counted by rows or columns.</p><p><span>The idea</span>Let p,q count positive and negative row margins and p′,q′ the corresponding column margins.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Signed row and column margins admit an alternating signed square matrix exactly when their total sums agree.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="ernst-lia-obrien-sheekey-zumbragel-2026-alternating-sign-margins"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Equal totals characterize margins of alternating signed square matrices</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>A. Ernst, S. Lia, C. O'Brien, J. Sheekey and J. Zumbrägel,
<em>Generalising Latin square orthogonality and Frobenius-König with alternating
