 remote-control dimension witness greater than four.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="lin-wang-liu-huang-2026-delayed-rcqc-dimension-witness"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Every data qubit of the delayed remote-controlled circuit violates the dimension witness S ≤ 4</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>P. Lin, D. Wang, Y. Liu and A. Huang, <em>Nonclassicality of a delayed remote-controlled quantum computing model</em>, arXiv:2606.31103v1, study a delayed 1-U-M remote-controlled quantum computing circuit (§III, Eq. (3), Fig. 3):</p>
<ul>
<li>a Bell pair on the program and remote-control qubits;</li>
<li>a controlled-A and a controlled-B gate on the data qubit, with A = diag(1, e^{i(β+δ)}) and B = [[0, −1], [e^{i(β−δ)}, 0]];</li>
<li>a Hadamard and a computational-basis measurement on the program qubit;</li>
<li>the remote measurements onto |P*_U⟩ = a₀*|0⟩ + a₁*|1⟩, with a₀ = e^{−i(β+δ)/2} cos(γ/2) and a₁ = e^{−i(β−δ)/2} sin(γ/2), whose β and δ must equal those of the gates.</li>
</ul>
<p>Read as a prepare-and-measure scenario with four preparations and two binary measurements, a violation of the dimension witness S = E₀₀ − E₀₁ − E₁₀ + E₁₁ − E₂₀ − E₂₁ + E₃₀ + E₃₁ ≤ 4 (Eq. (2)) rules out every classical causal explanation with preshared correlations. Simulated annealing found violations at all 900 points of a 30 × 30 grid of initial data qubits, and the authors write: &quot;It is reasonable to conjecture that for any arbitrary initial data qubit |d⟩, there exists a measurement on the data qubit and specific parameter values for β, δ, γ₀ and γ₁, such that, under an appropriate labeling strategy, violating the dimension witness S ≤ 4&quot;. The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/QuantumBounds/lin2026rcqc.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/16465">#16465</a> fixes the reading. For every unit data vector d there are β, δ, γ₀, γ₁ and a unit data-measurement vector b such that, with the source's labeling x = 2m + n:</p>
<ul>
<li>every preparation has positive probability;</li>
<li>S &gt; 4.</li>
</ul>
<p>It is proved.</p>
