reprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2026</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Comparability of conical-design concurrence bounds</strong><span class="result-excerpt">Conical two-design concurrence bounds have a uniform ratio ordering.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Fei, Estimating the concurrence for quantum states via symmetric measurements, arXiv:2606.31010v2, Section IV, after Theorem 2:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>It proves one ordering for all states for every pair of finite designs.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Conical two-design concurrence bounds have a uniform ratio ordering.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="wang-zhou-chen-fei-2026-conical-design-concurrence-comparability"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">arXiv</p><h3>Comparability of conical-design concurrence bounds</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>H.-F. Wang, W. Zhou, L. Chen and S.-M. Fei, <em>Estimating the concurrence
