<p>It appears tempting to conjecture that for every integer d ≥ 1, the ratio D^(d+1)(⟦−m, m⟧^d)/m^d has a limit when m tends to infinity. This is clear when d = 1, and it follows from Theorems 1 and 5 when d ∈ {2, 3}. However, this problem remains open when d ≥ 4.</p>
