Question 14 asks:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Describe the set of natural bases (up to permutation and scaling) of a
non-degenerate evolution algebra. When is it finite? Can it be infinite
for an algebra whose automorphism group is finite?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The endpoint is the entire final interrogative only. Its positive answer
