six-step recurrence quoted verbatim in
<code>Library/RecurrenceComposition/mathar2015a000159.md</code>. The source is
OEIS-only, with no DOI or arXiv identifier. Preregistration: #24301.</p>
<p>For $n&gt;0$, define</p>
<p>$$
U_n(t)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}\frac{2n}{2n-k}\binom{2n-k}{k}(n-k)!(t-1)^k,
\qquad U_0(t)=1,\qquad a(n)=[t^3]U_n(t).
$$</p>
<p>The A058087 triangle lists coefficients in descending order, so this is
A058087$(n,n-3)$ for $n\ge3$, exactly A000159. The conjecture asserts
$\sum_{j=0}^6 c_j(n)a(n-j)=0$ for every integer $n\ge9$, where</p>
<p>$$
\begin{aligned}
c_0(n)&amp;=2(-252307n+1041077),\
c_1(n)&amp;=504614n^2-3362985n+5118150,\
c_2(n)&amp;=1280831n^2-7397886n+6461565,\
c_3(n)&amp;=746598n^2-2913543n-1336090,\
c_4(n)&amp;=-405481n^2+6175011n-15469320,\
c_5(n)&amp;=-375862n^2+4098537n-8846430,\
c_6(n)&amp;=2(-187931n+560630).
\end{aligned}
$$</p>
<h3>Statement echo</h3>
<p>| Source clause | Formal counterpart and boundary |
| --- | --- |
| A058087's displayed finite rook sum | <code>U</code>, over rational polynomials, with the literal summand and summation range |
| Maple's explicit zero row | <code>U 0 = 1</code> is the zero branch of the definition |
| Descending coefficient order; A000159$(n)=$A058087$(n,n-3)$ | <code>a n</code> is the coefficient of degree three of <code>U n</code> |
| Mathar's seven terms and equality to zero | <code>claim</code> contains exactly these coefficients and shifts |
| Sequence offset three, with six backward shifts | The binder is a natural number with $9\le n$; every shifted argument is at least three |
| Universal conjecture | <code>result : claim</code>, with no additional hypothesis |</p>
<p>Rational division preserves the displayed source expression. In every
positive-row summand $k\le n$, hence $2n-k\ge n&gt;0$. Natural subtraction
therefore agrees with integer subtraction both in the sum and in the
recurrence. The definitions totalize $a$ below the source offset; the
settled statement only uses source-domain values.</p>
