integer-valued and defined by Bala's recurrence, extended to zero with
<code>a(0)=1=Lucas(5^0)=Lucas(1)</code>. This gives <code>a(1)=11=A144837(1)</code> and agrees
with the OEIS domain <code>n &gt;= 1</code>. Congruence means that the integer
<code>5^(n+r+1)</code> divides the integer difference <code>a(n+1)-a(n)</code>.</p>
<p>The exact Lean statement is:</p>
<pre><code class="language-lean">theorem result (n r : ℕ) (hr : r ≤ n) :
