n></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Gregory Gerard Wojnar&#x27;s OEIS A301420, NAME and COMMENTS, defines the sequence by:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The conjecture relates an unbounded monomial positivity filter to a rational formal series.</p><p><span>The idea</span>Multinomial expansion groups multiplicity vectors by their factor count.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Strict positive monomial coefficients give the rational shifted generating function and the positive-index recurrence for A301420.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="oeis-a301420-positive-newton-sums"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Integer sequences (OEIS)</p><h3>A301420: positive monomial coefficients for five data</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Gregory Gerard Wojnar's <a href="https://oeis.org/A301420">OEIS A301420</a>, NAME and COMMENTS, defines the sequence by:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>for a family of 5 data, the sum of the positive coefficients in these polynomials is a(n).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The FORMULA field states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>G.f.: (-x*(x+1)^4+1)/(x^6+4<em>x^5+5</em>x^4-5<em>x^2-6</em>x+1); this denominator equals (1-x)*(2-(x+1)^5) (conjectured).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It also states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a(n+14) = 7*a(n+13) - a(n+12) - 6*a(n+11) + 2*a(n+10) - a(n+9) + 4*a(n+8) + a(n+7) + 4*a(n+5) + 2*a(n+4) - a(n+3) - 5*a(n+2) - 4*a(n+1) - a(n) (conjectured).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The source snapshot is A301420 revision #28; the full generating-function conjecture occurs in revision #2 and the recurrence is explicitly conjectural in revision #16. The published offset is 1,2. The shift and the universal recurrence domain $n\ge1$ are explicit interpretations accepted in <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/23723">#23723</a>, rather than printed source quantifiers. The <a href="../Library/RecurrenceComposition/wojnar2018a301420.md">Library note</a> gives the source and coefficient normalization.</p>
<p>For $k\ge1$ and $m=(m_1,\ldots,m_5)\in\mathbb N_0^5$ of weighted degree $\sum_{i=1}^5 i m_i=k$, put $r=\sum_i m_i$ and define</p>
<p>$$
c_m=\frac{k}{5r}(-1)^{k+r}\frac{r!}{\prod_i m_i!}\prod_{i=1}^5\binom5i^{m_i},\qquad
a(k)=\sum_{\sum i m_i=k,\ c_m&gt;0}c_m.
$$</p>
<p>These are definitions, using equation (2) of Wojnar, Wojnar and Brin, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.08381v2">arXiv:1706.08381v2</a>, pp. 3–4. Each distinct monomial contributes separately, before substituting data values. No $a(0)$ is defined.</p>
<p>The exact target is the conjunction of the rational identity</p>
<p>$$
F(X)=\sum_{k\ge1}a(k)X^{k-1}
=\frac{1-X(1+X)^4}{(1-X)(2-(1+X)^5)}\quad\text{in }\mathbb Q[[X]]
$$</p>
<p>and the displayed recurrence for every integer $n\ge1$.</p>
