Section 3.3 immediately after Theorem 3.6, asks:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A natural question is whether $\mathcal{R}<em>{\mathcal{M}}(G)$ is maximally connected for every connected $G$, that is, whether $\kappa(\mathcal{R}</em>{\mathcal{M}}(G))=\delta(\mathcal{R}_{\mathcal{M}}(G))$ holds, where $\delta$ denotes minimum degree?</p>
