| Some original-host geodesic avoids the other selected vertices | <code>Visible</code> uses an existential <code>H.Walk</code> of length <code>H.dist</code>; shortest walks are paths |
| All feasible subsets, including empty | <code>Configuration H</code> is the subtype of all visible <code>Finset V</code> |
| Addition/removal and actual host-edge slides | The two disjuncts of <code>MixedMove</code>, used by <code>reconfiguration</code> |
| Standard vertex connectivity | <code>Separates</code> deletes to at most one vertex or to an induced graph that is not preconnected; <code>vertexConnectivity</code> minimizes cut size |
| Equality to minimum degree | <code>result : FullMaximalConnectivityClaim</code> |</p>
<p>The separator convention gives $\kappa(K_q)=q-1$ for every positive $q$;
<code>Connectivity.connectivity_complete</code> verifies this convention. No geodesic,
separator, sparse-slide, girth or diameter premise is added to the conclusion.</p>
