<p>%N A165719 Integers of the form k*(k+9)/8.
%C A165719 Only one term is a prime number (17). Are all others composite?
%F A165719 Conjecture: Valid k values are pairs of the form (8<em>m-1,8</em>m) for m=1,2,3.... If true, 17 is the only prime term. - <em>Bill McEachen</em>, May 06 2026
