<p>The published question is:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Are there terms with three distinct prime divisors?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The exact target is existence of a positive natural n with
<code>n.primeFactors.card = 3</code> and <code>f : Polynomial Int</code> such that, for every
<code>j &lt; n.divisors.card</code>, evaluation at the integer cast of j equals entry j
of the actual increasingly sorted finset of all positive divisors of n.
Both factor count and divisor list belong to this same n. The list has no
duplicates; the inputs start at zero. No minimum, degree bound, numerical
