<p>Let $\bar p(m)$ be the coefficient of $q^m$ in $\prod_{k\geq1}(1+q^k)/(1-q^k)$, and put $G(x)=\sum_{n\geq0}\bar p(n^2)x^n$. The settlement proves that every positive-degree coefficient $a(m)=[x^m]xG'(x)/G(x)$ is an integer, with $a(m)\equiv 2$ for odd $m$ and $a(m)\equiv0$ for even $m$, modulo four. Preregistration: <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/18874">#18874</a>.</p>
