<h3>Statement echo</h3>
<p>Over $\mathbb Q[[X]]$, set
$T_m=\lfloor m(m+1)/2\rfloor$,
$H(X)=\sum_{m\ge1}X^{T_m}/m!$ and $A(X)=\exp(H(X))$.
For every $n\in\mathbb N$, including zero, there is a $k\in\mathbb Z$ with
$(n!: \mathbb Q)[X^n]A=1+3(k:\mathbb Q)$.</p>
<p>The public definitions <code>triangular</code>, <code>H</code> and <code>A</code> retain the literal
exponent, coefficientwise positive-index rational sum and formal exponential
substitution. The denominator is $m!$, not $T_m!$.
The private <code>coeff_H</code> proves local finiteness using $m\le T_m$.
The public <code>innerIntegral</code> is the natural finite sum over $0\le m\le n$
of $(m+1)^{\overline{n-m}}$ when $0&lt;m$ and $T_m=n$, zero otherwise.
The private <code>factorial_ratio</code> and <code>eCoeff_H</code> derive its equality to
$n![X^n]H$. There is no assumed integer representation or finite cutoff.
The sole public theorem <code>result</code> is exactly the displayed all-index event.</p>
