9v1), Section 4, Example 1, state:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We have not found a proof of $M_{\alpha,\beta}^H(\rho)\geq M_{\alpha,\beta}^E(\rho)$ for any $\alpha\in (0,1)$, $\beta\in (0,1]$ and any qubit state $\rho$, however, numerical experiments shows that it might be true, and it seems difficult to find a counterexample. It is also conjectured that $M_{\alpha,\beta}^H(\rho)\geq M_{\alpha,\beta}^E(\rho)$ for any $\alpha\in (0,1)$, $\beta\in (0,1]$ and any quantum state $\rho$.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This quotation is from lines 573–579 of the downloaded v1 TeX, <code>20250301WuCF-imaginarity_monotone_R2.tex</code> (md5 <code>eb104c03d3638b12044677758c200bae</code>).</p>
<p>Fix the coordinate basis and let $\bar\rho$ mean entrywise complex conjugation, denoted $\rho^*$ in the paper. For density matrices, write</p>
<p>$D_{\alpha,\beta}(\rho\Vert\sigma)=\big[(\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{tr}(\rho^\alpha\sigma^{1-\alpha}))^\beta-1\big]/\big[(\alpha-1)\beta\big]$,</p>
<p>$M^H_{\alpha,\beta}(\rho)=D_{\alpha,\beta}(\rho\Vert\bar\rho)$, and</p>
<p>$M^E_{\alpha,\beta}(\rho)=\inf_{\sigma\in\mathcal F}D_{\alpha,\beta}(\rho\Vert\sigma)$,</p>
<p>where $\mathcal F$ consists of positive semidefinite matrices of trace one with real entries. Matrix powers are spectral powers from continuous functional calculus. These are the module's definitions; the source's Eqs. (7), (13) and (20) use the trace without an explicit real part, and Eq. (20) uses a minimum. The corresponding source definitions and locators are in <a href="../Library/Divergence/wuwu2025unifiedimaginarity.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/20971">#20971</a> fixes the formal reading: for every natural $d\ge1$, every density matrix $\rho\in M_d(\mathbb C)$, every $0&lt;\alpha&lt;1$ and every $0&lt;\beta\le1$, $M^E_{\alpha,\beta}(\rho)\le M^H_{\alpha,\beta}(\rho)$. Singular states are included. This infimum comparison is proved.</p>
