<p>The preceding example, lines 726–746, uses general generator eigenvalues, all nonzero, at physical dimension $d=D^2-D$ with bond dimension $D\ge3$. The question concerns the remaining four-level case. Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/23698">#23698</a> fixes its general-generator reading as follows.</p>
<p>For $D\in\mathbb N$, let $A:\mathrm{Fin},4\to\mathcal M_D(\mathbb C)$, let $W$ be a unitary $4\times4$ matrix, and let $\lambda:\mathrm{Fin},4\to\mathbb R$. Define</p>
<p>$$u(\varphi)=W\operatorname{diag}(e^{i\varphi\lambda_k})W^\dagger,\qquad
\Psi_N(w)=\operatorname{tr}(A_{w_0}\cdots A_{w_{N-1}}).$$</p>
<p><code>IsSymmetric</code> means that for every real $\varphi$ and every positive $N$ there is a real $\theta$, allowed to depend on both, with $u(\varphi)^{\otimes N}\Psi_N=e^{i\theta}\Psi_N$. <code>IsInjective</code> means that for some natural block length $n$ the map</p>
<p>$$\Gamma_n:X\longmapsto\bigl(w\longmapsto\operatorname{tr}(XA_{w_0}\cdots A_{w_{n-1}})\bigr)$$</p>
<p>is injective on $\mathcal M_D(\mathbb C)$. These are the trace-amplitude, symmetry and injectivity conventions of the source at lines 222–237, 134–140 and 267–276, respectively; <a href="../Library/StatisticalMechanics/sanzwolfperezgarciacirac2009mps.md">the literature note</a> records the locators.</p>
