and endpointeqbeatty proves its all-order golden beatty law. jacomaximumdegree.degreeformula counts the actual incoming and outgoing neighbor intervals. unresolved extensions: the result does not settle other graph parameters or other jaco defining functions. released-dossier d6e821bf1f99f7f50f43a644644f6c92b372fc8ec17d09442e46f5fdb28637e3 "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Analysis &amp; dynamics</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Question resolved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>First preprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2025</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Kok&#x27;s maximum degree and literal A319433 deletion</strong><span class="result-excerpt">The ordinary maximum degree of every positive-order recursive linear Jaco graph is its same-index literal Zeckendorf deletion.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Johan Kok, Integer sequences with conjectured relation with certain graph parameters of the family of linear Jaco graphs, arXiv:2507.16500v1, Section 2.2, Conjecture 2.2, states:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The theorem supplies a complete all-order resolution of the two clauses in Conjecture 2.2 for the source&#x27;s actual recursive graph and sequence indexing.</p><p><span>The idea</span>JacoEndpointBeatty.endpointrecurrence identifies the actual recursive endpoint array, and endpointeqbeatty proves its all-order golden Beatty law. JacoMaximumDegree.degreeformula counts the actual incoming and outgoing neighbor intervals.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>The ordinary maximum degree of every positive-order recursive linear Jaco graph is its same-index literal Zeckendorf deletion.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>Unresolved extensions: The result does not settle