<p>Definitions 4.1 and 4.3 (<code>unisto9.tex</code>, lines 606–612 and 623–627) specify the relations:</p>
<ul>
<li>Permutation matrices $P,Q$ are complementary if, for every $i,j,h,k$, the equalities $P_{ij}=P_{hk}=Q_{ik}=1$ imply $Q_{hj}=1$.</li>
<li>They are strongly complementary if they are complementary and, for every $i,j$, $P_{ij}=1$ implies $Q_{ij}=0$.</li>
