<p>Here $h(x)$ and $h(p)$ are the Shannon differential entropies of the quadrature distributions, and $\gamma$ has diagonal entries $\sigma_x^2,\sigma_p^2$ and symmetrized cross covariance $\sigma_{xp}$. These conventions are defined in Sections II.A–B, lines 108–117 and 155–166, and in <a href="../Library/Entropy/hertzjabbourcerf2017entropypower.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/26413">#26413</a> fixes the universal reading to be refuted in units $\hbar=1$. For every natural number $n$, take real families $w_i,\mu_{xi},\mu_{pi},a_i,b_i,c_i$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin},n$, with $w_i\ge0$, $\sum_iw_i=1$, $a_i&gt;0$, $c_i&gt;0$ and $\Delta_i=a_ic_i-b_i^2\ge1/4$. The definition <code>gaussianWigner</code> gives</p>
<p>$G_i(x,p)=\dfrac{1}{2\pi\sqrt{\Delta_i}}\exp!\left(-\dfrac{c_i(x-\mu_{xi})^2-2b_i(x-\mu_{xi})(p-\mu_{pi})+a_i(p-\mu_{pi})^2}{2\Delta_i}\right)$.</p>
<p>Let $W(x,p)=\sum_iw_iG_i(x,p)$, $W_x(x)=\int W(x,p),dp$, $W_p(p)=\int W(x,p),dx$, and $h(f)=-\int f\ln f$. The module defines the means as the phase-space integrals of $xW$ and $pW$, and $\gamma_{xx},\gamma_{pp},\gamma_{xp}$ as the integrals of $(x-\bar x)^2W$, $(p-\bar p)^2W$ and $(x-\bar x)(p-\bar p)W$, respectively. All integrals use Lebesgue volume.</p>
<p>The proposition <code>claim</code> asserts that, whenever $W_x\ln W_x$, $W_p\ln W_p$ and $(x^2+p^2)W$ are integrable,</p>
<p>$F(W):=h(W_x)+h(W_p)-\frac12\ln!\left(\dfrac{\gamma_{xx}\gamma_{pp}}{\gamma_{xx}\gamma_{pp}-\gamma_{xp}^2}\right)\ge\ln(\pi e)$.</p>
<p>Normalization excludes the empty mixture. Refuting this subclass of the source's all-state assertion suffices to refute its universal mixed-state reading; the source's conditional variational argument is not being represented as an unconditional proof.</p>
