284005</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>This dossier anchors exactly the November 10, 2019 FORMULA in
<a href="https://oeis.org/A284005">OEIS A284005</a>, attributed to Mikhail Kurkov:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjecture: a(n) = 2*a(f(n)) + Sum_{k=0..floor(log_2(n))-1} a(f(n) + 2^k*(1 - T(n,k))) for n &gt; 1 with a(0) = 1, a(1) = 2, f(n) = A053645(n), T(n,k) = floor(n/2^k) mod 2. - <em>Mikhail Kurkov</em>, Nov 10 2019</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The NAME defines <code>a(n)=(1+A000120(n))*a(floor(n/2))</code> for <code>n&gt;1</code>.
The initial data begins <code>1,2,4,6,8,12,18,24</code>, including <code>a(1)=2</code>.
Here <code>wt(n)=A000120(n)</code> is binary digit sum, <code>L=floor(log_2(n))</code>,
and removing the leading binary one gives <code>f(n)=n-2^L</code>.
All operations in the formal statement are natural-number operations.
Every index <code>0 &lt;= k &lt; L</code> occurs: an existing one bit contributes
<code>a(f(n))</code>, and these repeated contributions are retained.</p>
<p>The exact native result is:</p>
<pre><code class="language-lean">theorem result :
    a 0 = 1 ∧ a 1 = 2 ∧
    (∀ n : ℕ, 1 &lt; n → a n = (1 + wt n) * a (n / 2)) ∧
    (∀ n : ℕ, 1 &lt; n →
      a n = 2 * a (n - 2 ^ Nat.log 2 n) +
        ∑ k ∈ Finset.range (Nat.log 2 n),
          a (n - 2 ^ Nat.log 2 n + 2 ^ k * (1 - n / 2 ^ k % 2)))
</code></pre>
<p>This includes <code>n=2</code> and every power of two. The lower-bit identity
asserts nothing at zero or one. The April 24, 2023 two-parameter
binomial conjecture and the A329369 modulo-two binomial transform are
distinct questions. The divisor-count representation in the entry's
NAME is outside this result.</p>
