 states the following in the subsection “On the almost palindromicity”, conjecture labelled conj:palindromic-width-three, phases.tex, lines 8770–8779:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>Okada&#x27;s paper studies merged-log-concavity, unimodality and palindromicity of expressions constructed from Gaussian binomial coefficients, with applications to ideal boson-fermion gases.</p><p><span>The idea</span>These are the hypotheses of indexbounds, lowend, reverseddegreegap and highend below.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Almost strictly pre-fitting tuples of width at least three give pre-merged Gaussian determinants that are not almost palindromic.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="okada-2020-premerged-determinant-nonpalindromic"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Okada&#x27;s pre-merged Gaussian determinants of width at least three are not almost palindromic</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>So Okada, <em>Merged-log-concavity of rational functions, almost strictly unimodal sequences, and phase transitions of ideal boson-fermion gases</em>, arXiv:2003.02112v2 (2020 preprint, revised 2024), states the following in the subsection “On the almost palindromicity”, conjecture labelled <code>conj:palindromic-width-three</code>, <code>phases.tex</code>, lines 8770–8779:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Let $\mu\in\Z_{\geq 3}$. Then, $\dt(U)_{a}^{b}(\mu,\iota^{\mu}(1),\iota^{\mu}(1), 0, \iota^{\mu}(q))$ is not an almost palindromic $q$-polynomial, provided $\tp{\mu,a,b}$ is almost strictly pre-fitting.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The quotation retains the source macros: <code>\Z</code> denotes $\mathbb Z$, <code>\dt</code> denotes $\tilde d$, and <code>\tp</code> prints a tuple. The source defines almost strictly pre-fitting by $0\le a_1&lt;\cdots&lt;a_\mu\le b_1&lt;\cdots&lt;b_\mu$ (lines 8337–8346), and almost palindromic by equality of the coefficient list with its reverse after zero coefficients are omitted (Definition <code>def:almost</code>, lines 8503–8512).</p>
<p>At these parameters, the pre-merged determinant is the integer polynomial $P=A-B$, where $A=\prod_{i=1}^{\mu}{b_i\brack a_i}<em>q$ and $B=\prod</em>{i=1}^{\mu}{b_i\brack a_{\mu+1-i}}_q$. This specialization follows from the source's tuple Gaussian product (lines 3505–3519), unit base-shift factors (lines 5942–5955), and pre-parcel and pre-merged determinant definitions (lines 6005–6048). The scalar degree shift is zero.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/25498">#25498</a> fixes the reading: for every natural $\mu\ge3$ and every such pair of tuples, the nonzero coefficients of $P$, ordered by increasing degree, do not form a palindrome. This is proved.</p>
