:2101.11288, J. Math. Phys. 63, 012202, DOI 10.1063/5.0046581, Section IV, states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjecture 19. The sets Cd ∩ Ud and Cd² coincide for all d, i.e., for every circulant unistochastic matrix it is possible to find a corresponding circulant unitary matrix.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The universal assertion is <strong>Refuted</strong> at dimension ten. <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/16445">Preregistration #16445</a> fixes the source, quantifiers and Lean conventions. Definition 6 defines doubly circulant unistochastic matrices as those having a circulant unitary realization. The source quotations and locator are in <a href="../Library/QuantumBounds/rajchelkorzekwapuchalazyczkowski2021birkhoff.md">the existing Library note</a>.</p>
<h3>Statement echo</h3>
<p>| Source clause | Lean counterpart | Fidelity |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Every dimension $d$ | <code>claim</code> quantifies over natural $d$ | No restriction to even or positive dimensions in the assertion |
| Every circulant matrix $B$ | Every real <code>Matrix (Fin d) (Fin d)</code> with the reused <code>IsCirculant</code> | <code>Matrix.circulant</code> uses $v(i-j)$ with modular indices; the source's reversed convention describes the same class |
| Unistochastic $B$ | Reused <code>IsUnistochastic</code>, using <code>Matrix.unitaryGroup</code> and <code>RHLinalg.normSqMatrix</code> | Allows every complex unitary realization, including a real orthogonal one |
| A corresponding circulant unitary matrix | <code>HasCirculantLift</code> quantifies over a complex vector $z$, requires its circulant to be unitary, and requires entrywise squared norms to equal $B$ | The full source condition, with no certificate restriction |
| Equality of the two sets | <code>claim</code> gives the inclusion from circulant unistochastic matrices to matrices with a circulant unitary lift | The reverse inclusion follows from the source definitions |
| Refutation of the all-dimensional claim | <code>result</code> proves the literal negation of <code>claim</code> | One instance at $d=10$ suffices |</p>
<p>All binders and conjuncts implement these clauses. There is no additional hypothesis on $B$ or on a realizing unitary. <code>HasCirculantLift</code> mirrors Definition 6 verbatim: “The set of d × d doubly circulant unistochastic matrices Cd² consists of these circulant unistochastic matrices for which there exists the corresponding unitary matrix that is circulant.” <code>claim</code> mirrors the quoted Conjecture 19. The two other source predicates are reused from <code>CirculantBraceletNonUnistochastic</code>, without aliases.</p>
