<p>This quotation is from <code>Arxiv.tex</code>, line 482, in the arXiv v1 source archive (534 lines; md5 <code>cc2fa845c0b0f4155ed18dcb76e4c92e</code>). The source macros <code>\hS</code>, <code>\hA</code> and <code>\btn{k}</code> are expanded to $\mathcal S$, $\mathcal A$ and $1\mapsto k$; the wording is unchanged. The main-text conjecture is on line 348. The definitions and further quotations are in <a href="../Library/QuantumContext/jokinenetal2024nobroadcasting.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/21862">#21862</a> fixes the reading of generation: $\mathcal A$ is the real convex hull of the binary classical post-processings $\sum_o c_oM_j(o)$, with $0\le c_o\le1$, of $k$ finite POVMs. A subtheory has a convex set $\mathcal T$ of density matrices and a convex set $\mathcal A$ of effects, contains $I$ among its effects, and is closed under $E\mapsto I-E$. The conjectured equivalence is refuted by a qubit subtheory generated by one four-outcome POVM.</p>
