<p>The radius is taken for series (16) at the theorem's given $\mu$.
As the source states on printed p. 12, “Writing Rg &gt; 0 for the radius
of convergence in (16), we claim that the next conjecture is true.”
Mathlib's <code>FormalMultilinearSeries.ofScalars</code> represents its coefficient
sequence, and <code>FormalMultilinearSeries.radius</code> supplies the standard
extended nonnegative radius. For this scalar series the coefficient-map
norm is exactly the absolute value of the coefficient.</p>
<p>At the example, absolute summability at $x=3/2$ gives $3/2\le R_g$.
Thus $0&lt;93/100&lt;3/2\le R_g$, so the refutation holds strictly inside
the disk of convergence of (16). The same geometric comparison proves
summability of all four shifted series at $x=93/100$.</p>
