<p>Conjecture 4.9. Let $n\in\mathbb Z^+$ and let $F$ be a field with $p(F)&gt;n+1$, where $p(F)=p$ if the characteristic of $F$ is a prime $p$, and $p(F)=+\infty$ if the characteristic of $F$ is zero. Let $A$ be any finite subset of $F$ with $|A|\ge n+\delta_{n,3}$, where $\delta_{n,3}$ is 1 or 0 according as $n=3$ or not. Then, for the set $S(A):={\sum_{k=1}^n k a_k:a_1,\ldots,a_n\text{ are distinct elements of }A}$, we have $|S(A)|\ge\min{p(F),(|A|-n)n(n+1)/2+n(n^2-1)/6+1}$.</p>
