<p>The source is the TeX member <code>BT_Hyper.tex</code> from the <a href="https://arxiv.org/src/2012.07872v1">v1 source archive</a>, md5 <code>e001e89a911f72e1614de54e82230780</code>. Lines 409–416 define the same linear combination on entropies and subflows; the footnote at line 417 expressly includes ordinary 2-graphs among the geometries. The definitions and source locators are collected in <a href="../Library/Entropy/baoharper2020hypergraphs.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/22654">#22654</a> fixes the finite-graph reading. Let $X$ be any finite vertex set, $k$ any natural number, $b:\mathrm{Fin},k\hookrightarrow X$ an injective boundary labelling, and $c:X\times X\to\mathbb R$ a symmetric capacity function with $c(u,u)=0$ and $c(u,v)\ge0$. For each boundary region $I$:</p>
<ul>
<li>$S_I$ is the minimum of $\sum_{u\in W,,v\notin W}c(u,v)$ over cuts $W\subseteq X$ containing precisely the boundary vertices labelled by $I$.</li>
<li>A multiflow consists of real pair flows $f_{ij}$ and thread numbers $N_{ij}$, using $i&lt;j$ once for each unordered pair. Each such flow is antisymmetric on vertex pairs, has zero divergence away from $b(i),b(j)$, and has divergences $N_{ij}\ge0$ and $-N_{ij}$ at these two endpoints. On every ordered vertex pair, $\sum_{i&lt;j}|f_{ij}(u,v)|\le c(u,v)$.</li>
<li>$V_I$ sums $N_{ij}$ over unordered pairs with exactly one endpoint in $I$; a max multiflow is a multiflow satisfying $V_{{i}}=S_{{i}}$ for every boundary index $i$.</li>
<li>For arbitrary real coefficients $\alpha_I$, write $R(x)=\sum_I\alpha_Ix_I$.</li>
</ul>
<p>The assertion <code>claim</code> is that for every such choice of $X,k,c,b,\alpha$, if $R(V)\ge0$ for every multiflow and $R(V)\ne0$ for some multiflow, then $R(S)=R(V)$ for every max multiflow. The result is its negation.</p>
