<p>These are verbatim TeX excerpts; the labels refer to equation (1.9) and Theorem 1. The definitions and source locators are also recorded in <a href="../Library/StatisticalMechanics/chen2017movingparticle.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>For a finite vertex set $V$, let $c:V\times V\to\mathbb R$ be nonnegative and symmetric, with zero weights representing absent edges. A configuration is $\zeta\in{0,1}^V$, $\zeta^{xy}$ exchanges its occupations at $x,y$, and $\nabla_{xy}f(\zeta)=f(\zeta^{xy})-f(\zeta)$. Write $\nu_\alpha$ for the product Bernoulli measure of constant density $\alpha$, and put</p>
<p>$\mathcal E^{\rm el}(h)=\tfrac12\sum_{u\in V}\sum_{w\in V}c_{uw}(h(u)-h(w))^2$,</p>
<p>$\mathcal E^{\rm EX}<em>{\nu</em>\alpha}(f)=\tfrac14\sum_{u\in V}\sum_{w\in V}c_{uw}\nu_\alpha[(\nabla_{uw}f)^2]$,</p>
<p>$C(x,y)=\inf{\mathcal E^{\rm el}(h):h:V\to\mathbb R,\ h(x)=1,\ h(y)=0}$.</p>
<p>The factors remove ordered-pair double counting and retain the source's additional Dirichlet-energy factor $\tfrac12$ for exclusion. For positive $C(x,y)$, the source's effective resistance is $R_{\rm eff}(x,y)=1/C(x,y)$.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/24189">#24189</a> fixes the finite-graph reading: for every such $V,c$, every distinct $x,y\in V$, every $0&lt;\alpha&lt;1$ and every real $k$, if</p>
<p>$\tfrac12\nu_\alpha[(\nabla_{xy}f)^2]\le k\mathcal E^{\rm EX}<em>{\nu</em>\alpha}(f)$ for every $f:{0,1}^V\to\mathbb R$,</p>
<p>then $1\le kC(x,y)$. This is the proposition <code>claim</code> proved by <code>result</code>.</p>
