<p>The same line describes the numerical thresholds:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>In particular, we highlight that there seem to exist values $c_{\rm , CHSH}=0.5$ and $c_{\rm , F_3} = 0.66$, such that states with QSE centres' magnitudes greater than these values, can no longer lead to a violation of the $\rm CHSH$-inequality and the $\rm F_3$-inequality, respectively.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>For a positive semidefinite trace-one complex two-qubit matrix $\rho$, write $\boldsymbol a$, $\boldsymbol b$ for its Bloch vectors and $T_{ij}=\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{tr}[\rho(\sigma_i\otimes\sigma_j)]$. The module defines Bob's centre by</p>
<p>$\boldsymbol c_B=(\boldsymbol b-T^{\mathsf T}\boldsymbol a)/(1-|\boldsymbol a|^2)$ when $|\boldsymbol a|\ne1$, and $\boldsymbol c_B=\boldsymbol b$ when $|\boldsymbol a|=1$; put $c_B=|\boldsymbol c_B|$.</p>
<p>Its $\mathrm F_3(\rho)$ is the real supremum of</p>
<p>$\displaystyle \frac1{\sqrt3}\left|\sum_{i=1}^3\operatorname{tr}[\rho,((\boldsymbol\alpha^i\cdot\boldsymbol\sigma)\otimes(\boldsymbol\beta^i\cdot\boldsymbol\sigma))]\right|$</p>
<p>over real unit Alice directions $\boldsymbol\alpha^i$ and real orthonormal Bob frames $\boldsymbol\beta^i$. The absolute value here is the complex norm. The source's Eq. (CAC), lines 209–214, gives its optimized value as $\sqrt{s_1^2+s_2^2+s_3^2}$, where the $s_i$ are the singular values of $T$; the relationship to the frame formulation is discussed below. The source definitions and locator are in <a href="../Library/Entropy/ducuarasusaskrzypczyk2024hidden.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/26164">#26164</a> fixes the settlement as the conjunction of</p>
<p>$\displaystyle \mathrm F_3(\rho)\le\max{\sqrt{3(1-c_B)},1}$</p>
<p>for every positive semidefinite trace-one two-qubit matrix, and the existence, for every real $0\le t&lt;2/3$, of such a matrix with $c_B=t$ and $\mathrm F_3(\rho)&gt;1$. This conjunction is proved.</p>
