n</span>A qubit Pauli channel has output maximal coherence 3/4, while two copies on a Bell input give maximal coherence 225/272, contradicting Conjecture 1 of Lee, Baek, Park, Kim and Nha.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="lee-baek-park-kim-nha-2022-output-coherence-tensorization-refutation"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The output maximal coherence of channels is not tensorization-stable</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>J. Lee, K. Baek, J. Park, J. Kim and H. Nha, <em>Fundamental limits on concentrating and preserving tensorized quantum resources</em>, Phys. Rev. Research 4, 043070 (2022), arXiv:2104.12307, ask whether correlated inputs preserve more of a resource through parallel noisy channels than product inputs.</p>
