 Markov generator in its own right.</p><p><span>The idea</span>1. Witness. The four-state generator L = (1/256)[[−295, 25, 25, 281], [273, −303, 17, 17], [7, 263, −313, 7], [15, 15, 271, −305]].</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>An irreducible steady-state block of a four-state Markov generator is not similar to any real Markov generator, even by a complex change of basis.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="sa-ribeiro-prosen-bernard-2024-steady-state-block-refutation"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The steady-state block of a Markov generator with a commuting symmetry need not admit a Markov form</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>L. Sá, P. Ribeiro, T. Prosen and D. Bernard, <em>Symmetry Classes of Classical Stochastic Processes</em>, J. Stat. Phys. 192, 41 (2025), arXiv:2406.17955, classify the symmetries of Markov generators L, real matrices with nonnegative off-diagonal rates and zero column sums (Eqs. (2)–(4)).</p>
<p>A commuting symmetry U splits L into blocks, and the classification applies to each irreducible block that is itself a Markov generator. The authors write after Eq. (5): &quot;It is, however, natural to conjecture that the block containing the invariant measure of the Markov process (henceforth referred to as the steady-state block) can still be recast into Markov form.&quot; Appendix A proves this under the extra assumption (A3).</p>
<p>The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/StatisticalMechanics/saribeiroprosenbernard2024symmetryclasses.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/17999">#17999</a> fixes the reading. Take a Markov generator L, a commuting real orthogonal U, and a stationary probability p. Let the steady-state block be a whole eigenspace of U that contains p, with no further unitary symmetry. Then the restriction of L to it is similar to a Markov generator. This conjecture is refuted.</p>
