| Every dimension | <code>n : ℕ</code> in <code>claim</code> | No upper bound is imposed. |
| Real symmetric positive definite $P$ | <code>P : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ</code> and <code>P.PosDef</code> | Over the reals, Mathlib's Hermitian condition is symmetry. |
| Every real diagonal $D$ | <code>d : Fin n → ℝ</code> and <code>Matrix.diagonal d</code> | All real entries are allowed. |
| Spectrum of $PDP^{-1}$ is majorized by its diagonal | Final <code>Majorizes</code> expression in <code>claim</code> | The diagonal is the majorizing vector and <code>d</code> the majorized vector. |
| The unrestricted assertion is false | <code>result : ¬ claim</code> | One seven-dimensional instance refutes the universal statement. |</p>
<p>No positivity requirement on $D$ is added; the chosen witness also has positive diagonal entries. The source's small-dimension theorem retains its dimensional hypothesis.</p>
