<blockquote>
<p>We note that the configurational entropy Sc = S + (−SN) is a sum of a concave and a convex function. Therefore, one cannot directly apply majorization to Sc based on the already obtained results for S and SN. However, this does not rule our that Sc is also a concave function of the parameters {Ck}. Similar to the original Shepp-Olkin paper [22] we will here just investigate the cases M = 2 and M = 3. Based on these results, we conjecture that Sc({Ck}) is indeed Schur concave and majorization thus applies.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>For independent Bernoulli variables X₁,…,X_M with probabilities c₁,…,c_M, put N=Σk Xk, S(c)=Σk h(ck) and SN(c)=H(N). Natural logarithms and 0 log 0=0 are used. The claim is that F(c)=Sc(c)=S(c)−SN(c) is Schur concave on [0,1]^M for every natural M: if d has the same coordinate sum as c and every descending partial sum of d is no larger than the corresponding one of c, then F(c)≤F(d).</p>
