<p>The witness and candidate value are given at lines 111–115; the supplement, Section “Entanglement detection based on the CHSH quantity” (<code>AppCHSH</code>, lines 232–256), specifies two qubits, targets $X=\sigma_X$ and $Z=\sigma_Z$ on both sites, and a common inaccuracy bound $\varepsilon$. See <a href="../Library/QuadraticForms/morelliyamasakihubertavakoli2022imprecise.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>In the formal statement, each of $A_1,A_2,B_1,B_2$ is a complex $2\times2$ matrix satisfying <code>IsBinaryObservable</code>: it is Hermitian and $I-A$ and $I+A$ are positive semidefinite. <code>Admissible</code> additionally requires</p>
<p>$\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{Tr}(A_1X),\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{Tr}(A_2Z),\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{Tr}(B_1X),\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{Tr}(B_2Z)\ge 2-4\varepsilon$.</p>
<p><code>Separable</code> means membership in the real convex hull of $\sigma\otimes\tau$, where $\sigma,\tau$ are positive semidefinite complex $2\times2$ matrices with trace one. The witness is</p>
<p>$W(\rho;A_1,A_2,B_1,B_2)=\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{Tr}[\rho(A_1\otimes B_1+A_1\otimes B_2+A_2\otimes B_1-A_2\otimes B_2)]$.</p>
<p>Put $\varepsilon_0=\frac12-\frac1{2\sqrt2}$. The definition <code>separableValue</code> is the source's candidate:</p>
<ul>
<li>for $\varepsilon\le\varepsilon_0$, $V(\varepsilon)=4(1-2\varepsilon)\sqrt{\varepsilon(1-\varepsilon)}+\sqrt{2-16\varepsilon(1-\varepsilon)(1-2\varepsilon)^2}$;</li>
<li>for $\varepsilon&gt;\varepsilon_0$, $V(\varepsilon)=2$.</li>
</ul>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/22442">#22442</a> fixes the reading: for every $\varepsilon\in[0,1]$, $V(\varepsilon)$ is a greatest element of the set of witness values attained by separable states and admissible observables. This is <code>claim</code>, proved by <code>result : claim</code>. Greatestness includes both attainment and an upper bound on every value in that set.</p>
