<p>$t_{c,d}(x)=x^3-(cd^2+c^2+2cd+c+1)x^2-c(cd^3+3c^2d+cd^2+c^2+cd+c+3d+1)(d-1)x+(d^2+4d+1)c^3(d+1)(d-1)^3$.</p>
<p>The definitions and source context are in <a href="../Library/StatisticalMechanics/dukes2023permaspin.md">the literature note</a>. The module's <code>dukesCubic c d</code> is this polynomial, defined for all real $c,d$, and <code>largestRoot c d</code> is $\lambda^*(c,d)=\sup S_{c,d}$, where $S_{c,d}={x\in\mathbb R:t_{c,d}(x)=0}$.</p>
