d positive variance hypotheses.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Fifth central moment inequalities for probability laws bounded on one side.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="meer-weeks-2024-bounded-fifth-moment-limit"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The Meer–Weeks fifth-moment bounds for distributions bounded on one side</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>D. J. Meer and E. R. Weeks, <em>Bounded distributions place limits on skewness and larger moments</em>, PLOS ONE 19, e0297862 (2024), arXiv:2308.05006v2, subsection “Higher order generalized moments”, <code>plos_latex_template.tex</code>, lines 506–510:</p>
