an>The idea</span>The output-register cut is positive under partial transpose and has unit trace, hence contributes zero negativity.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Both classicalization gaps for tripartite negativity are unbounded with a qubit measured party.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="xu-imai-guhne-2022-classicalization-simultaneous-unboundedness"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Two unbounded classicalization gaps with a qubit</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Zhen-Peng Xu, Satoya Imai and Otfried Gühne, <em>Fate of multiparticle entanglement when one particle becomes classical</em>, arXiv:2206.12834v2, Phys. Rev. A 107, L040401, Section V.B, page 5:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Inspired by those two examples, an interesting question arises whether there exist entanglement measures E and states ρ_ABC such that both Δ_E(ρ_ABC) and Δ̃_E(ρ_ABC) − Δ_E(ρ_ABC) can be arbitrarily large in the sense that they are not limited by the size of C, even if C is only a qubit. We leave this question for further research.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The answer is <strong>Proved</strong> for the fixed tripartite negativity of Equation (4), with no dimension-dependent rescaling. The source and conventions are in <a href="../Library/QuantumContext/xuimaiguhne2023classicalization.md">the Library note</a>; <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/19638">#19638</a> is the preregistration.</p>
<h3>Statement echo</h3>
<p>| Source clause | Formal counterpart | Scope |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Equation (4), sum of three bipartite negativities | <code>tripartiteNegativity</code> | Partial transposes on C, A and B; positive negativity $(|\rho^{T_Y}|_1-1)/2$. |
| Equation (1), $\sum_i p_i\sigma_i\otimes\tau_i$ | <code>branch</code>, <code>classicalize</code> | Unnormalized branches $p_i\sigma_i=\operatorname{tr}_C(\rho m_i)$, including zero-probability outcomes. |
| Equation (2), minimum entanglement loss | <code>delta</code> | Infimum over every finite POVM and every finite register dimension; attainment is proved for the constructed family. |
| Equation (9), discard C and prepare its zero flag | <code>deltaTilde</code> | The prepared flag is the zero basis state of a qubit. |
