<p>Here the coefficient subscript includes the proof that $t\bmod m&lt;m$. Equal coefficients at distinct indices remain independently selectable; $\Sigma$ identifies only equal sum values. The first denominator exponent is one. <code>blockSums</code>, <code>sourceTerm</code> and <code>achievement</code> are these three definitions.</p>
<p>The closed proposition <code>claim</code> is the complete universal assertion</p>
<p>$$
\forall m&gt;0\ \forall k:\operatorname{Fin}(m)\to\mathbb N\ \forall n\in\mathbb N,\quad
\Bigl[(\forall i,\ k_i&gt;0)\land \operatorname{Antitone}(k)\land n&gt;1\land
