<p>These quotations were checked in <code>finite_graphs_and_configurations_of_points_v5.tex</code> from the <a href="https://arxiv.org/src/2508.13472v3">v3 source archive</a>, md5 <code>3c520a352e066a90cdcffb75a2ee568c</code>. See also <a href="../Library/QuadraticForms/malkoun2025finitegraphs.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/22163">#22163</a> fixes the reading: for every natural number $n$, every pair of equivalence relations $r_1,r_2$ on $\mathrm{Fin},n$, and every complex Hermitian positive semidefinite matrix $H$, the proposed inequality holds, with $P_j={\sigma:\forall i,\ r_j(\sigma(i),i)}$. The real-valued formulation uses $\prod_i\operatorname{Re}H_{ii}$. The universal assertion is refuted.</p>
