 after proposition v.4 of the pinned pdf. both branches of the binary quantum information-combining expression are equalities at renyi order three, in arbitrary finite dimensions including singular marginals. the proof reuses ghzmeasurebiseparablebound.isdensity, partialtracemutualinformation.partialtraceleft, partialtracemutualinformation.kroneckereqconjdiagonaleigenvalues, projectionprobabilityflow.tracehermitianproductreal, and rhlinalg.tracemulnonnegofpossemidef.  released-dossier a34111cb63651882f399d129e163f92396e7c10c113da2ed64655fba938336c9 "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Quantum information</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Question resolved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>First preprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2023</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Order-three Rényi information-combining equality</strong><span class="result-excerpt">Both branches of the binary quantum information-combining expression are equalities at Renyi order three, in arbitrary finite dimensions including singular marginals.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Tomamichel, “Chain Rules for Rényi Information Combining”, arXiv:2305.02589v1, Section V, Conjecture V.5, state:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>It provides the quantum, noncommuting counterpart of the classical order-three equality and the explicit expression anticipated in the remark after Proposition V.4 of the pinned PDF.</p><p><span>The idea</span>The proof reuses GHZMeasureBiseparableBound.IsDensity, PartialTraceMutualInformation.partialTraceLeft, PartialTraceMutualInformation.kroneckereqconjdiagonaleigenvalues, ProjectionProbabilityFlow.tracehermitianproductreal, and RHLinalg.tracemulnonnegofposSemidef.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Both branches of the binary quantum information-combining expression are equalities at Renyi order three, in arbitrary finite dimensions including singular marginals.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="hirche-guan-tomamichel-2023-renyi-order-three-equality"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Order-three Rényi information-combining equality</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>C. Hirche, X. Guan and M. Tomamichel, “Chain Rules for Rényi Information
Combining”, arXiv:2305.02589v1, Section V, Conjecture V.5, state:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For $\alpha\in[2,3]$ the same holds with $\geq$ exchanged by $\leq$ and
for $\alpha\in{2,3}$ the above holds with equality.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The settlement is the $\alpha=3$ equality clause for two independent,
equiprobable binary classical-quantum inputs. Each input has two
positive semidefinite, trace-one complex matrices in an arbitrary finite
dimension. Put $H_i=\widetilde H_3^\downarrow(X_i|B_i)<em>{\rho_i}$ and
$H</em>{\rm out}=\widetilde H_3^\downarrow(X_1+X_2|B_1B_2)_\tau$, with $X_2$
traced out of the CNOT state. Then</p>
<p>$$
\begin{aligned}
H_1+H_2\leq\log2&amp;\Longrightarrow
H_{\rm out}=h_3(h_3^{-1}(H_1)\ast h_3^{-1}(H_2)),\
\log2\leq H_1+H_2&amp;\Longrightarrow
H_{\rm out}=H_1+H_2-\log2+
h_3(h_3^{-1}(\log2-H_1)\ast h_3^{-1}(\log2-H_2)).
\end{aligned}
$$</p>
<p>Here $p\ast q=p(1-q)+(1-p)q$, and $h_3^{-1}$ is the inverse on probabilities
in $[0,1/2]$. Both guards hold at the common boundary. The binding matrix,
