<p>This is the verbatim text of <code>channel-quantum.tex</code>, line 354, in the <a href="https://arxiv.org/src/2209.10177v3">v3 source</a>, md5 <code>1478712c3cb6058c040039d9ae9978e6</code>. The source macros <code>\FA</code>, <code>\In</code>, <code>\A</code> and <code>\X</code> denote $\mathsf R$, $\mathbf I$, $\mathbb A$ and $\mathbb X$. The definitions and locators are also in <a href="../Library/QuantumContext/zjawinschmidhobansainz2023channel.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>The family has binary outcomes and settings, $a,x\in{0,1}$, and angles $\theta\in(0,\pi/2]$. Alice and Bob share $|\phi\rangle=(|00\rangle+|11\rangle)/\sqrt2$. Bob applies the controlled gate $|0\rangle\langle0|<em>B\otimes I+|1\rangle\langle1|<em>B\otimes U</em>\theta$, where $U</em>\theta$ has rows $(\cos(\theta/2),-\sin(\theta/2))$ and $(\sin(\theta/2),\cos(\theta/2))$. The construction traces out $B$, applies Alice's effect $M_{a|0}=(I+(-1)^a\sigma_z)/2$ or $M_{a|1}=(I+(-1)^a\sigma_x)/2$, and traces out $A$ (Eqs. <code>eq:CR</code> and <code>eq:CRfam</code>, TeX lines 316–333).</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/21490">#21490</a> fixes the reading: for every pair of angles in $(0,\pi/2]$, LOSR conversion between these literal assemblages is possible exactly when the source angle is at least the target angle. The conjecture is refuted.</p>
