<ul>
<li><strong>Slow-mode criterion.</strong> The Mpemba effect occurs iff the slow-mode coefficient |b_2| of the initial Gibbs state Π(β_in) has a maximum at some β_in ≠ β_b (p. 2).</li>
<li><strong>Three-level conditions.</strong> For three levels they derive the necessary condition (3) on the rates.</li>
<li><strong>Triplets.</strong> For N levels they apply (3) to every triplet of levels, keeping the original rates.</li>
<li><strong>The conjecture</strong> (p. 4): &quot;we conject that if for an N−level system, all its triplets violate conditions (3), then the N−level system does not experience the Mpemba effect.&quot;</li>
</ul>
<p>The follow-up arXiv:2609.09988v1 (§II) restates the conjecture as shown.</p>
<p>The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/StatisticalMechanics/avitanfactorgelbwaserklimovsky2026mpembatriplets.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/17871">#17871</a> fixes the reading:</p>
<ul>
<li>the slow-mode coefficient is ℓ·Π(β) for a left eigenvector ℓ of the slowest nonzero eigenvalue, assumed simple;</li>
<li>the effect is two initial temperatures on the same side of β_b, the farther one with the smaller |ℓ·Π(β)|. This implies the source's criterion.</li>
