pan>The exact weight-one and weight-two classes are given by classone and classtwo.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Two queries to a fixed four-address memory contain discrimination information beyond the plus count.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>The source&#x27;s optimal error exponent, the collective Helstrom optimum, and any claim for a different prior model remain open.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="bohac-2025-qram-count-statistic-insufficiency"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The plus-count statistic is insufficient for exact-weight discrimination</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>L. Bohac, <em>Bias-Class Discrimination of Universal QRAM Boolean Memories</em>, arXiv:2512.17503v1, asks in Remark 5.3, “Open question: do collective measurements help?” The source TeX <code>bias_class_discrimination.tex</code>, lines 454–457, states:</p>
