ction of the nonpositive quadratic-form tests closed.  released-dossier 26c8a1402b1bb8bd83a7c94ce75e328945849d18c425e6f45fd86a67b9e34b3b "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Quantum information</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Question resolved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>First preprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2026</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Local distinguishability at every boundary projection state</strong><span class="result-excerpt">Adjacent trace-one blockpositive sets are locally distinguishable at every boundary projection state.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Young-Hoon Kiem and Seung-Hyeok Kye, Local geometry for Schmidt number witnesses, arXiv:2608.14199v1, Section 5, states:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>This is an external named problem with no digestion atom.</p><p><span>The idea</span>Compactness of unit low-rank vectors makes the projection of the nonpositive quadratic-form tests closed.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Adjacent trace-one blockpositive sets are locally distinguishable at every boundary projection state.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="kiem-kye-2026-local-distinguishability"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Local distinguishability at every boundary projection state</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Young-Hoon Kiem and Seung-Hyeok Kye, <em>Local geometry for Schmidt number witnesses</em>, arXiv:2608.14199v1, Section 5, states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Nevertheless, we conjecture that the inclusion BP_ℓ ⊋ BP_{ℓ+1} is locally distinguishable around ϱ_{E⊥} for ℓ ≥ k, whenever ϱ_{E⊥} is on the boundary of the convex set BP_k.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>For a nonzero proper complex subspace $E\subset\mathbb C^m\otimes\mathbb C^n$, write $\rho=P_{E^\perp}/\dim E^\perp$. The result says that if $\rho\in\partial_H BP_k$, then every neighbourhood of $\rho$ meets $BP_\ell\setminus BP_{\ell+1}$ whenever $1\le k\le\ell&lt;\min(m,n)$. Here $H$ is the trace-one Hermitian affine space, and $BP_j$ tests nonnegativity against all vectors of Schmidt rank at most $j$.</p>
