<pre><code class="language-lean">open scoped ArithmeticFunction.sigma in
theorem result {p : ℕ} (hp : p.Prime) (hq : (σ 1 (p - 1)).Prime) :
    (∃ m : ℕ, p = 2 ^ 2 ^ m + 1) ∧
      (∃ r : ℕ, r.Prime ∧ σ 1 (p - 1) = 2 ^ r - 1)
</code></pre>
<p>Natural subtraction does not weaken this statement. <code>Nat.Prime.two_le</code>
gives <code>2 ≤ p</code>, and the proof separately rules out <code>p = 2</code> from
<code>σ 1 (2 - 1) = σ 1 1 = 1</code>, which is not prime.</p>
<p>Not claimed: item 1 is a finiteness statement about the resulting class of
