<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/22599">#22599</a> fixes the reading for two identical copies with the truncated number observable $L=\sum_{n=0}^{d-1}n|n\rangle\langle n|$. For every integer $d\ge3$, there is a positive semidefinite matrix $\rho$ of trace one with $[\rho,L]\ne0$, which is not an equal-amplitude pure state, such that for every unitary $V$ commuting with $L\otimes I+I\otimes L$,</p>
<p>$M^{(j)}\bigl(\operatorname{tr}_B[V(\rho\otimes\rho)V^\dagger]\bigr)\le M^{(j)}(\rho)\quad(1\le j\le d-1).$</p>
<p>Here $\rho^{(j)}$ retains the entries with row number minus column number equal to $j$, and $M^{(j)}(\rho)=|\rho^{(j)}|_1$. An equal-amplitude pure state means $|\psi\rangle\langle\psi|$ with $\psi_n=e^{i\theta_n}/\sqrt d$ for real phases $\theta_n$. This reading is proved. The source definitions and their locators are in <a href="../Library/Eigenstructure/strattonhsiehskrzypczyk2026concentration.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
