<p>The binding interpretation in <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/22706">#22706</a> is over every $x\in\mathbb C$. Put</p>
<p>$$S_n(x)=\exp((x+1)\log n)\sum_{k=0}^n\frac{(-1)^k}{n+k}\binom{x}{k}.$$</p>
<p>The logarithm is real for positive $n$. The entire source function satisfies $H(m+1)=m!$ and, away from positive integers,</p>
<p>$$H(y)=\frac{\psi(1-y/2)-\psi((1-y)/2)}{2\Gamma(1-y)}.$$</p>
<p>The assertion includes existence of such an entire function and convergence $S_n(x)\to H(x+1)$ for every such function and every complex parameter. No existence assumption is substituted for this conclusion.</p>
