span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Further frontiers</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Question resolved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>Posed in</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2026</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>The exact halting time of Wolfram machine 3626</strong><span class="result-excerpt">The signed Moebius and totient divisor sum counts every transition of the one-sided machine on every positive binary input.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Peter Bala, OEIS A393210, conjecture of September 11, 2026, revision 18:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>Operational execution is defined independently of the arithmetic formula.</p><p><span>The idea</span>A block of k zero bits followed by one and arbitrary higher cells admits a restoring trace.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>The signed Moebius and totient divisor sum counts every transition of the one-sided machine on every positive binary input.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="bala-machine3626-exact-halting-time"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Integer sequences (OEIS)</p><h3>The exact halting time of Wolfram machine 3626</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Peter Bala, OEIS A393210, conjecture of September 11, 2026, revision 18:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjecture: a(n) = Sum_{d | n} m(d)^2 * phi(d), where m(n) = Sum_{d | n} (-1)^(d+1) * moebius(d) = A069517(n) and phi(n) denotes Euler's totient function A000010(n). Cf. A296306.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The sequence has offset 1. The equivalent conjectural relation in A069517,
revision 31, is the same question, counted once. Here a(n) is the actual
number of transitions of the one-sided two-state two-symbol machine 3626
on every positive natural input n in binary. Its half-tape extends
infinitely leftward, blank zero beyond the most significant bit. The head
starts in state A at the right edge on the least significant bit. Its
rules are A0 → A0L, A1 → B1R, B0 → A1L, B1 → B0R. A simultaneous read,
write, state change and move counts as one transition. Moving right off
the edge terminates the run, and that final transition is counted.
Input zero is excluded. There is no time cap, tape bound or counter width.
Both divisor sums range over positive divisors; the signed Moebius
arithmetic is in the integers.</p>
