ia, K.-S. Chen, M.-E. Liu, T. Vértesi, N. Brunner and Y.-C. Liang, <em>Trading symmetry for Hilbert-space dimension in Bell-inequality violation</em>, arXiv:2601.02893v4; Quantum Science and Technology 11(3), 035003 (2026), conjecture following Eq. <code>Eq:symSATWAP</code>:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Our computation results show that for the symmetric inequalities of~\cref{Eq:symSATWAP}, the measurement of \cref{Eq:CGLMP-Opt}, in conjunction with a symmetric maximally entangled two-qudit state, indeed reproduces the maximal quantum violation~\cite{SAT+17} of $2(d-1)$ for $d\le 100$. Together with the fact~\cite{Sarkar:2021aa} that this maximal quantum violation self-tests a maximally entangled two-qudit state,  we know that the symmetric family of SATWAP inequalities, \cref{Eq:symSATWAP}, also cannot exhibit a trade-off for $d\le 100$. Moreover, we conjecture that this holds true for any higher $d$ as well.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This quotation is from line 532 of the downloaded v4 TeX member <code>SymmetricBIV-arXiv_v2.tex</code> (2736 lines, md5 <code>6116dc142244f252c16a835d291626cf</code>). The symmetric-strategy definition is at lines 285–297, the measurements at lines 488–497, and the correlators and symmetric SATWAP expression at lines 513–530. See also <a href="../Library/Fourier/hsuetal2026tradingsymmetry.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>The module uses computational indices $0,\ldots,d-1$ and real-exponent phases $\omega^t=e^{2\pi i t/d}$. Its measurement matrices are</p>
<p>$M_{a|0}=|a\rangle\langle a|$, $M_{a|1}=U|a\rangle\langle a|U^\dagger$, $U=TW$,</p>
<p>where $T=\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,\ldots,1)$ and $W_{ij}=1/[d\sin((i-j-1/2)\pi/d)]$. Both parties use this same measurement function. Module settings $0,1$ correspond respectively to settings $1,2$ in the source's symmetric SATWAP expression.</p>
<p>For a vector $\psi$, put $P_\psi(a,b|x,y)=\langle\psi|(M_{a|x}\otimes M_{b|y})|\psi\rangle$ and $C_{xy}^{(k)}=\sum_{a,b=0}^{d-1}\omega^{-k(a+b)}P_\psi(a,b|x,y)$. With $a_k=(1-i)\omega^{k/4}/2$, <code>satwapValue</code> is the complex-valued finite sum</p>
<p>$\tilde I_d(\psi)=\sum_{k=1}^{d-1}\left[\omega^{-2k}\left(a_k C_{00}^{(k)}+a_k^*C_{01}^{(k)}+a_k^*C_{10}^{(k)}\right)+\omega^{-3k}a_k C_{11}^{(k)}\right]$.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/22009">#22009</a> fixes the attainment statement: for every natural $d\ge2$, there exists $\psi\in\mathbb C^d\otimes\mathbb C^d$ with $|\psi|=1$, $S\psi=\psi$, $\operatorname{Tr}_B|\psi\rangle\langle\psi|=I/d$, and $\tilde I_d(\psi)=2(d-1)$. This is proved. The universal quantum upper bound and the self-testing statement used by the source to infer minimal dimension are separate literature inputs.</p>
