<p>The original definition is:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Irregular triangle, read by rows, where row n lists the coefficients of nonpositive powers of x in the doubly infinite series Sum_{k=-oo..oo} x^k * (1 - x^k)^(n+k) for n &gt;= 1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Thus, for every positive natural n, expand
<code>S_n(x)=Sum_{j in Z} x^j*(1-x^j)^(n+j)</code> formally at zero and let
<code>T(n,k)=[x^(-k)]S_n(x)</code>. The outer sum includes every integer j;
negative integer powers use Laurent-field inverses. The row includes its
constant coefficient at k=0 and its exact inclusive final index
<code>floor((n+1)/2)^2</code>. Coefficients and the weighted row sum are signed integers.
The literal Laurent realization uses rational coefficients and the exact
integer-to-rational coefficient bridge. The shared library note's claim
quotation concerns formula (2); the quoted formula (3) is the distinct target here.</p>
