<p>This quotation is from the downloaded v1 source <code>arxiv_v1.tex</code>, lines 1684–1685, md5 <code>abcdd29ea99d1c5adf0206c6b9a9d211</code>. The source macro <code>\ADset</code> denotes the amplitude-damping family; the coherent process is the subject of “it”. The arXiv abstract page supplies the arXiv-issued DOI in the front matter.</p>
<p>The source defines measure-and-prepare processes as a measurement consuming $N$ channel queries, followed by an outcome-dependent global $M$-qubit channel preparation (TeX lines 1094–1103). Its preparations need not be tensor powers of an estimated channel; that narrower class is introduced separately at lines 1105–1115.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/20683">#20683</a> fixes the target as impossibility of one such process reproducing $\mathcal E_\gamma^{\otimes N}$ for every $\gamma\in[0,1]$, at $N=M\geq1$. This is proved for finite outcome sets with the trace-pairing interpretation specified below. The compiled statement also allows every $N\geq0$ and every $M\geq1$ independently.</p>
<p>Precisely, the module defines the following objects:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>adChoi</code> is the unnormalized, reference-first Choi matrix $J_\gamma$ of the source's Kraus operators $A_0=\operatorname{diag}(1,\sqrt{1-\gamma})$ and $A_1=\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;\sqrt\gamma\0&amp;0\end{pmatrix}$ (source TeX lines 1538–1553). Its entry at $((r,o),(r',o'))$ is $\sum_{k=0}^1 A_k(o,r)\overline{A_k(o',r')}$.</li>
<li><code>D5.S3.Quantum.Recovery.ProductPrefixRigidity.productMap (H := fun _ =&gt; Fin 2 × Fin 2) (fun _ : Fin n =&gt; J_γ)</code> supplies the coordinate tensor power: for assignments $x,y:\operatorname{Fin}n\to\operatorname{Fin}2\times\operatorname{Fin}2$, its entry is $\prod_i J_\gamma(x_i,y_i)$. At $n=0$ this is the one-dimensional matrix with entry one.</li>
<li><code>IsChannelChoi</code> requires a preparation matrix to be positive semidefinite and to have reference marginal equal to the identity: $\sum_o K((r,o),(r',o))=\delta_{r,r'}$, where $r,r',o:\operatorname{Fin}M\to\operatorname{Fin}2$ and each pair denotes its sitewise assignment.</li>
<li><code>claim</code> says that, for every pair of natural numbers $N,M$ with $M\geq1$, there are no finite $L$, fixed complex matrices $T_\ell$ on the $N$-fold Choi space and fixed preparation matrices $K_\ell$ on the $M$-fold Choi space satisfying <code>IsChannelChoi</code>, such that for every $\gamma\in[0,1]$ the numbers $p_\ell(\gamma)=\operatorname{tr}(T_\ell J_\gamma^{\otimes N})$ are real and nonnegative, sum to one, and satisfy $\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}p_\ell(\gamma)K_\ell=J_\gamma^{\otimes M}$. The real nonnegative requirement is expressed using the complex order. No further positivity or tester constraints are imposed on $T_\ell$.</li>
</ul>
