ound for the uniform overlap of the least adjacency eigenspace.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="sarkis-prosniak-nigro-tkatchenko-2026-uniform-overlap-refutation"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>A 1225-vertex graph refutes the star bound on the minimal-energy uniform overlap of quantum batteries</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>M. Sarkis, O. A. Prośniak, S. Nigro and A. Tkatchenko, <em>Star Topology Optimizes the Charging Power of Quantum Batteries</em>, arXiv:2603.10853v1, study a battery of N fermionic cells coupled along a graph G.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Overlaps and mode energies.</strong> The adjacency matrix A has orthonormal eigenvectors u_k with eigenvalues ε_k and uniform overlaps w_k = (1ᵀu_k)² (Eq. (11)). With a local field h, the mode energies are E_k(h) = (N/M)ε_k + h (Eq. (14)).</li>
<li><strong>The charging power.</strong> It is a weighted mean of the w_k, and the authors single out w_min = Σ_{k′} w_{k′} over the modes of least energy.</li>
<li><strong>The star.</strong> It gives w_min(S) = N/2 − √(N − 1) (Eq. (23)).</li>
<li><strong>The conjecture.</strong> &quot;Conjecture 1 (Star optimality for the uniform overlap). Let G be a non-empty graph on N vertices. Its minimal energy uniform overlap w_min(G) is upper bounded by w_min(G) ≤ w_min(S) = N/2 − √(N − 1).&quot; The authors base it on an exhaustive check for N ≤ 7 and random samples.</li>
</ul>
<p>The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/GraphInvariants/sarkis2026starbattery.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/16578">#16578</a> fixes the reading.</p>
<ul>
<li>Because E_k(h) is increasing in ε_k, w_min(G) is the squared length of the projection of 1 onto the lowest adjacency eigenspace.</li>
<li>&quot;Non-empty&quot; means at least one edge.</li>
<li>The conjecture is refuted.</li>
