Australasian Journal of Combinatorics 92(2), 164–183, Conjecture 4.1, p. 180,
states:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If z is a nonzero degree root of a graph of order n with argument arg(z) ∈ (−π, π], then |z| ≤ (n − 1)^{|arg(z)/π|}.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Section 1 defines $D(G;x)=\sum_{v\in V(G)}x^{\deg(v)}$.
The arXiv version is <em>The Degree Polynomial</em>, arXiv:2505.04882v1.
The settled proposition is</p>
<p>$$
\forall n\ge1;\forall G\text{ simple on }\operatorname{Fin}(n);\forall z\in\mathbb C,
\quad z\ne0\land D(G;z)=0\Longrightarrow
|z|\le(n-1)^{|\arg z|/\pi}.
$$</p>
<h3>Statement echo</h3>
<p>| Source clause | Lean counterpart | Fidelity |
