| Nonzero degree root | Complex <code>z</code>, <code>z ≠ 0</code>, polynomial evaluation equal to zero | Both hypotheses retained |
| $\arg z\in(-\pi,\pi]$ | <code>Complex.arg z</code> | Pinned Mathlib branch convention |
| Modulus and power | Complex norm and real power | $\pi&gt;0$ gives $|\arg(z)/\pi|=|\arg z|/\pi$ |
| All nonzero roots | <code>result : claim</code> | Universal inequality; no extra root hypothesis |</p>
<p>The public definitions <code>degreePolynomial</code> and <code>claim</code> reproduce the two
preregistered expressions literally. Positive order is explicit: at order
zero the vertex sum is the zero polynomial, so a universal root bound
would have a different meaning.</p>
