<p>The label <code>eq:bound_r</code> is the inequality at <code>draft.tex</code> lines 776–779: for fixed rank-$k$ binary $R$, $\min_{Q',c}S_\alpha(p_{Q',c,R})\ge S_\alpha(q_R)$, stated there for integer $\alpha&gt;1$. The states indexed by the diagonal part of $Q$ and the translation $t$ give the squared-overlap law $p$; $q_R$ uses zero off-diagonal matrix and zero phase vector after replacing the amplitudes of $\psi$ by their absolute values. The definitions and source locators are in <a href="../Library/Entropy/tarabunga2025asymmetry.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/24993">#24993</a> fixes the reading at $k=N=n\ge1$ and $R=I_n$, where the translation quotient has one element. Write $B_n=\mathbb F_2^n$. For every unit vector $\psi:B_n\to\mathbb C$, strictly upper-triangular $Q'\in\mathbb F_2^{n\times n}$ and $c\in B_n$, define</p>
<p>$\phi_d(x)=2^{-n/2}(-1)^{x^\top(\operatorname{diag}d+Q')x}i^{\sum_j\widetilde c_j\widetilde x_j}$,</p>
<p>$p(d)=\left|\sum_{x\in B_n}\overline{\phi_d(x)}\psi(x)\right|^2$, and $q(d)=\left|\sum_{x\in B_n}2^{-n/2}(-1)^{d\cdot x}|\psi(x)|\right|^2$.</p>
<p>Here the quadratic and dot-product exponents of $-1$ are computed in $\mathbb F_2$ and represented by zero or one, whereas each tilde is the natural representative zero or one and the exponent of $i$ is summed in $\mathbb N$. Put $S_1(r)=-\sum_d r(d)\ln r(d)$, with $0\ln0=0$. The module's <code>claim</code> asserts $S_1(q)\le S_1(p)$ for every such $n,\psi,Q',c$, with the unit condition $\sum_x|\psi(x)|^2=1$. Its <code>result</code> proves the negation. This refutes a subcase of the source's Shannon conjecture.</p>
