<p>Corollary 2 states that for c &gt; 1/√2 and N = 2 or N ≥ 4 the bound (22), B(c) = min over θ ∈ [0, arccos c] of D(θ) + D(arccos c − θ), is c-optimal. That is, it equals the minimum of the entropy sum over all states and all unitary T ∈ U(N) with c(T) = max |T_ij| = c. The entropies, the overlap and the function D are quoted in <a href="../Library/QuantumContext/zozor2014entropylikeuncertainty.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/19610">#19610</a> fixes the reading for the Tsallis pair of order 2, S₂(p) = 1 − Σ p_i², an admissible pair of the corollary. The suspicion then says that, for every c with 1/√2 &lt; c ≤ 1, some T ∈ U(3) with c(T) = c and some state attain B(c). The suspicion is refuted.</p>
