<blockquote>
<p>Let Φ : M_n → M_k be a positive linear map between the algebras of matrices of size n and k and let F_n and F_k be the sets of non-expansive, positive operators in M_n and M_k respectively. Does Φ⁻¹(F_k) ⊂ F_n imply ‖f ∘ Φ(M)‖ ≤ ‖Φ ∘ f(M)‖ for all M ≥ 0, all symmetric norms and all non-negative concave functions on the positive half line?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The matrix algebras are over $\mathbb C$. Write $F_j={X:0\preceq X\preceq I_j}$. The inclusion means non-strict set inclusion, and the inverse image is taken in the entire domain algebra. A symmetric norm is invariant under left and right multiplication by unitaries. The preregistration is <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/18573">#18573</a>.</p>
