ons preserves their combined counts. gramfactor expresses this same matrix as seven rank-one positive semidefinite terms with the nonnegative weights gramWeight; statepsd proves positivity and statetrace proves trace one.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>A completely symmetric density matrix on three qutrits has no fully separable decomposition.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>Thus complete symmetry permits separable states as well as the entangled instance; a classification of the separable part remains open here. - Effect on the source.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="chen-chu-qian-shen-2019-multi-qutrit-completely-symmetric-separability"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Completely symmetric three-qutrit states need not be fully separable</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>L. Chen, D. Chu, L. Qian and Y. Shen, <em>Separability of completely symmetric states in a multipartite system</em>, Phys. Rev. A 99, 032312 (2019), arXiv:1812.04182v4, Conclusion, item 2 (v4 TeX, line 1857):</p>
