<p>The source's Definition 1 (TeX lines 360–391) requires invariance of matrix entries under every permutation of all $2d$ ket and bra index positions, including permutations mixing ket and bra. Its multipartite convention is explicit (lines 449–452):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>For simplicity, a separable state will indicate the fully separable one in the multipartite case.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/23788">#23788</a> fixes the assertion as follows. For every natural $d\ge3$, every positive semidefinite complex matrix $\rho$ of trace one on $(\mathbb C^3)^{\otimes d}$ that is completely symmetric is fully separable. Here full separability means a finite convex combination, with strictly positive real weights summing to one, of projectors onto products of unit local complex vectors. This assertion is <code>claim</code>; it is refuted.</p>
<p>The source definitions and locator are also recorded in <a href="../Library/Entropy/chenchuqianshen2019cs.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
