<p>The source assumes $0&lt;\eta&lt;1$, $\epsilon&lt;1-\eta$, initially $(Wx)_j&gt;\eta$ for every cell, and restricts to trajectories with distinct coordinates and no simultaneous firings (Section 4, lines 239–255). Exhaustiveness means that every three consecutive firing labels form a permutation of the three cells (line 68). The quoted belief extends the source's exclusion of a particular six-firing itinerary to every non-exhaustive periodic trajectory in this graph.</p>
