<p>COMMENTS conjecture line (verbatim; Robert G. Wilson v, Jul 22 2015):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjecture: if a(2n-1) is prime then a(2n) is composite and vice versa. And when a(2n-1) is composite, it is congruent to 0 (mod 6). - <em>Robert G. Wilson v</em>, Jul 22 2015</p>
