</blockquote>
<p>The first three pairs in the SEQUENCE lines are <code>(3, 8)</code>, <code>(7, 16)</code>, and
<code>(11, 18)</code>. The formal definitions use
<code>S(n) = ∑ p ∈ n.primeFactors, p</code> and the frozen repository definition
<code>squarefreeDeriv(n) = ∑ p ∈ n.primeFactors, n / p</code>, where the division is
natural-number division and is exact because each indexed prime divides <code>n</code>.
The predicate <code>IsPair(x, y)</code> means
<code>x &lt; y ∧ S(x) + S(y) = squarefreeDeriv(x) + squarefreeDeriv(y) ∧ S(x) ≠ S(y) ∧ S(y) ≠ squarefreeDeriv(y)</code>.
