ee-three-two-six"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The rank vector $(3_2,2_6)_7$ is realized by an extreme POVM</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>E. Haapasalo and J.-P. Pellonpää, <em>Effective methods for constructing extreme quantum observables</em>, arXiv:1809.09935v1 (J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 53, 245301 (2020)), define finite-outcome POVMs as tuples of positive operators summing to the identity and define extremality by the midpoint condition (source TeX <code>laatikkopaperi_v4.tex</code>, lines 139 and 148–152). They order rank vectors and omit rank-one outcomes (lines 219–222). Their low-dimensional discussion says:</p>
