<p>The formal question is whether there is an extreme POVM on $\mathbb C^7$ whose rank-at-least-two multiset is two 3s and six 2s. The module's <code>claim</code> states that every <code>n</code> and every family $M:\operatorname{Fin}(n)\to\operatorname{Matrix}(\operatorname{Fin}(7),\operatorname{Fin}(7),\mathbb C)$ satisfying <code>IsPOVM M</code> and <code>IsExtreme M</code> has <code>bigRanks M</code> different from ${3,3,2,2,2,2,2,2}$. The declaration <code>result</code> has type $\lnot\claim$.</p>
