Continue in this fashion until all qubits are measured.</p>
<p>If $ 0 $ has been measured on every qudit, apply a Hadamard gate to every qudit.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Write $p$ for the source's prime dimension $d$, and $V=\mathbb F_p^n$, represented by <code>Fin n → ZMod p</code>. An affine partition (<code>isAffinePartition</code>) is a finite set of nonempty affine subspaces, with distinct parts disjoint, such that a vector belongs to a part if and only if it is nonzero. Its objective is <code>sqSum</code>, namely $\sum_{K\in\mathcal K}|K|^2$.</p>
<p>The cells $K_{i,x}={v\in V:(\forall j&lt;i,\ v_j=0),\ v_i=x}$, for $0\le i&lt;n$ and $x\in\mathbb F_p\setminus{0}$, form <code>flagPartition p n</code>. Put $S_p(n)=\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}(p-1)p^{2k}$, the definition <code>flagValue p n</code>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/25329">#25329</a> fixes the reading: for every prime $p$ and every $n\in\mathbb N$, the flag family is an affine partition, its objective equals $S_p(n)$, and every affine partition of $V\setminus{0}$ has objective at most $S_p(n)$. This is the proposition <code>claim</code>, proved by <code>result</code>.</p>
