a eckardt, on the number of bose-selected modes in driven-dissipative ideal bose gases, phys. the source distinguishes a few macroscopically occupied modes from an extensive selected set. two cubic product-coupled baths admit an open set with five bose-selected modes. for each pair of indices, asymcontinuouson proves continuity of the cubic matrix entry on this domain; the positive sums of the coupling coordinates supply the nonzero denominators. the settlement makes no claim about the source&#x27;s continuum-rate or driven-rotor results. released-dossier 8545a03fbffe02eb85b1c19f7ce00aef56118e11bcf7cb7be29462170caf7556 "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Analysis &amp; dynamics</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Counterexample found</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>First preprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2018</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>The expected two-bath Bose-selection bound is refuted for cubic spectra</strong><span class="result-excerpt">Two cubic product-coupled baths admit an open set with five Bose-selected modes.</span></span><span class="result-outcome refuted">Refuted</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Eckardt, On the number of Bose-selected modes in driven-dissipative ideal Bose gases, Phys.</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The source distinguishes a few macroscopically occupied modes from an extensive selected set.</p><p><span>The idea</span>For each pair of indices, asymcontinuousOn proves continuity of the cubic matrix entry on this domain; the positive sums of the coupling coordinates supply the nonzero denominators.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Two cubic product-coupled baths admit an open set with five Bose-selected modes.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>The settlement makes no claim about the source&#x27;s continuum-rate or driven-rotor results.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="schnell-ketzmerick-eckardt-2018-bose-selection-cubic-refutation"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The expected two-bath Bose-selection bound is refuted for cubic spectra</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>A. Schnell, R. Ketzmerick and A. Eckardt, <em>On the number of Bose-selected modes in driven-dissipative ideal Bose gases</em>, Phys. Rev. E 97, 032136 (2018), DOI 10.1103/PhysRevE.97.032136, arXiv:1802.04088v2, section “Rates with product structure”, <code>main.tex</code> lines 1173–1178 (TeX macros expanded and mathematical delimiters normalized):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We expect that there is a generalization of the above arguement also to non-ohmic systems described by arbitrary spectral densities. We have checked functions of the form (remember that $J$ must be odd) $J(\varepsilon)\propto\vert\varepsilon\vert^d\mathrm{sgn}(\varepsilon)$ with some power $d$ (not necessarily integer) and similarly observe $M_S\leq2M_B-1$.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Here $M_B$ is the number of baths and $M_S=|S|$ the number of selected modes. The two-bath matrix in <code>main.tex</code> lines 1062–1083 uses opposite bath spectra and projector couplings, with weights $f_i=|\langle i|f\rangle|^2$ and $g_i=|\langle i|g\rangle|^2$. The selection condition is Eq. <code>MS-problem</code>, lines 374–382. These definitions are also recorded in <a href="../Library/StatisticalMechanics/schnellketzmerickeckardt2018bose.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/25984">#25984</a> fixes a generic reading for $M_B=2$. For $m\in\mathbb N$, take unrestricted real energies $\varepsilon$ and coordinatewise positive real vectors $F,G$, and put $f_i=F_i/\sum_jF_j$, $g_i=G_i/\sum_jG_j$. The module's <code>asym</code> is
$A_{ij}=J_d(\varepsilon_j-\varepsilon_i)(f_if_j-g_ig_j)$,
where <code>spow</code> defines $J_d(0)=0$ and $J_d(x)=x|x|^{d-1}$ for $x\ne0$.</p>
<p><code>IsSelected A S w</code> means that, for every index $i$, membership in $S$ implies $w_i&gt;0$ and $(Aw)<em>i=0$, while nonmembership implies $w_i=0$ and $(Aw)<em>i&lt;0$. Write $V</em>{d,m}$ for <code>violating d m</code>: the parameter triples $(\varepsilon,F,G)$ with $F,G&gt;0$ admitting such $S,w$ with $|S|\ge4$. The proposition <code>claim</code> says that for every real $d&gt;0$ and every natural $m$, $\operatorname{int}(V</em>{d,m})=\varnothing$ in the full real parameter space $\mathbb R^{3m}$. This generic reading is weaker than an unconditional three-mode ceiling; it is refuted.</p>
