li noise and quantum central limit theorem for quantum bernoulli noise, advances in mathematical physics 2018, article 2507265, doi 10.1155/2018/2507265, section 6, “conclusion remarks,” published pdf p. 8: the question asks whether the classical diffusive gaussian limit persists throughout the infinite-dimensional coin space. every unit localized quantum bernoulli noise state has the standard gaussian scaling limit. the definitions annihilation, creation, r, l and walk implement the operators and recursion above. the spectral-measure identification itself is not a formalized statement of result. - neighbouring questions. released-dossier cd3dea6672a505b2312880bfb9cbf0dca129dcee55b05de8091f9efca0c2f03b "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Quantum information</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Question resolved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>Source</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2018</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Every localized quantum Bernoulli noise walk has the standard Gaussian limit</strong><span class="result-excerpt">Every unit localized quantum Bernoulli noise state has the standard Gaussian scaling limit.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Ren, Quantum Walk in Terms of Quantum Bernoulli Noise and Quantum Central Limit Theorem for Quantum Bernoulli Noise, Advances in Mathematical Physics 2018, Article 2507265, DOI 10.1155/2018/2507265, Section 6, “Conclusion Remarks,” published PDF p. 8:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The question asks whether the classical diffusive Gaussian limit persists throughout the infinite-dimensional coin space.</p><p><span>The idea</span>The definitions annihilation, creation, R, L and walk implement the operators and recursion above.</p><p><span>O