gh intersection of the three-state lower bounds gives zero.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>A general sufficient compatibility criterion, or a characterization of the larger graphs and data for which interval propagation is exact, remains open here. - Effect on the paper.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="galvao-brod-2020-overlap-interval-propagation"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Three-state overlap interval propagation is not always optimal</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>E. F. Galvão and D. J. Brod, <em>Quantum and classical bounds for two-state overlaps</em>, Phys. Rev. A 101, 062110 (2020), arXiv:1902.11039v3, Section II.B, <code>overlap_pra_v3.tex</code>, line 165:</p>
