<p>A bistochastic real n × n matrix P is d-orthostochastic when P_rc = ‖V_rc‖² for vectors V_rc ∈ ℝ^d satisfying the source's equations (1) and (2): column orthogonality, Σ_r ⟨V_rj, V_rk⟩ = δ_jk, and row orthogonality, Σ_c ⟨V_jc, V_kc⟩ = δ_jk. The definitions are quoted in <a href="../Library/QuantumContext/gutkin2013orthostochastic.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/19782">#19782</a> fixes the reading:</p>
