</div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The Liu–DeBrota fewer-effects construction does not minimize orthogonality</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Y. Liu and J. B. DeBrota, <em>Relating measurement disturbance, information and orthogonality</em>, arXiv:2105.02074v2 (Phys. Rev. A 104, 052216, 2021), Appendix C, subsection “Fewer effects”, Conjecture 2 (<code>apssamp.tex</code>, lines 795–797):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The above constructed POVM has
minimal orthogonality $O$ among POVMs having $n(n&lt;d)$ nonvanishing effects.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>For a POVM $F=(F_i)<em>{i=1}^n$ on $\mathbb C^d$, Section IV (<code>apssamp.tex</code>, lines 403–420) defines $S(F)</em>{ij}=\operatorname{tr}(\sqrt{F_i}\sqrt{F_j})$ and $O(F)=|S(F)-I_n|<em>F^2$. The square roots are the positive semidefinite square roots. Equivalently, $O(F)=\sum</em>{i,j}|S(F)<em>{ij}-\delta</em>{ij}|^2$.</p>
<p>For natural numbers $0&lt;n&lt;d$, write $d=an+b$, where $a=\lfloor d/n\rfloor$ and $0\le b&lt;n$. The proposed construction $E^{(n,d)}$ consists of diagonal coordinate projectors on consecutive disjoint blocks: the first $n-1$ blocks have size $a$, and the last has size $a+b$. Its Gram matrix is $\operatorname{diag}(a,\ldots,a,a+b)$, as displayed in Appendix C (<code>apssamp.tex</code>, lines 765–778).</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/25254">#25254</a> fixes the formal reading: for every $n,d\in\mathbb N$ with $0&lt;n&lt;d$ and every family of nonzero positive semidefinite complex $d\times d$ matrices $F_i$ satisfying $\sum_iF_i=I_d$, one has $O(E^{(n,d)})\le O(F)$. This universal assertion is refuted.</p>
