<p>The success probability p^coh_s(N⁰, N¹) is the supremum of Eq. (17) over the prover's strategies (Eq. (18)), and 1/2 ≤ p^coh_s ≤ 1 (Proposition 2). Section VI asks: &quot;An intriguing open question is to determine if p^coh_s − 1/2 is a metric on quantum channels.&quot; The incoherent analogue p^inc_s − 1/2 is a metric: by Eq. (8) it is half the normalized diamond distance (1/2)‖N⁰ − N¹‖_⋄.</p>
