<p>$\sigma_P=P\lvert+\rangle\langle+\rvert+(1-P)\lvert-\rangle\langle-\rvert$,</p>
<p>with the same $P\in[0,1]$. Put $\rho_G(P)=U_G\sigma_P^{\otimes(n_A+n_B)}U_G^\dagger$, where $U_G$ is the product of controlled-Z gates over the edges. Writing $\rho_A=\operatorname{Tr}_B\rho_G(P)$ and $\rho_B=\operatorname{Tr}_A\rho_G(P)$, define</p>
<p>$\mathcal I_A=H(\rho_A)-H(\rho_G(P))$, $\mathcal I_B=H(\rho_B)-H(\rho_G(P))$,</p>
<p>where $H$ is base-two von Neumann entropy. The module's <code>claim</code> asserts $\mathcal I_B\le\mathcal I_A$ for every such pair of sizes, every such graph with decidable adjacency, and every such $P$. Edges within either part are allowed. This non-strict assertion is refuted.</p>
