 Papamikos, <em>Entwining Yang–Baxter maps over Grassmann algebras</em>, Physica D 472, 134469 (2025), arXiv:2311.18673v1, construct birational entwining Yang–Baxter maps R_{a,b}, S_{a,b}, T_{a,b} with variables in the Grassmann algebra Γ(n) (Eqs. (17)–(19)).</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>The map.</strong> S_{a,b} (Eq. (18)) sends (x₁, x₂, χ₁, χ₂, y₁, y₂, ψ₁, ψ₂), with x, y even and χ, ψ odd, to u₁ = y₁²(1 + χ₁ψ₂)/(b x₁) + y₁(y₂ − a − ψ₁ψ₂)/b, u₂ = b/y₁, v₁ = x₁, v₂ = a + x₁x₂ − y₁/x₁ + χ₁χ₂, ξ₁ = ψ₁ − (y₁/x₁)χ₁, ξ₂ = ψ₂, η₁ = χ₁, η₂ = χ₂ + (y₁/x₁)ψ₂. Expanding every variable in a basis of Γ(n) gives a map on 2^{n+2} commutative coordinates.</li>
<li><strong>Measure preservation.</strong> A map preserves the measure m when its Jacobian determinant is J = m(z)/m(S(z)) (§4). The authors verify m = 1/y₁ for n = 1 and m = 1/y₁₁² for n = 2.</li>
<li><strong>The conjecture.</strong> &quot;We conjecture that in Γ(n) the map R_{a,b} is volume preserving for every n, while the maps S_{a,b} and T_{a,b} preserve measures of the form y₁₁^{−n} and x₁₁^{−n}, respectively&quot;.</li>
</ul>
<p>The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/StatisticalMechanics/adamopoulou2025entwininggrassmann.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
