<li><strong>The conjecture.</strong> From exact values of L_D for dimensions up to 5 (Table XII), Conjecture III.4 states &quot;L_(d₁,d₂,d₃) = Σ_{i=1}^{3} d_i − 2 for min(d₁, d₂, d₃) ≥ 3&quot;, together with two clauses for d₁ = 2.</li>
</ul>
<p>The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/QuantumBounds/buniy2024maximallyentangledclasses.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/16992">#16992</a> fixes the reading: the lower-bound half of the third clause, i.e. every v ∈ C_D has L(v) ≥ d₁ + d₂ + d₃ − 2 when all d_i ≥ 3. Refuting it refutes the conjecture. It is refuted at D = (3, 3, 7).</p>
