<p>COMMENT (Peter Bala, Jun 01 2022):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Conjecture: Let p be prime. The sequence obtained by reducing a(n) modulo p for n &gt;= 1 is purely periodic with period p - 1. For example, modulo 7 the sequence becomes [1, 1, 6, 1, 0, 4, 1, 1, 6, 1, 0, 4, 1, 1, 6, 1, 0, 4 ...], with an apparent period of 6.</p>
