ction li, quantumness and dequantumness power of quantum channels, entropy 24(8), 1146 (2022), doi 10.3390/e24081146, section 3, page 5 of the publisher pdf, in the paragraph following the amplitude-damping calculation: a strict separation means that an input with slightly less quantumness can lose more quantumness under the same channel. a translated qubit contraction has strictly greater unrestricted two-state dequantumness power than its restriction to maximally quantum inputs. their hermitian, idempotent and trace-one certificates satisfy all hypotheses of projectiondensity.  released-dossier 28639b3076893b1e66ba1d5ca86672fb5453d84668b4190877ffbc6c81fb2a6f "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Quantum information</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Counterexample found</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>Source</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2022</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Unrestricted two-state dequantumness power can exceed its maximal-quantumness restriction</strong><span class="result-excerpt">A translated qubit contraction has strictly greater unrestricted two-state dequantumness power than its restriction to maximally quantum inputs.</span></span><span class="result-outcome refuted">Refuted</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Li, Quantumness and Dequantumness Power of Quantum Channels, Entropy 24(8), 1146 (2022), DOI 10.3390/e24081146, Section 3, page 5 of the publisher PDF, in the paragraph following the amplitude-damping calculation:</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>A strict separation means that an input with slightly less quantumness can lose more quantumness under the same channel.</p><p><span>The idea</span>Their Hermitian, idempotent and trace-one certificates satisfy all hypotheses of projectiondensity.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>A translated qubit contraction has strictly greater unrestricted two-state dequantumness power than its restriction to maximally quantum inputs.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="song-li-2022-dequantumness-power-strict-gap"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Unrestricted two-state dequantumness power can exceed its maximal-quantumness restriction</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>H. Song and N. Li, <em>Quantumness and Dequantumness Power of Quantum Channels</em>, Entropy 24(8), 1146 (2022), DOI <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/e24081146">10.3390/e24081146</a>, Section 3, page 5 of the <a href="https://mdpi-res.com/d_attachment/entropy/entropy-24-01146/article_deploy/entropy-24-01146.pdf">publisher PDF</a>, in the paragraph following the amplitude-damping calculation:</p>
