us refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The optimized GHZ witness bound need not equal the geometric GME measure</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>X.-Y. Xu, Q. Zhou, S. Zhao, S.-M. Hu, L. Li, N.-L. Liu and K. Chen, <em>A generic framework for genuine multipartite entanglement detection</em>, arXiv:2211.05563v1; published as <em>General framework for genuine multipartite entanglement detection</em>, Phys. Rev. A 107 (2023) 052405, DOI 10.1103/PhysRevA.107.052405. In the arXiv TeX member <code>GMEwitness.tex</code>, subsection “Estimating entanglement measures”, line 325, they ask:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It remains open whether $\epsilon_o^{n,d}(p)$ equals $E_G(\rho_{n,d}(p))$.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The definitions are at lines 284–311:</p>
<ul>
<li>$|GHZ_n^d\rangle=d^{-1/2}\sum_{i=0}^{d-1}|i\rangle^{\otimes n}$ and $\rho_{n,d}(p)=pI/d^n+(1-p)|GHZ_n^d\rangle\langle GHZ_n^d|$.</li>
<li>$E_G(\psi)=1-\sup_{\phi\text{ biseparable}}|\langle\phi,\psi\rangle|^2$, where both vectors are unit vectors and biseparability means a product across some nonempty proper bipartition; the mixed-state measure is its convex roof.</li>
<li>$\mathcal W=P/d-|GHZ_n^d\rangle\langle GHZ_n^d|$, where $P$ projects onto computational words using at most two distinct symbols. This is the orthogonal sum in lines 297–298, with the distinct arrangements specified by the orthogonal set $S$ at lines 690–692.</li>
<li>$w_{n,d}(p)=\operatorname{Tr}(\rho_{n,d}(p)\mathcal W)$, $\hat E_G(r\mathcal W)=\sup_{|\psi|=1,\ \phi\text{ unit biseparable}}{\langle\psi,(r\mathcal W+|\phi\rangle\langle\phi|)\psi\rangle-1}$ over unit vectors, and $\epsilon_o^{n,d}(p)=\sup_{r\in\mathbb R}{r w_{n,d}(p)-\hat E_G(r\mathcal W)}$.</li>
</ul>
<p>The source locators are also collected in <a href="../Library/Divergence/xuzhouzhaohu2023gme.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/25044">#25044</a> fixes the universal reading: for every pair of integers $n,d\ge3$ and every real $p\in[0,1]$, $\epsilon_o^{n,d}(p)=E_G(\rho_{n,d}(p))$. The formal convex roof takes the real infimum over all finite ensembles with nonnegative weights summing to one, unit pure vectors and exact reconstruction of the density matrix. This universal equality is refuted.</p>
