<p>This quotation is from the downloaded v1 source, <code>EffOfBayesianFB.tex</code>, lines 910–912, md5 <code>aeee6c3398ec2e49e99d0f461ed53290</code>; the spelling “Marokovian” is the source's. The <a href="../Library/HilbertOperators/rexitioskoueimancini2024bayesianfeedback.md">literature note</a> gives the feedback definitions and source locators.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/23263">#23263</a> specifies an answer to the first request using the qutrit Werner–Holevo channel
$\Phi(X)=\tfrac12(\operatorname{tr}(X)I_3-X^{\mathsf T})$.
For a finite family $K=(K_a)_{a\in\mathrm{Fin},m}$ of complex $3\times3$ matrices, <code>IsKrausDecomposition K</code> means
$\sum_a K_a X K_a^\dagger=\Phi(X)$ for every complex $3\times3$ matrix $X$.</p>
<p>The module specializes the source's two-step formulas in Section 2, lines 245–253, to dimension three:</p>
<p>$F_{\mathrm M}(K,L)=\tfrac19\sum_{a,b}\bigl(\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{tr}(|L_b|,|K_a|)\bigr)^2$,</p>
<p>$F_{\mathrm B}(K,L)=\tfrac19\sum_{a,b}|L_b|K_a||_1^2$,</p>
<p>where $|T|=\sqrt{T^\dagger T}$ and $|M|<em>1=\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{tr}\sqrt{M^\dagger M}$.
The settled statement is that every pair of finite Kraus decompositions has $F</em>{\mathrm M}\le\tfrac12$, while some pair of three-operator Kraus decompositions has $F_{\mathrm B}&gt;\tfrac12$.</p>
