en xx chain question resolved quantum information the temporal bell endpoint contraction identity for every open xx chain andrea tononi and maciej lewenstein, temporal bell inequalities in non-relativistic many-body physics, quantum science and technology 10 (2025), arxiv:2409.17290v4, methods, “derivation of eq. ichexact”, conjecture in arxiv.tex, lines 343–353 (md5 225051e786fe4712ac07f5226a0a99ac): the paper evaluates temporal clauser–horne probabilities for a bell pair at the endpoints of an open xx chain. the endpoint vacuum contractions of the open xx chain equal a difference of one-particle propagator entries. its vacuumindex n is the all-false occupation configuration, and fulloperator n is the complex matrix algebra on these configurations. pairing terms and interactions require different evolution formulas and remain open here. - the printed spectral sign. released-dossier cc66bba1eaa6bebf591529f069bdcd07b55e63df606ca6e90f7af4d7bb95b196 "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Quantum information</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Question resolved</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>First preprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2024</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>The temporal Bell endpoint contraction identity for every open XX chain</strong><span class="result-excerpt">The endpoint vacuum contractions of the open XX chain equal a difference of one-particle propagator entries.</span></span><span class="result-outcome proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Andrea Tononi and Maciej Lewenstein, Temporal Bell inequalities in non-relativistic many-body physics, Quantum Science and Technology 10 (2025), arXiv:2409.17290v4, Methods, “Derivation of Eq. ICHexact”, conjecture in arxiv.tex, lines 343–353 (md5 225051e786fe4712ac07f5226a0a9