<p>The quotation preserves the TeX wording and citation keys, with display delimiters and the equation label omitted. The source's references identify <code>sneg</code> as R. Žitko's SNEG package (2011) and <code>mullerrigat2025</code> as preliminary results of G. Müller-Rigat, M. Płodzień, D. Farina, M. Lewenstein and A. Tononi (2025).</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/21106">#21106</a> fixes the reading: for every integer $N\ge2$ and every real $J,\mu,t$, use the Jordan–Wigner annihilators $f_j$ on the full occupation space $(\mathbb C^2)^{\otimes N}$, its empty vacuum $|0\rangle$, and</p>
<p>$H=-J\sum_{j=1}^{N-1}(f_j^\dagger f_{j+1}+f_{j+1}^\dagger f_j)-\mu\sum_{j=1}^N f_j^\dagger f_j$,</p>
<p>$h_{jj}=-\mu$, $h_{j,j+1}=h_{j+1,j}=-J$, with all other entries zero, and $G(t)=e^{ith}$.</p>
<p>The observable is $\sigma_N^x=\big<a href="f_N%5E%5Cdagger+f_N">\prod_{j&lt;N}(1-2f_j^\dagger f_j)\big</a>$, with its prefix product in increasing site order, and $\sigma_N^x(t)=e^{itH}\sigma_N^xe^{-itH}$. With these definitions, the displayed real-part identity is proved.</p>
<p>The source introduces $G$ through the relation $f_j^\dagger(t)=\sum_iG_{ij}(t)f_i^\dagger$ (<code>arxiv.tex</code>, lines 153–154 and 291). The settlement follows this relation. Its matrix exponential is not identified with the source's printed spectral formula containing $(-1)^{j-1}$ in $u_{jk}$; the sign distinction is addressed below. The source quotations and bibliography are also in <a href="../Library/QuantumContext/tononilewenstein2025temporalbell.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
