<p>Section 1.2 defines <code>F(n)</code> to be the square of the product of the nonzero
decimal digits of <code>n</code>. A positive integer is a sequence member when some
finite iterate reaches one. With <code>F^[0](n) = n</code>, exact convergence length
three means <code>F^[3](n) = 1</code> and <code>F^[k](n) != 1</code> for every natural <code>k &lt; 3</code>.</p>
<p>The closed proposition <code>claim</code> is exactly:</p>
<pre><code class="language-text">∀ n : ℕ, 0 &lt; n → (∃ r : ℕ, n = r ^ 2) →
  SequenceMember n → ¬ FirstHit n 3
</code></pre>
<p><code>SequenceMember n</code> is <code>∃ t : ℕ, step^[t] n = 1</code>, and <code>FirstHit n t</code> is
<code>step^[t] n = 1 ∧ ∀ k : ℕ, k &lt; t → step^[k] n ≠ 1</code>. The square root is
