cle class="news-result" id="rubboli-takagi-tomamichel-2024-magic-additivity-refutation"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The boundary α-z Rényi relative entropies of magic are not additive on three qubits</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>R. Rubboli, R. Takagi and M. Tomamichel, <em>Mixed-state additivity properties of magic monotones based on quantum relative entropies for single-qubit states and beyond</em>, Quantum <strong>8</strong>, 1492 (2024), arXiv:2307.08258v4, define the α-z Rényi relative entropies of magic D_{α,z}(ρ) = inf over σ ∈ S̄_n of D_{α,z}(ρ‖σ) (Eq. (10)), where:</p>
<ul>
<li>S̄_n is the convex hull of the pure stabilizer states, the Clifford images of |0^n⟩ under the group generated by H, S and CNOT;</li>
