<p>They prove additivity for all single-qubit states on the boundary |(1 − α)/z| = 1 of the data-processing region. §5 states: &quot;It is still an open problem whether the α-z Rényi relative entropies of magic in the range |(1−α)/z| = 1 are additive for all two and three-qubit states&quot;. Table 1 and §10 conjecture that they are. The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/QuantumBounds/rubboli2024magicadditivity.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/15943">#15943</a> fixes the reading: for every (α, z) in the region D with |(1 − α)/z| = 1, every pair of states on two or three qubits each satisfies D_{α,z}(ρ₁ ⊗ ρ₂) = D_{α,z}(ρ₁) + D_{α,z}(ρ₂).</p>
