ed not exist counterexample found quantum information logical z operators with z support on every stabilizer coset need not exist liu, from magic state distillation to dynamical systems, quantum 9, 1858 (2025), arxiv:2412.04402, model magic state distillation by a stabilizer code as a map of the bloch ball. the fixed-plane property lets the authors reduce the three-dimensional distillation dynamics to a two-dimensional flow on the equator, the plane of magic states that can be injected directly. a five-qubit stabilizer code has a z-free word in every nontrivial logical coset. 1. witness. the five-qubit code with generators xzzxi, ixzzz, xixzy and zxixy.  released-dossier 847d0fb4a16a29f19dba830c28c263342da8759f5381c06a4f1058ce0eac28d7 "><summary><span class="result-impact-list"><span class="result-impact-field">Quantum information</span><span class="result-impact-tag">Counterexample found</span><span class="result-impact-history"><span>First preprint</span> <span class="result-impact-year">2024</span></span></span><span class="result-summary"><strong>Logical Z operators with Z support on every stabilizer coset need not exist</strong><span class="result-excerpt">A five-qubit stabilizer code has a Z-free word in every nontrivial logical coset.</span></span><span class="result-outcome refuted">Refuted</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Liu, From Magic State Distillation to Dynamical Systems, Quantum 9, 1858 (2025), arXiv:2412.04402, model magic state distillation by a stabilizer code as a map of the Bloch ball.</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The fixed-plane property lets the authors reduce the three-dimensional distillation dynamics to a two-dimensional flow on the equator, the plane of magic states that can be injected directly.</p><p><span>The idea</span>1. Witness. The five-qubit code with generators XZZXI, IXZZZ, XIXZY and ZXIXY.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>A five-qubit stabilizer code has a Z-free word in every nontrivial logical coset.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="zheng-liu-2024-logical-z-support-refutation"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Logical Z operators with Z support on every stabilizer coset need not exist</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Y. Zheng and D. E. Liu, <em>From Magic State Distillation to Dynamical Systems</em>, Quantum 9, 1858 (2025), arXiv:2412.04402, model magic state distillation by a stabilizer code as a map of the Bloch ball.</p>
<p>Proposition 3 gives a sufficient condition for z = 0 to be a fixed plane of the map: for every logical operator Z̄_i and every stabilizer element s_j, the product s_j Z̄_i contains a Pauli Z tensor factor. The authors write after Eq. (23): &quot;This condition is satisfied by most known protocols that we have examined and we conjecture it to be generally true for any stabilizer codes by properly choosing the logical Z operators without modifying the stabilizer groups.&quot;</p>
<p>The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/QuantumChannels/zhengliu2024magicdistillationdynamics.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/17951">#17951</a> fixes the reading. For every stabilizer code with at least one logical qubit, some nontrivial logical Pauli word L has a literal Z factor in every product s·L with s in the stabilizer group. This conjecture is refuted.</p>
