rnal implementation.</p><p><span>The idea</span>All parameters in the following lemmas are real.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Qubit channels give a strict deterministic-input violation of the separable energy bound for every positive energy budget below one half.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>The exact minimum over this family or all allowed devices remains open here.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="davino-et-al-2025-energy-constrained-deterministic-violation"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Deterministic-input violations exist at every positive energy budget below one half</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>R. D'Avino, G. Senno, M. Alimuddin and A. Acín, <em>Entanglement in the energy-constrained prepare-and-measure scenario: applications to randomness certification and channel discrimination</em>, arXiv:2510.27559v3 (2025 preprint; v3, 2026), Section IV.A, state:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We conjecture that this holds for all $\omega &gt; 0$.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is verbatim from <code>paper_Quantum.tex</code>, line 284 (MD5 <code>012a72f4d8cfd30e14dc3813eda8f546</code>). The preceding sentence's assertion is the existence of behaviors allowing entanglement that are deterministic for input $x=0$ but violate the separable deterministic-input inequality. The global restriction is $\omega\in[0,1/2)$ (line 154), so the conjecture concerns every $0&lt;\omega&lt;1/2$.</p>
<p>The paper considers a shared state $\sigma_{PM}$, local channels $\Lambda_x:P\to S$ for $x\in{0,1}$, and a binary POVM ${\Pi^0,\Pi^1}$ on $S\otimes M$. Its behavior formula is $p(b|x)=\operatorname{Tr}[\Pi^b(\Lambda_x\otimes\mathrm{id}<em>M)(\sigma</em>{PM})]$ (lines 137–148), and $E_x=p(0|x)-p(1|x)$ (lines 165–166). For separable devices with $p(0|0)=1$, its displayed inequality is:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>$E_1\geq 2(1-2\omega)^2-1=:I_\mathrm{det}^{\omega,\mathrm{sep}}$</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is line 268, equation labelled <code>eq:deterministic-ineq-for-fixed-input-0</code>. The source defines $\mathcal Q_\omega^{\mathrm{ent}}$ by allowing entanglement, rather than by requiring an additional entanglement test (line 158).</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/22022">#22022</a> fixes the following finite-dimensional reading, which is proved. For every real $0&lt;\omega&lt;1/2$, there exist natural dimensions $d_p,d_s,d_m$, a complex matrix $\sigma$ on $P\otimes M$, two complex-linear matrix maps $\Lambda_x:P\to S$, a matrix $H$ and vector $g$ on $S$, and two effects $\Pi^b$ on $S\otimes M$, such that:</p>
<ul>
<li>$\sigma\succeq0$ and $\operatorname{Tr}\sigma=1$;</li>
<li>each $\Lambda_x$ is completely positive and preserves the trace of every complex matrix;</li>
<li>$H=H^\dagger$, $g^\dagger g=1$, $Hg=0$, and $H-(I-|g\rangle\langle g|)\succeq0$;</li>
<li>$\Pi^b\succeq0$ for both outcomes and $\Pi^0+\Pi^1=I$;</li>
<li>$\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{Tr}[H\Lambda_x(\operatorname{Tr}_M\sigma)]\leq\omega$ for both inputs;</li>
<li>$p(0|0)=1$ and $p(0|1)-p(1|1)&lt;2(1-2\omega)^2-1$.</li>
</ul>
<p>Here the Lean definition <code>probability</code> takes the real part of the Born trace displayed above. The claim has no separate separability or entanglement predicate. The source permits arbitrary, including infinite, dimensions; finite witnesses are sufficient for its existential question. See also <a href="../Library/Entropy/davinoetal2025energyconstrained.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
