<p>We conjecture that up to unitary equivalence $A$ is the only noncommutative reversible $4 \times 4$ matrix algebra.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The preregistered formal reading takes a complex submodule $b$ of $M_4(\mathbb C)$ to be a matrix algebra when it is closed under multiplication, noncommutative when it contains a noncommuting pair, and reversible when some $m&gt;0$ and complex-linear map $\rho:M_4(\mathbb C)\to M_m(\mathbb C)$ reverse multiplication on $b$ and preserve every block operator norm. <code>UnitarilyEquivalent b carAlgebra</code> means that some $q\in\operatorname{Matrix.unitaryGroup}(\operatorname{Fin} 4,\mathbb C)$ satisfies $x\in b$ exactly when $q^*xq\in carAlgebra$ for every $x$. Thus <code>claim</code> is the universal statement that every such $b$ is unitarily equivalent to the CAR submodule <code>carAlgebra</code>.</p>
