<p>The NAME is <code>a(n) = A235224(A003415(n)) - A400164(n)</code>, with offset one.
Let $P_k$ be the product of the first $k$ primes and $P_0=1$.
Set $L(0)=0$ and, for $m&gt;0$, let $L(m)$ be the largest $k\ge1$ with
$P_{k-1}\le m$, equivalently the least $k\ge0$ with $m&lt;P_k$.
Set $D(0)=D(1)=0$ and
$D(n)=\sum_{p\mid n}v_p(n)(n/p)$. Let $M(1)=0$ and, for $n\ge2$,
$M(n)=\max_{p^e\mid n,\ p\text{ prime},\ e\ge1} L(n/p^e)$.
