<blockquote>
<p>As noted in Remark 2.7, the sequence grows exponentially fast (faster than the Fibonacci sequence). Is there a construction involving a strictly increasing sequence that grows slower than the Fibonacci sequence, or perhaps even like n^k for some k?</p>
