<p>The TeX label <code>ax:T4</code> denotes monotonicity under every completely positive trace-preserving channel covariant under the spin representation of $\mathrm{SU}(2)$ (Definition 2, lines 180–200). Identify a spin-$j$ state $\rho$ with a symmetric state $\rho_S$ of $N=2j$ qubits and put $\rho_t=\operatorname{Tr}<em>{N-t}(\rho_S)$. In the normalized Dicke basis the reference state is $\rho_0^{(t)}=I</em>{t+1}/(t+1)$. The source's candidate (lines 333–358) is</p>
<p>$\mathcal A_t^{T,d_1}(\rho)=1-|\rho_t-\rho_0^{(t)}|<em>1/K_t$, with $K_t=\max</em>{\sigma\in\mathcal D(\mathcal H_{t/2})}|\sigma-\rho_0^{(t)}|_1$.</p>
<p>The source uses the full Schatten one-norm. Its mixed-state domain includes every $t\in{1,\ldots,N}$; the footnote at line 178 says:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Whenever we consider pure states, we usually assume $t\le N/2$.</p>
</blockquote>
