quared overlaps above, and overlapattained supplies unit local factors attaining gMax.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>The symmetric localized coin maximizes full-mode geometric entanglement at every time on every finite circle.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>Its conjecture in lines 645–649 about the asymptotic local-maximum great circle on the infinite line remains open here: result supplies neither an infinite-line limit nor a characterization of a contour of local maxima.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="donkersloot-sondenheimer-sperling-2026-symmetric-coin-entanglement"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>The symmetric coin maximizes full-mode entanglement of the Hadamard walk on every finite circle</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>E. K. F. Donkersloot, R. Sondenheimer and J. Sperling, <em>Multipartite entanglement dynamics in quantum walks</em> (2026), arXiv:2603.24679v1, Section III C 2, “Arbitrary localized initial conditions”, state in <code>arxiv-v1.tex</code>, lines 653–654:</p>
