me proved">Proved</span><span class="result-disclosure" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="reading-item-body"><div class="result-story-expanded"><p><span>The question</span>Dirichlet g.f.: Sum{n&gt;0} a(n)/n^s = (zeta(s)zeta(6s))/(zeta(2s)zeta(3s)).</p><p><span>Why it matters</span>The independent question is Schulte&#x27;s published product conjecture, relating three coefficient sequences for every positive natural index.</p><p><span>The idea</span>Use coprime power extraction and the exact-power guard to transfer multiplicativity to the power lifts.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>Schulte&#x27;s A299406 coefficients equal the Liouville function times A210826.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="oeis-a299406-schulte-liouville-cube-mobius"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status proved">Proved in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Integer sequences (OEIS)</p><h3>Schulte&#x27;s Liouville and cube-Möbius product formula</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>OEIS A299406, NAME (<code>%N</code>, verbatim):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dirichlet g.f.: Sum_{n&gt;0} a(n)/n^s = (zeta(s)*zeta(6*s))/(zeta(2*s)*zeta(3*s)).</p>
