e into the Bell state ϕ+.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Universality.</strong> Definition 1: an n-to-1 LOCC map E1 is a universal conclusive protocol if ⟨ϕ+|E1(ρ⊗n)|ϕ+⟩ = Tr E1(ρ⊗n) for every input in the set, here every pure state |ψ⟩ = c1|00⟩ + c2|01⟩ + c3|10⟩ + c4|11⟩ (Eq. (1)).</li>
<li><strong>The bound.</strong> Theorem 3 bounds the four-copy success probability of concatenated protocols based on two-qubit operations by B(c) = 2|c2⁴c3⁴| + 2|c1⁴c4⁴| − 4Re[c1²c4²(c2*)²(c3*)²] (Eq. (8)).</li>
<li><strong>The conjecture.</strong> §VIII: &quot;protocols that process four copies directly without intermediate Schmidt-state conversion warrant investigation. We conjecture that such protocols cannot surpass the success probability bound in Eq. (8)&quot;.</li>
</ul>
<p>The verbatim statements are in <a href="../Library/QuantumBounds/ortheyphilipkondrastreltsov2026optimality.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
