<p>This quotation is from the downloaded v2 source <code>mn_revision_clean.tex</code>, line 1749, MD5 <code>08daa608d307e41e61bcd9c0d9f06c31</code>. The generalized mirroring relation is $W+M=K$ in lines 1688–1692; the witness definition, detection sets, optimality and spanning criterion are in lines 276–281, 388–396 and 485–490. See <a href="../Library/QuantumContext/seongberahiesmayrchruscinskibae2026mirrored.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/20970">#20970</a> fixes a nontrivial reading: for every natural number $d\ge3$, there are optimal witnesses $W,M$ on $\mathbb C^d\otimes\mathbb C^d$ such that $W+M$ is optimal, each detects a density matrix the other does not, and some density matrix is detected by both. This is proved.</p>
<p>Here a density matrix is positive semidefinite with trace one; a witness is Hermitian, block-positive on every product vector, and has negative real trace pairing with some density matrix. Optimality means that for every real $\epsilon&gt;0$ and every nonzero positive semidefinite $P$, the operator $A-\epsilon P$ is not block-positive. Write $D_A={\rho:\rho\text{ is a density matrix},\ \operatorname{Re}\operatorname{tr}(A\rho)&lt;0}$.</p>
