<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/17440">#17440</a> fixes the reading of the non-FS case: for every density matrix ρ on C^N ⊗ C^M and every integer 1 ≤ χ ≤ min(N, M), does N(ρ) = (χ − 1)/2 imply <a href="%CF%81">1 ⊗ RED_χ</a> = ρ_A ⊗ 1 − ρ/χ ≥ 0? The attained value is the stronger hypothesis, so a counterexample also refutes the sublevel reading N(ρ) ≤ (χ − 1)/2.</p>
<p>The non-FS inclusion is refuted.</p>
