<p>Equation <code>state_regularized</code> defines</p>
<p>$$A_\varepsilon=(1-\varepsilon)A+\frac{\varepsilon}{d}I,
\qquad 0&lt;\varepsilon&lt;1.$$</p>
<p>Equation <code>regularized_Cu-Q</code> and the definition of relative quantumness give</p>
<p>$$Q(A\Vert B)=-S_0^Q(A\Vert B)
=\ln\operatorname{Tr}\left[A\exp(\ln B-\ln A)\right].$$</p>
<p>Density means positive semidefinite with trace one. CPTP means complete
positivity at every finite amplification and trace preservation on every
matrix. CoP quantifies over every pair of commuting density matrices.
