<p>Here $d=2^n$, $\bar I$ averages the Fisher information over all $3^n$ product Pauli settings, and $\lambda_{min}=\lambda_{min}(G^{-1/2}\bar I G^{-1/2})$, where $G$ is the Frobenius metric of the local rank-$r$ parametrisation. The measurement model, metric and Fisher matrix are in the same source, lines 114–121, 157–176 and 178–180; see also <a href="../Library/Estimation/acharyakypraiosguta2016lowranktomography.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/24270">#24270</a> fixes the tangent reading. For complex matrices on $n$ qubits, let $u_{s,o}$ be the product Pauli eigenvector, $p_\rho(o\mid s)=\operatorname{Re}\langle u_{s,o}|\rho|u_{s,o}\rangle$, and $\bar I_\rho(v)=3^{-n}\sum_s\sum_o(\operatorname{Re}\langle u_{s,o}|v|u_{s,o}\rangle)^2/p_\rho(o\mid s)$, with zero-probability terms assigned zero.</p>
<p><code>IsRankTangent r ρ v</code> means that there exists a curve $\gamma:\mathbb R\to M_{2^n}(\mathbb C)$ with $\gamma(0)=\rho$, derivative $v$ at zero, and $\gamma(t)$ a positive semidefinite trace-one matrix of rank $r$ for every real $t$. Differentiability is required only at zero.</p>
<p><code>claim</code> asserts that for every natural rank $r\ge1$ there exists a real $c&gt;0$ such that, for every $n\in\mathbb N$, every rank-$r$ density matrix $\rho$ and every <code>IsRankTangent r ρ v</code>, one has $c\operatorname{Re}\operatorname{Tr}(v^2)\le\bar I_\rho(v)$. The quantifier over $n$ includes zero. The module proves <code>result : ¬ claim</code>; its witnesses have rank one and $n&gt;0$.</p>
