<p>a(n) is the smallest number k &gt; n such that n^k == n (mod k). Conjecture: a(n) is the smallest number k &gt; n such that n^(k-1) == 1 (mod k). Thus a(n) is coprime to n. - <em>Thomas Ordowski</em>, Aug 03 2018</p>
