ence polygamy.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>The numerical observations in Appendix D cannot justify a universal dimension threshold; a characterization of the mixed states satisfying the unmodified inequality remains open here.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="yu-2017-skew-coherence-mixed-state-polygamy"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Yu&#x27;s mixed-state skew-coherence polygamy conjecture is false</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Chang-shui Yu, <em>Quantum coherence via skew information and its polygamy</em>, Phys. Rev. A 95, 042337 (2017), arXiv:1704.04871v1, Discussion and Conclusions, <code>coherenceLy.tex</code>, lines 997–999:</p>
