<p>The source's <code>\ketbra</code> macro is expanded in the displayed quotation. The source archive member <code>article.tex</code> has MD5 <code>614f0961ea15b65fb0b83ac83bd3fffb</code>.</p>
<p>Here channels are completely positive, trace-preserving complex linear maps. Two POVMs are compatible when a positive normalized family indexed by both outcome sets has them as its marginals. Two channels are compatible when a single channel to the tensor product of their outputs has them as its partial-trace marginals on every input matrix. These definitions are in the source at lines 124–146 and 179–199 and in <a href="../Library/QuantumContext/zhangnechita2022fisherchannelincompatibility.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/21608">#21608</a> fixes the reading: for every positive dimension and every pair of channels on that space, compatibility of the two induced POVMs for every pair of orthonormal bases implies channel compatibility. This is refuted by two copies of the qubit depolarizing channel $\Phi_{7/10}$.</p>
