<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/21843">#21843</a> fixes the reading: for every natural size $d$, four positive semidefinite complex $d\times d$ matrices with $A_0$ and $B_0$ having equal characteristic polynomials, and likewise $A_1$ and $B_1$, satisfy the norm comparison for every real $p\ge1$ whenever every ordered-word trace of the $A$ pair is real and dominates the absolute value of the corresponding $B$ trace. The universal implication is refuted.</p>
