ance.</p><p><span>The idea</span>All vectors and constants in the construction are fixed, except where a lemma&#x27;s real parameter and hypotheses are stated explicitly.</p><p><span>Our contribution</span>A positive three-state cyclic chain violates the proposed two-state lower bound on non-adiabatic entropy production.</p><p><span>Scope &amp; next question</span>Whether detailed balance suffices for Eq. (13), or which additional compatibility condition on the binary dynamics suffices for general multistate processes, remains open here.</p></div><details class="verification-details"><summary>Verification details</summary><article class="news-result" id="gu-2023-pseudo-coarse-grained-tradeoff"><div class="news-result-meta"><span>Release source record</span><span class="news-status refuted">Refuted in Lean</span></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Open problem</p><h3>Gu&#x27;s pseudo-coarse-grained dissipation-time trade-off is false</h3><div class="result-statement prose"><p>Jie Gu, <em>Speed limit, dissipation bound and dissipation-time trade-off in thermal relaxation processes</em>, Phys. Rev. E 108, L052103 (2023), DOI 10.1103/PhysRevE.108.L052103, arXiv:2304.08752v2, states the following conjecture in the section “Trade-off between dissipation and time,” Eq. (13). The verbatim sentence and equation are from <code>relaxation.tex</code>, lines 328 and 331 (the equation's mathematical content is rendered inline):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Let us state  the third main result: for $N$-state dynamics evolving from $\boldsymbol{p}^\text{(i)}$ to $\boldsymbol{p}^\text{(f)}$ during $\tau$ with an total rate $\mathcal{W}$, the conjecture is that the entropy production $\Sigma$ is bounded from below by (referred to as trade-off bound)</p>
<p>$\Sigma_\text{na} \ge \Sigma_{\Omega_i}(\mathcal W \tau) \quad i =1,2,\ldots,S_N^{(2)}.$</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The displayed inequality concerns non-adiabatic entropy production, despite the sentence's use of $\Sigma$. Lines 333–337 define each binary comparison by a partition into two nonempty sets, the aggregate endpoints, and the original process's total rate and elapsed time. The source conventions and the two-state steady-state formula are also recorded in <a href="../Library/StatisticalMechanics/gu2023dissipationtimetradeoff.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/21842">#21842</a> fixes the following restricted reading, encoded by <code>claim</code>. For every natural number $n$, rate array $a:\mathrm{Fin},n\to\mathrm{Fin},n\to\mathbb R$, vector $u$, real curve $P:\mathbb R\to\mathbb R^n$, real time $\tau$, and finite subset $\Omega$ of the states, put</p>
<p>$W_{ij}=a_{ij}$ for $i\ne j$, and $W_{jj}=-\sum_{i\ne j}a_{ij}$.</p>
<p>Assume all of the following:</p>
<ul>
<li>$a_{ij}&gt;0$ whenever $i\ne j$;</li>
<li>$u_i&gt;0$ for every state, $\sum_i u_i=1$, and $Wu=0$;</li>
<li>$P$ has derivative $WP(t)$ at every real $t$;</li>
<li>$\tau&gt;0$, every coordinate of $P(0)$ is positive, $\sum_iP_i(0)=1$, and every coordinate of $P(\tau)$ is positive;</li>
<li>$\Omega$ and its complement are both nonempty.</li>
</ul>
<p>Define $D(v|w)=\sum_i v_i\log(v_i/w_i)$, $d(z|b)=D((z,1-z)|(b,1-b))$, and</p>
<p>$x=\sum_{i\in\Omega}P_i(0)$, $y=\sum_{i\in\Omega}P_i(\tau)$, $k=-\operatorname{Tr}W$, $s=x+(y-x)/(1-e^{-k\tau})$.</p>
<p>Whenever $0&lt;s&lt;1$, the proposed inequality is</p>
<p>$d(x|s)-d(y|s)\le D(P(0)|u)-D(P(\tau)|u)$.</p>
<p>The module proves <code>result : ¬ claim</code>. Thus even this restriction to positive off-diagonal rates, positive endpoints and an interior fitted binary steady state is false.</p>
