<p>The optimization in that subsection is the ordinary overlap modulus over product vectors with every local factor normalized (l. 1234–1243). Write $|0\rangle=|\downarrow\rangle$ and $|1\rangle=|\uparrow\rangle$. For $q&gt;0$, the three-qubit vectors at l. 581–582 are</p>
<p>$|D^1_3\rangle_q=(\sqrt q,|001\rangle+|010\rangle+q^{-1/2}|100\rangle)/\sqrt{q+1+q^{-1}}$,</p>
<p>$|D^2_3\rangle_q=(\sqrt q,|011\rangle+|101\rangle+q^{-1/2}|110\rangle)/\sqrt{q+1+q^{-1}}$.</p>
<p>Here $[3]_q=q+1+q^{-1}$ follows from the source's q-number at l. 469, with its undeformed convention at $q=1$. The source identifies $\mathrm{Sym}_q\mathcal H$ with the complex span of $|000\rangle$, $|D^1_3\rangle_q$, $|D^2_3\rangle_q$ and $|111\rangle$ (l. 586). These definitions are recorded in <a href="../Library/LieTheory/ballesterosetal2025qsymmetric.md">the literature note</a>.</p>
<p>Issue <a href="https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/issues/21970">#21970</a> fixes the reading: for every real $q&gt;0$, there exist unit $a,b,c\in\mathbb C^2$ such that $a\otimes b\otimes c$ maximizes $|\langle D^1_3|_q(a\otimes b\otimes c)\rangle|$ over all unit local factors and belongs to $\mathrm{Sym}_q\mathcal H$. This three-qubit, one-excitation instance of the conjecture is refuted.</p>
