| Exponential similarity | <code>similarity</code> | Scale-one exponential of negative distance. |
| Zero extension of the inverse solve | <code>weighting</code> | Literal principal <code>Matrix.submatrix</code> inverse times the constant-one vector. |
| Start with every point and retain strictly positive weights | <code>active</code> | Both recursion cases are explicit. |
| First nonnegative solve | <code>stopped</code>, <code>FirstStop</code> | No earlier stop; all visited supports nonempty and all visited principal determinants nonzero. |
| Return the normalized weighting | <code>mass</code>, <code>output</code> | <code>claim</code> requires positive normalization. |
| Minimum similarity energy over every original-space probability | <code>DiversityMaximizing</code> | Feasibility in <code>Convexity.StdSimplex</code> and the full double-sum comparison. |
