<p>Let $V=\operatorname{AGL}(1,29)=(\mathbb Z/29\mathbb Z)^\times\times\mathbb Z/29\mathbb Z$, with $(x,y)(z,w)=(xz,xw+y)$. For each $a\in{3,8,10,11}$, put $t=(-1,0)$, $g=(a,1)$ and $r=g^{-1}$. Let $B_a$ be the simple undirected Cayley graph joining $x$ to $xt,xg,xr$.</p>
